[{"id":"a363","title":"網路入侵偵測工程","titleEn":"Network intrusion-detection engineering","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以網路可觀察性、協議解碼與告警品質串連 16 個領域技術單元、32 個保存步驟；分析架構、原理、介面、故障、量化案例與防禦證據。","summaryEn":"Sixteen domain-specific technical units and 32 saved steps connect network visibility, protocol decoding and alert quality through architecture, principles, interfaces, faults, quantitative cases and defensive evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":11,"depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a363-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求、元件與基本模型","titleEn":"Requirements, components and baseline models","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a363-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"觀察點：架構與原理","titleEn":"Observation points: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「觀察點」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For observation points, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「觀察點」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「鏡像完整性」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around observation points, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix events and vary mirror placement. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat mirror completeness as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「觀察點」與「鏡像完整性」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for observation points and mirror completeness supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「觀察點」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for observation points. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-01-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。","textEn":"Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-01-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「鏡像完整性」：鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「觀察點」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring mirror completeness: Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove observation points passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-01-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-01-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 流中 200 異常；偵測 160、正常誤報 100，precision=160/260=61.54%、recall=80%。資料分布改變時這些比率亦改變。","textEn":"Among 100000 hypothetical flows with 200 anomalies, 160 detections and 100 false positives give precision=61.54% and recall=80%; distribution shifts change these values.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「觀察點」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of observation points?","options":["觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。","IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「鏡像完整性」，便可取代「觀察點」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic.","An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking mirror completeness alone replaces verification specific to observation points."],"answer":0,"explanation":"觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。 相鄰的「鏡像完整性」有不同責任：鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Neighboring mirror completeness has a different role: Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-01"],"title":"觀察點：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Observation points: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「觀察點」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For observation points, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「鏡像完整性」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix events and vary mirror placement. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from mirror completeness to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「觀察點」與「鏡像完整性」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for observation points and mirror completeness supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「觀察點」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for observation points. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-02-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。","textEn":"Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-02-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「鏡像完整性」：鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「觀察點」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring mirror completeness: Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove observation points passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-02-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-02-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 流中 200 異常；偵測 160、正常誤報 100，precision=160/260=61.54%、recall=80%。資料分布改變時這些比率亦改變。","textEn":"Among 100000 hypothetical flows with 200 anomalies, 160 detections and 100 false positives give precision=61.54% and recall=80%; distribution shifts change these values.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「觀察點」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of observation points?","options":["觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。","IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「鏡像完整性」，便可取代「觀察點」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic.","An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking mirror completeness alone replaces verification specific to observation points."],"answer":0,"explanation":"觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。 相鄰的「鏡像完整性」有不同責任：鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Neighboring mirror completeness has a different role: Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-02"],"title":"鏡像完整性：架構與原理","titleEn":"Mirror completeness: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「鏡像完整性」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For mirror completeness, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「鏡像完整性」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「流識別」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around mirror completeness, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix events and vary mirror placement. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat flow identification as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「鏡像完整性」與「流識別」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for mirror completeness and flow identification supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「鏡像完整性」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for mirror completeness. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-03-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。","textEn":"Mirror ports can overload and drop packets.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-03-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「流識別」：五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「鏡像完整性」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring flow identification: Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove mirror completeness passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-03-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「鏡像完整性」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of mirror completeness?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。","只檢查「流識別」，便可取代「鏡像完整性」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Mirror ports can overload and drop packets.","Checking flow identification alone replaces verification specific to mirror completeness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。 相鄰的「流識別」有不同責任：五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Neighboring flow identification has a different role: Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-03"],"title":"鏡像完整性：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Mirror completeness: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「鏡像完整性」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For mirror completeness, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「流識別」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix events and vary mirror placement. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from flow identification to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「鏡像完整性」與「流識別」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for mirror completeness and flow identification supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「鏡像完整性」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for mirror completeness. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-04-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。","textEn":"Mirror ports can overload and drop packets.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-04-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「流識別」：五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「鏡像完整性」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring flow identification: Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove mirror completeness passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-04-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「鏡像完整性」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of mirror completeness?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。","只檢查「流識別」，便可取代「鏡像完整性」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Mirror ports can overload and drop packets.","Checking flow identification alone replaces verification specific to mirror completeness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鏡像埠可能超載並丟包。 相鄰的「流識別」有不同責任：五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Mirror ports can overload and drop packets. Neighboring flow identification has a different role: Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-04"],"title":"流識別：架構與原理","titleEn":"Flow identification: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「流識別」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For flow identification, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「流識別」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「重組假設」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around flow identification, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix events and vary mirror placement. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat reassembly assumptions as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「流識別」與「重組假設」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for flow identification and reassembly assumptions supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「流識別」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for flow identification. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-05-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。","textEn":"Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-05-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「重組假設」：亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「流識別」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring reassembly assumptions: Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove flow identification passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-05-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「流識別」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of flow identification?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「重組假設」，便可取代「流識別」的專屬驗證。","五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking reassembly assumptions alone replaces verification specific to flow identification.","Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows."],"answer":2,"explanation":"五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。 相鄰的「重組假設」有不同責任：亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Neighboring reassembly assumptions has a different role: Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-05"],"title":"流識別：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Flow identification: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「流識別」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For flow identification, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「重組假設」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix events and vary mirror placement. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from reassembly assumptions to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「流識別」與「重組假設」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for flow identification and reassembly assumptions supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「流識別」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for flow identification. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-06-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。","textEn":"Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-06-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「重組假設」：亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「流識別」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring reassembly assumptions: Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove flow identification passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-06-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「流識別」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of flow identification?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「重組假設」，便可取代「流識別」的專屬驗證。","五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking reassembly assumptions alone replaces verification specific to flow identification.","Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows."],"answer":2,"explanation":"五元組與時間範圍一起界定流。 相鄰的「重組假設」有不同責任：亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Five-tuples and time ranges jointly identify flows. Neighboring reassembly assumptions has a different role: Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-06"],"title":"重組假設：架構與原理","titleEn":"Reassembly assumptions: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「重組假設」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For reassembly assumptions, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「重組假設」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「協議解碼」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around reassembly assumptions, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix events and vary mirror placement. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat protocol decoding as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「重組假設」與「協議解碼」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for reassembly assumptions and protocol decoding supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「重組假設」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for reassembly assumptions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-07-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。","textEn":"Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-07-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「協議解碼」：協議辨識不能只依埠號。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「重組假設」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring protocol decoding: Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove reassembly assumptions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-07-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「重組假設」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of reassembly assumptions?","options":["亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。","封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「協議解碼」，便可取代「重組假設」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content.","Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking protocol decoding alone replaces verification specific to reassembly assumptions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。 相鄰的「協議解碼」有不同責任：協議辨識不能只依埠號。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Neighboring protocol decoding has a different role: Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-07"],"title":"重組假設：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Reassembly assumptions: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「重組假設」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For reassembly assumptions, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「協議解碼」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix events and vary mirror placement. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from protocol decoding to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 比較「重組假設」與「協議解碼」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Compare whether evidence for reassembly assumptions and protocol decoding supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「重組假設」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for reassembly assumptions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-08-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。","textEn":"Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-08-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「協議解碼」：協議辨識不能只依埠號。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「重組假設」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring protocol decoding: Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove reassembly assumptions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-08-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定事件，只改鏡像點位置。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix events and vary mirror placement. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「重組假設」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of reassembly assumptions?","options":["亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。","封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「協議解碼」，便可取代「重組假設」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content.","Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking protocol decoding alone replaces verification specific to reassembly assumptions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"亂序及缺包會限制可解析內容。 相鄰的「協議解碼」有不同責任：協議辨識不能只依埠號。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Reordering and missing packets limit parsable content. Neighboring protocol decoding has a different role: Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a363-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"介面、狀態與資源配置","titleEn":"Interfaces, states and resource allocation","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a363-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-08"],"title":"協議解碼：架構與原理","titleEn":"Protocol decoding: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「協議解碼」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For protocol decoding, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「協議解碼」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：協議辨識不能只依埠號。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「加密邊界」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around protocol decoding, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat encryption boundaries as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「協議解碼」與「加密邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for protocol decoding and encryption boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「協議解碼」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for protocol decoding. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-09-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"協議辨識不能只依埠號。","textEn":"Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-09-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「加密邊界」：加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「協議解碼」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring encryption boundaries: Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove protocol decoding passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-09-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「協議解碼」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of protocol decoding?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","協議辨識不能只依埠號。","只檢查「加密邊界」，便可取代「協議解碼」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers.","Checking encryption boundaries alone replaces verification specific to protocol decoding."],"answer":1,"explanation":"協議辨識不能只依埠號。 相鄰的「加密邊界」有不同責任：加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Neighboring encryption boundaries has a different role: Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-09"],"title":"協議解碼：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Protocol decoding: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「協議解碼」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For protocol decoding, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「協議辨識不能只依埠號。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「加密邊界」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from encryption boundaries to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「協議解碼」與「加密邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for protocol decoding and encryption boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「協議解碼」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for protocol decoding. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-10-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"協議辨識不能只依埠號。","textEn":"Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-10-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「加密邊界」：加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「協議解碼」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring encryption boundaries: Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove protocol decoding passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-10-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「協議解碼」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of protocol decoding?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","協議辨識不能只依埠號。","只檢查「加密邊界」，便可取代「協議解碼」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers.","Checking encryption boundaries alone replaces verification specific to protocol decoding."],"answer":1,"explanation":"協議辨識不能只依埠號。 相鄰的「加密邊界」有不同責任：加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protocol identification cannot rely solely on port numbers. Neighboring encryption boundaries has a different role: Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-10"],"title":"加密邊界：架構與原理","titleEn":"Encryption boundaries: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「加密邊界」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For encryption boundaries, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「加密邊界」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「規則條件」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around encryption boundaries, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat rule conditions as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「加密邊界」與「規則條件」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for encryption boundaries and rule conditions supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「加密邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for encryption boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-11-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。","textEn":"Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-11-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「規則條件」：規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「加密邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring rule conditions: Rules must match fields actually collected. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove encryption boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-11-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「加密邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of encryption boundaries?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「規則條件」，便可取代「加密邊界」的專屬驗證。","加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking rule conditions alone replaces verification specific to encryption boundaries.","Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded."],"answer":2,"explanation":"加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。 相鄰的「規則條件」有不同責任：規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Neighboring rule conditions has a different role: Rules must match fields actually collected. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-11"],"title":"加密邊界：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Encryption boundaries: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「加密邊界」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For encryption boundaries, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「規則條件」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from rule conditions to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「加密邊界」與「規則條件」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for encryption boundaries and rule conditions supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「加密邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for encryption boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-12-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。","textEn":"Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-12-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「規則條件」：規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「加密邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring rule conditions: Rules must match fields actually collected. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove encryption boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-12-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「加密邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of encryption boundaries?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「規則條件」，便可取代「加密邊界」的專屬驗證。","加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking rule conditions alone replaces verification specific to encryption boundaries.","Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded."],"answer":2,"explanation":"加密限制內文觀察，metadata 證據仍有範圍。 相鄰的「規則條件」有不同責任：規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Encryption limits payload visibility; metadata evidence remains bounded. Neighboring rule conditions has a different role: Rules must match fields actually collected. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-12"],"title":"規則條件：架構與原理","titleEn":"Rule conditions: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「規則條件」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For rule conditions, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「規則條件」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「基線模型」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around rule conditions, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Rules must match fields actually collected. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat baseline models as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「規則條件」與「基線模型」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for rule conditions and baseline models supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「規則條件」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for rule conditions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-13-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。","textEn":"Rules must match fields actually collected.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-13-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「基線模型」：正常變異應由代表性資料估計。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「規則條件」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring baseline models: Estimate benign variability from representative data. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove rule conditions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-13-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「規則條件」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of rule conditions?","options":["規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。","IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「基線模型」，便可取代「規則條件」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Rules must match fields actually collected.","An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking baseline models alone replaces verification specific to rule conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。 相鄰的「基線模型」有不同責任：正常變異應由代表性資料估計。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Rules must match fields actually collected. Neighboring baseline models has a different role: Estimate benign variability from representative data. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-13"],"title":"規則條件：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Rule conditions: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「規則條件」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For rule conditions, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「基線模型」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Rules must match fields actually collected. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from baseline models to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「規則條件」與「基線模型」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for rule conditions and baseline models supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「規則條件」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for rule conditions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-14-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。","textEn":"Rules must match fields actually collected.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-14-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「基線模型」：正常變異應由代表性資料估計。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「規則條件」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring baseline models: Estimate benign variability from representative data. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove rule conditions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-14-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「規則條件」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of rule conditions?","options":["規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。","IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「基線模型」，便可取代「規則條件」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Rules must match fields actually collected.","An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking baseline models alone replaces verification specific to rule conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"規則需匹配實際可收集欄位。 相鄰的「基線模型」有不同責任：正常變異應由代表性資料估計。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Rules must match fields actually collected. Neighboring baseline models has a different role: Estimate benign variability from representative data. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-14"],"title":"基線模型：架構與原理","titleEn":"Baseline models: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「基線模型」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For baseline models, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「基線模型」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：正常變異應由代表性資料估計。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「異常與事故」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around baseline models, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Estimate benign variability from representative data. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat anomaly versus incident as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「基線模型」與「異常與事故」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for baseline models and anomaly versus incident supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「基線模型」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for baseline models. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-15-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"正常變異應由代表性資料估計。","textEn":"Estimate benign variability from representative data.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-15-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「異常與事故」：偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「基線模型」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring anomaly versus incident: Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove baseline models passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-15-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-15-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 流中 200 異常；偵測 160、正常誤報 100，precision=160/260=61.54%、recall=80%。資料分布改變時這些比率亦改變。","textEn":"Among 100000 hypothetical flows with 200 anomalies, 160 detections and 100 false positives give precision=61.54% and recall=80%; distribution shifts change these values.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「基線模型」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of baseline models?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","正常變異應由代表性資料估計。","只檢查「異常與事故」，便可取代「基線模型」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Estimate benign variability from representative data.","Checking anomaly versus incident alone replaces verification specific to baseline models."],"answer":1,"explanation":"正常變異應由代表性資料估計。 相鄰的「異常與事故」有不同責任：偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Estimate benign variability from representative data. Neighboring anomaly versus incident has a different role: Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-15"],"title":"基線模型：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Baseline models: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「基線模型」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For baseline models, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「正常變異應由代表性資料估計。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「異常與事故」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Estimate benign variability from representative data. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from anomaly versus incident to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 比較「基線模型」與「異常與事故」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Compare whether evidence for baseline models and anomaly versus incident supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「基線模型」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for baseline models. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-16-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"正常變異應由代表性資料估計。","textEn":"Estimate benign variability from representative data.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-16-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「異常與事故」：偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「基線模型」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring anomaly versus incident: Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove baseline models passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-16-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較只有流量摘要與完整合成協議記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare flow summaries with complete synthetic protocol records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-16-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 流中 200 異常；偵測 160、正常誤報 100，precision=160/260=61.54%、recall=80%。資料分布改變時這些比率亦改變。","textEn":"Among 100000 hypothetical flows with 200 anomalies, 160 detections and 100 false positives give precision=61.54% and recall=80%; distribution shifts change these values.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「基線模型」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of baseline models?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","正常變異應由代表性資料估計。","只檢查「異常與事故」，便可取代「基線模型」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Estimate benign variability from representative data.","Checking anomaly versus incident alone replaces verification specific to baseline models."],"answer":1,"explanation":"正常變異應由代表性資料估計。 相鄰的「異常與事故」有不同責任：偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Estimate benign variability from representative data. Neighboring anomaly versus incident has a different role: Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a363-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"驗證、故障與防禦邊界","titleEn":"Validation, faults and defensive boundaries","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a363-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-16"],"title":"異常與事故：架構與原理","titleEn":"Anomaly versus incident: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「異常與事故」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For anomaly versus incident, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「異常與事故」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改加密比例。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「偵測門檻」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around anomaly versus incident, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat detection thresholds as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「異常與事故」與「偵測門檻」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for anomaly versus incident and detection thresholds supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「異常與事故」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for anomaly versus incident. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-17-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。","textEn":"Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-17-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「偵測門檻」：低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「異常與事故」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring detection thresholds: Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove anomaly versus incident passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-17-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「異常與事故」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of anomaly versus incident?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「偵測門檻」，便可取代「異常與事故」的專屬驗證。","偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking detection thresholds alone replaces verification specific to anomaly versus incident.","Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。 相鄰的「偵測門檻」有不同責任：低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Neighboring detection thresholds has a different role: Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-17"],"title":"異常與事故：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Anomaly versus incident: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「異常與事故」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For anomaly versus incident, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改加密比例。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「偵測門檻」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from detection thresholds to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「異常與事故」與「偵測門檻」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for anomaly versus incident and detection thresholds supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「異常與事故」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for anomaly versus incident. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-18-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。","textEn":"Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-18-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「偵測門檻」：低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「異常與事故」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring detection thresholds: Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove anomaly versus incident passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-18-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「異常與事故」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of anomaly versus incident?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「偵測門檻」，便可取代「異常與事故」的專屬驗證。","偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking detection thresholds alone replaces verification specific to anomaly versus incident.","Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion."],"answer":2,"explanation":"偏離基線不自動等於已確認入侵。 相鄰的「偵測門檻」有不同責任：低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Baseline deviation is not automatically confirmed intrusion. Neighboring detection thresholds has a different role: Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-18"],"title":"偵測門檻：架構與原理","titleEn":"Detection thresholds: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「偵測門檻」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For detection thresholds, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「偵測門檻」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改加密比例。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「低基準率」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around detection thresholds, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat low base rates as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「偵測門檻」與「低基準率」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for detection thresholds and low base rates supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「偵測門檻」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for detection thresholds. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-19-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。","textEn":"Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-19-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「低基準率」：異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「偵測門檻」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring low base rates: Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove detection thresholds passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-19-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「偵測門檻」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of detection thresholds?","options":["低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。","封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「低基準率」，便可取代「偵測門檻」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives.","Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking low base rates alone replaces verification specific to detection thresholds."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。 相鄰的「低基準率」有不同責任：異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Neighboring low base rates has a different role: Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-19"],"title":"偵測門檻：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Detection thresholds: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「偵測門檻」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For detection thresholds, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改加密比例。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「低基準率」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from low base rates to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「偵測門檻」與「低基準率」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for detection thresholds and low base rates supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「偵測門檻」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for detection thresholds. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-20-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。","textEn":"Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-20-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「低基準率」：異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「偵測門檻」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring low base rates: Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove detection thresholds passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-20-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「偵測門檻」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of detection thresholds?","options":["低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。","封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「低基準率」，便可取代「偵測門檻」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives.","Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking low base rates alone replaces verification specific to detection thresholds."],"answer":0,"explanation":"低門檻可增加召回也增加誤報。 相鄰的「低基準率」有不同責任：異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Lower thresholds can raise recall and false positives. Neighboring low base rates has a different role: Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-20"],"title":"低基準率：架構與原理","titleEn":"Low base rates: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「低基準率」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For low base rates, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「低基準率」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改加密比例。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「效能限制」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around low base rates, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat performance limits as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「低基準率」與「效能限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for low base rates and performance limits supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「低基準率」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for low base rates. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-21-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。","textEn":"Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-21-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「效能限制」：解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「低基準率」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring performance limits: Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove low base rates passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-21-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「低基準率」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of low base rates?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。","只檢查「效能限制」，便可取代「低基準率」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision.","Checking performance limits alone replaces verification specific to low base rates."],"answer":1,"explanation":"異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。 相鄰的「效能限制」有不同責任：解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Neighboring performance limits has a different role: Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-21"],"title":"低基準率：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Low base rates: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「低基準率」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For low base rates, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改加密比例。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「效能限制」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from performance limits to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「低基準率」與「效能限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for low base rates and performance limits supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「低基準率」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for low base rates. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-22-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。","textEn":"Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-22-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「效能限制」：解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「低基準率」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring performance limits: Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove low base rates passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-22-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「低基準率」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of low base rates?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。","只檢查「效能限制」，便可取代「低基準率」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision.","Checking performance limits alone replaces verification specific to low base rates."],"answer":1,"explanation":"異常稀少時少量誤報亦降低 precision。 相鄰的「效能限制」有不同責任：解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Rare anomalies allow modest false alarms to reduce precision. Neighboring performance limits has a different role: Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-22"],"title":"效能限制：架構與原理","titleEn":"Performance limits: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「效能限制」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For performance limits, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「效能限制」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改加密比例。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「告警關聯」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around performance limits, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat alert correlation as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「效能限制」與「告警關聯」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for performance limits and alert correlation supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「效能限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for performance limits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-23-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。","textEn":"Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-23-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「告警關聯」：告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「效能限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring alert correlation: Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove performance limits passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-23-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「效能限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of performance limits?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「告警關聯」，便可取代「效能限制」的專屬驗證。","解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking alert correlation alone replaces verification specific to performance limits.","Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。 相鄰的「告警關聯」有不同責任：告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Neighboring alert correlation has a different role: Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-23"],"title":"效能限制：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Performance limits: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「效能限制」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For performance limits, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改加密比例。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「告警關聯」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from alert correlation to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 比較「效能限制」與「告警關聯」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Compare whether evidence for performance limits and alert correlation supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「效能限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for performance limits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-24-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。","textEn":"Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-24-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「告警關聯」：告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「效能限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring alert correlation: Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove performance limits passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-24-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改加密比例。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary encrypted-traffic share. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「效能限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of performance limits?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「告警關聯」，便可取代「效能限制」的專屬驗證。","解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking alert correlation alone replaces verification specific to performance limits.","Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"解析成本與流量峰值須在容量中計入。 相鄰的「告警關聯」有不同責任：告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Capacity must include parsing cost and traffic peaks. Neighboring alert correlation has a different role: Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a363-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"效能、復原與證據交接","titleEn":"Performance, recovery and evidence handoff","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a363-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-24"],"title":"告警關聯：架構與原理","titleEn":"Alert correlation: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「告警關聯」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For alert correlation, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「告警關聯」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「受控資料」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around alert correlation, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat controlled data as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「告警關聯」與「受控資料」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for alert correlation and controlled data supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「告警關聯」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for alert correlation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-25-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。","textEn":"Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-25-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「受控資料」：實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「告警關聯」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring controlled data: Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove alert correlation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-25-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「告警關聯」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of alert correlation?","options":["告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。","IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「受控資料」，便可取代「告警關聯」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence.","An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking controlled data alone replaces verification specific to alert correlation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。 相鄰的「受控資料」有不同責任：實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Neighboring controlled data has a different role: Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-25"],"title":"告警關聯：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Alert correlation: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「告警關聯」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For alert correlation, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「受控資料」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from controlled data to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「告警關聯」與「受控資料」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for alert correlation and controlled data supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「告警關聯」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for alert correlation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-26-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。","textEn":"Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-26-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「受控資料」：實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「告警關聯」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring controlled data: Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove alert correlation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-26-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「告警關聯」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of alert correlation?","options":["告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。","IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「受控資料」，便可取代「告警關聯」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence.","An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking controlled data alone replaces verification specific to alert correlation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"告警需與身分、端點及時間證據互證。 相鄰的「受控資料」有不同責任：實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Corroborate alerts with identity, endpoint and timing evidence. Neighboring controlled data has a different role: Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-26"],"title":"受控資料：架構與原理","titleEn":"Controlled data: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「受控資料」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For controlled data, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「受控資料」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「規則版本」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around controlled data, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat rule versions as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「受控資料」與「規則版本」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for controlled data and rule versions supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「受控資料」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for controlled data. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-27-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。","textEn":"Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-27-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「規則版本」：固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「受控資料」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring rule versions: Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove controlled data passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-27-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「受控資料」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of controlled data?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。","只檢查「規則版本」，便可取代「受控資料」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only.","Checking rule versions alone replaces verification specific to controlled data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。 相鄰的「規則版本」有不同責任：固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Neighboring rule versions has a different role: Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-27"],"title":"受控資料：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Controlled data: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「受控資料」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For controlled data, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「規則版本」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from rule versions to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「受控資料」與「規則版本」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for controlled data and rule versions supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「受控資料」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for controlled data. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-28-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。","textEn":"Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-28-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「規則版本」：固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「受控資料」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring rule versions: Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove controlled data passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-28-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「受控資料」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of controlled data?","options":["封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。","只檢查「規則版本」，便可取代「受控資料」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only.","Checking rule versions alone replaces verification specific to controlled data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"實作只使用自行生成資料或獲授權檔案。 相鄰的「規則版本」有不同責任：固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Labs use authored synthetic data or authorized files only. Neighboring rule versions has a different role: Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-28"],"title":"規則版本：架構與原理","titleEn":"Rule versions: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「規則版本」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For rule versions, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「規則版本」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「盲點報告」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around rule versions, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat blind-spot reporting as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「規則版本」與「盲點報告」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for rule versions and blind-spot reporting supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「規則版本」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for rule versions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-29-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。","textEn":"Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-29-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「盲點報告」：報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「規則版本」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring blind-spot reporting: Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove rule versions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-29-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「規則版本」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of rule versions?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「盲點報告」，便可取代「規則版本」的專屬驗證。","固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking blind-spot reporting alone replaces verification specific to rule versions.","Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。 相鄰的「盲點報告」有不同責任：報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Neighboring blind-spot reporting has a different role: Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-29"],"title":"規則版本：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Rule versions: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「規則版本」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For rule versions, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「盲點報告」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from blind-spot reporting to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「規則版本」與「盲點報告」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for rule versions and blind-spot reporting supports the same inference.","failure":"IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「規則版本」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for rule versions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-30-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。","textEn":"Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-30-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「盲點報告」：報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「規則版本」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring blind-spot reporting: Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove rule versions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-30-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「規則版本」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of rule versions?","options":["IDS 能直接讀取所有 TLS 加密內文。","只檢查「盲點報告」，便可取代「規則版本」的專屬驗證。","固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。"],"optionsEn":["An IDS directly reads every TLS-encrypted payload.","Checking blind-spot reporting alone replaces verification specific to rule versions.","Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"固定版本及設定才能重現判斷。 相鄰的「盲點報告」有不同責任：報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Pinned versions/configurations enable reproducible decisions. Neighboring blind-spot reporting has a different role: Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-30"],"title":"盲點報告：架構與原理","titleEn":"Blind-spot reporting: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「盲點報告」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For blind-spot reporting, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「盲點報告」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「觀察點」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around blind-spot reporting, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat observation points as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「盲點報告」與「觀察點」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for blind-spot reporting and observation points supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「盲點報告」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for blind-spot reporting. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-31-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。","textEn":"Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-31-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「觀察點」：觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「盲點報告」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring observation points: Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove blind-spot reporting passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-31-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-31-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 流中 200 異常；偵測 160、正常誤報 100，precision=160/260=61.54%、recall=80%。資料分布改變時這些比率亦改變。","textEn":"Among 100000 hypothetical flows with 200 anomalies, 160 detections and 100 false positives give precision=61.54% and recall=80%; distribution shifts change these values.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「盲點報告」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of blind-spot reporting?","options":["報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。","封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「觀察點」，便可取代「盲點報告」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection.","Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking observation points alone replaces verification specific to blind-spot reporting."],"answer":0,"explanation":"報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。 相鄰的「觀察點」有不同責任：觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Neighboring observation points has a different role: Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a363-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a363-v11-31"],"title":"盲點報告：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Blind-spot reporting: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「盲點報告」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For blind-spot reporting, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「觀察點」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from observation points to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 比較「盲點報告」與「觀察點」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Compare whether evidence for blind-spot reporting and observation points supports the same inference.","failure":"封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「盲點報告」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for blind-spot reporting. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a363-v11-32-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。","textEn":"Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-32-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「觀察點」：觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「盲點報告」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring observation points: Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove blind-spot reporting passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-32-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬感測器丟包導致的證據缺口。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model sensor packet loss and resulting evidence gaps. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a363-v11-32-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 流中 200 異常；偵測 160、正常誤報 100，precision=160/260=61.54%、recall=80%。資料分布改變時這些比率亦改變。","textEn":"Among 100000 hypothetical flows with 200 anomalies, 160 detections and 100 false positives give precision=61.54% and recall=80%; distribution shifts change these values.","sourceIds":["v11b-suricata","v11b-attack","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「盲點報告」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of blind-spot reporting?","options":["報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。","封包數沒有遺漏便保證應用解析完全正確。","只檢查「觀察點」，便可取代「盲點報告」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection.","Complete packet counts guarantee correct application parsing.","Checking observation points alone replaces verification specific to blind-spot reporting."],"answer":0,"explanation":"報告應列明未觀察區域而非聲稱全部防護。 相鄰的「觀察點」有不同責任：觀察位置決定看見哪些方向與流量。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Report unobserved regions rather than claiming complete protection. Neighboring observation points has a different role: Observation placement determines visible directions/traffic. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]}],"scope":"公開原理的離線／本地合成資料工程教育。只使用自行生成資料或明確獲授權的測試環境；不提供真實目標掃描、漏洞利用、惡意程式、車輛／工控注入或實際射頻發射程序。數值為原創假設，非供應商保證或現場驗收標準。","scopeEn":"Offline/local synthetic-data engineering education from public principles. Use authored data or explicitly authorized test environments only. No real-target scanning, exploitation, malware, vehicle/OT injection or live RF procedures. Numerical cases are original assumptions, not supplier guarantees or field acceptance criteria.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想量化例與限制","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative case and limits","text":"假想 100000 流中 200 異常；偵測 160、正常誤報 100，precision=160/260=61.54%、recall=80%。資料分布改變時這些比率亦改變。","textEn":"Among 100000 hypothetical flows with 200 anomalies, 160 detections and 100 false positives give precision=61.54% and recall=80%; distribution shifts change these values.","assumptions":"只採算例中明列的教學條件；效能與安全估計須依拓撲、分布、開銷、版本與不確定度重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use only the stated teaching assumptions; recalculate for topology, distribution, overhead, versions and uncertainty.","sourceScope":"作者自行設定的教學數值；官方來源支援原理與尺寸規格，未聲稱量測此假想平台。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen teaching inputs; official sources support principles and specified material sizes, not measurements of this hypothetical platform."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["觀察點","協議解碼","異常與事故","告警關聯"],"labelsEn":["Observation points","Protocol decoding","Anomaly versus incident","Alert correlation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a364","title":"工控網路分區與隔離","titleEn":"Industrial-control network segmentation","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以OT 區域、通道與不中斷的防禦證據串連 16 個領域技術單元、32 個保存步驟；分析架構、原理、介面、故障、量化案例與防禦證據。","summaryEn":"Sixteen domain-specific technical units and 32 saved steps connect ot zones, conduits and non-disruptive defensive evidence through architecture, principles, interfaces, faults, quantitative cases and defensive evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":11,"depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a364-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求、元件與基本模型","titleEn":"Requirements, components and baseline models","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a364-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"OT 資產邊界：架構與原理","titleEn":"OT asset boundaries: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「OT 資產邊界」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For ot asset boundaries, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「OT 資產邊界」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「程序依賴」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around ot asset boundaries, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat process dependencies as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「OT 資產邊界」與「程序依賴」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for ot asset boundaries and process dependencies supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「OT 資產邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for ot asset boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-01-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。","textEn":"Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-01-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「程序依賴」：網路中斷可能影響物理程序。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「OT 資產邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring process dependencies: Network disruption can affect physical processes. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove ot asset boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-01-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-01-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 12 區原本任意雙向連通，共 12×11=132 有向關係；核准流程只需 18 關係，減少 114 個允許方向。這只衡量可達性，不能當作風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Twelve fully connected zones have 132 directed relationships; approved flows need 18, removing 114 allowed directions. This measures reachability, not a percentage risk reduction.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「OT 資產邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of ot asset boundaries?","options":["控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。","OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「程序依賴」，便可取代「OT 資產邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs.","OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking process dependencies alone replaces verification specific to ot asset boundaries."],"answer":0,"explanation":"控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。 相鄰的「程序依賴」有不同責任：網路中斷可能影響物理程序。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Neighboring process dependencies has a different role: Network disruption can affect physical processes. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-01"],"title":"OT 資產邊界：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"OT asset boundaries: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「OT 資產邊界」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For ot asset boundaries, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「程序依賴」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from process dependencies to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「OT 資產邊界」與「程序依賴」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for ot asset boundaries and process dependencies supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「OT 資產邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for ot asset boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-02-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。","textEn":"Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-02-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「程序依賴」：網路中斷可能影響物理程序。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「OT 資產邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring process dependencies: Network disruption can affect physical processes. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove ot asset boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-02-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-02-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 12 區原本任意雙向連通，共 12×11=132 有向關係；核准流程只需 18 關係，減少 114 個允許方向。這只衡量可達性，不能當作風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Twelve fully connected zones have 132 directed relationships; approved flows need 18, removing 114 allowed directions. This measures reachability, not a percentage risk reduction.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「OT 資產邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of ot asset boundaries?","options":["控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。","OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「程序依賴」，便可取代「OT 資產邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs.","OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking process dependencies alone replaces verification specific to ot asset boundaries."],"answer":0,"explanation":"控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。 相鄰的「程序依賴」有不同責任：網路中斷可能影響物理程序。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Neighboring process dependencies has a different role: Network disruption can affect physical processes. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-02"],"title":"程序依賴：架構與原理","titleEn":"Process dependencies: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「程序依賴」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For process dependencies, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「程序依賴」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：網路中斷可能影響物理程序。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「區域定義」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around process dependencies, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Network disruption can affect physical processes. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat zone definitions as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「程序依賴」與「區域定義」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for process dependencies and zone definitions supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「程序依賴」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for process dependencies. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-03-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"網路中斷可能影響物理程序。","textEn":"Network disruption can affect physical processes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-03-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「區域定義」：區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「程序依賴」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring zone definitions: Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove process dependencies passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-03-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「程序依賴」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of process dependencies?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","網路中斷可能影響物理程序。","只檢查「區域定義」，便可取代「程序依賴」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Network disruption can affect physical processes.","Checking zone definitions alone replaces verification specific to process dependencies."],"answer":1,"explanation":"網路中斷可能影響物理程序。 相鄰的「區域定義」有不同責任：區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Network disruption can affect physical processes. Neighboring zone definitions has a different role: Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-03"],"title":"程序依賴：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Process dependencies: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「程序依賴」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For process dependencies, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「網路中斷可能影響物理程序。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「區域定義」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Network disruption can affect physical processes. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from zone definitions to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「程序依賴」與「區域定義」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for process dependencies and zone definitions supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「程序依賴」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for process dependencies. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-04-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"網路中斷可能影響物理程序。","textEn":"Network disruption can affect physical processes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-04-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「區域定義」：區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「程序依賴」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring zone definitions: Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove process dependencies passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-04-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「程序依賴」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of process dependencies?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","網路中斷可能影響物理程序。","只檢查「區域定義」，便可取代「程序依賴」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Network disruption can affect physical processes.","Checking zone definitions alone replaces verification specific to process dependencies."],"answer":1,"explanation":"網路中斷可能影響物理程序。 相鄰的「區域定義」有不同責任：區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Network disruption can affect physical processes. Neighboring zone definitions has a different role: Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-04"],"title":"區域定義：架構與原理","titleEn":"Zone definitions: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「區域定義」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For zone definitions, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「區域定義」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「通道定義」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around zone definitions, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat conduit definitions as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「區域定義」與「通道定義」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for zone definitions and conduit definitions supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「區域定義」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for zone definitions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-05-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。","textEn":"Zones group function/risk, not merely floors.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-05-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「通道定義」：跨區通道應對應必要業務流。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「區域定義」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring conduit definitions: Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove zone definitions passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-05-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「區域定義」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of zone definitions?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「通道定義」，便可取代「區域定義」的專屬驗證。","區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking conduit definitions alone replaces verification specific to zone definitions.","Zones group function/risk, not merely floors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。 相鄰的「通道定義」有不同責任：跨區通道應對應必要業務流。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Neighboring conduit definitions has a different role: Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-05"],"title":"區域定義：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Zone definitions: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「區域定義」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For zone definitions, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「通道定義」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from conduit definitions to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「區域定義」與「通道定義」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for zone definitions and conduit definitions supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「區域定義」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for zone definitions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-06-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。","textEn":"Zones group function/risk, not merely floors.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-06-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「通道定義」：跨區通道應對應必要業務流。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「區域定義」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring conduit definitions: Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove zone definitions passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-06-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「區域定義」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of zone definitions?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「通道定義」，便可取代「區域定義」的專屬驗證。","區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking conduit definitions alone replaces verification specific to zone definitions.","Zones group function/risk, not merely floors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"區域按功能與風險組合，不僅按樓層。 相鄰的「通道定義」有不同責任：跨區通道應對應必要業務流。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Zones group function/risk, not merely floors. Neighboring conduit definitions has a different role: Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-06"],"title":"通道定義：架構與原理","titleEn":"Conduit definitions: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「通道定義」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For conduit definitions, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「通道定義」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：跨區通道應對應必要業務流。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「流矩陣」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around conduit definitions, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat flow matrices as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「通道定義」與「流矩陣」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for conduit definitions and flow matrices supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「通道定義」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for conduit definitions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-07-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"跨區通道應對應必要業務流。","textEn":"Interzone conduits should map required operational flows.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-07-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「流矩陣」：來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「通道定義」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring flow matrices: Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove conduit definitions passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-07-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「通道定義」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of conduit definitions?","options":["跨區通道應對應必要業務流。","VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「流矩陣」，便可取代「通道定義」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Interzone conduits should map required operational flows.","Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking flow matrices alone replaces verification specific to conduit definitions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"跨區通道應對應必要業務流。 相鄰的「流矩陣」有不同責任：來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Neighboring flow matrices has a different role: Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-07"],"title":"通道定義：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Conduit definitions: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「通道定義」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For conduit definitions, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「跨區通道應對應必要業務流。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「流矩陣」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from flow matrices to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 比較「通道定義」與「流矩陣」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Compare whether evidence for conduit definitions and flow matrices supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「通道定義」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for conduit definitions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-08-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"跨區通道應對應必要業務流。","textEn":"Interzone conduits should map required operational flows.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-08-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「流矩陣」：來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「通道定義」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring flow matrices: Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove conduit definitions passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-08-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定設備，只改核准流矩陣。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix equipment and vary approved-flow matrices. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「通道定義」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of conduit definitions?","options":["跨區通道應對應必要業務流。","VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「流矩陣」，便可取代「通道定義」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Interzone conduits should map required operational flows.","Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking flow matrices alone replaces verification specific to conduit definitions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"跨區通道應對應必要業務流。 相鄰的「流矩陣」有不同責任：來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Interzone conduits should map required operational flows. Neighboring flow matrices has a different role: Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a364-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"介面、狀態與資源配置","titleEn":"Interfaces, states and resource allocation","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a364-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-08"],"title":"流矩陣：架構與原理","titleEn":"Flow matrices: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「流矩陣」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For flow matrices, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「流矩陣」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「IT/OT 介面」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around flow matrices, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat it/ot interfaces as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「流矩陣」與「IT/OT 介面」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for flow matrices and it/ot interfaces supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「流矩陣」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for flow matrices. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-09-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。","textEn":"Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-09-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「IT/OT 介面」：緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「流矩陣」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring it/ot interfaces: DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove flow matrices passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-09-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「流矩陣」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of flow matrices?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。","只檢查「IT/OT 介面」，便可取代「流矩陣」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules.","Checking it/ot interfaces alone replaces verification specific to flow matrices."],"answer":1,"explanation":"來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。 相鄰的「IT/OT 介面」有不同責任：緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Neighboring it/ot interfaces has a different role: DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-09"],"title":"流矩陣：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Flow matrices: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「流矩陣」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For flow matrices, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「IT/OT 介面」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from it/ot interfaces to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「流矩陣」與「IT/OT 介面」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for flow matrices and it/ot interfaces supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「流矩陣」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for flow matrices. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-10-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。","textEn":"Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-10-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「IT/OT 介面」：緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「流矩陣」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring it/ot interfaces: DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove flow matrices passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-10-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「流矩陣」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of flow matrices?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。","只檢查「IT/OT 介面」，便可取代「流矩陣」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules.","Checking it/ot interfaces alone replaces verification specific to flow matrices."],"answer":1,"explanation":"來源、目的、方向與協議共同限定規則。 相鄰的「IT/OT 介面」有不同責任：緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Source, destination, direction and protocol constrain rules. Neighboring it/ot interfaces has a different role: DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-10"],"title":"IT/OT 介面：架構與原理","titleEn":"IT/OT interfaces: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「IT/OT 介面」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For it/ot interfaces, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「IT/OT 介面」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「遠端維護」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around it/ot interfaces, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat remote maintenance as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「IT/OT 介面」與「遠端維護」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for it/ot interfaces and remote maintenance supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「IT/OT 介面」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for it/ot interfaces. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-11-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。","textEn":"DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-11-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「遠端維護」：維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「IT/OT 介面」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring remote maintenance: Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove it/ot interfaces passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-11-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「IT/OT 介面」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of it/ot interfaces?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「遠端維護」，便可取代「IT/OT 介面」的專屬驗證。","緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking remote maintenance alone replaces verification specific to it/ot interfaces.","DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。 相鄰的「遠端維護」有不同責任：維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Neighboring remote maintenance has a different role: Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-11"],"title":"IT/OT 介面：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"IT/OT interfaces: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「IT/OT 介面」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For it/ot interfaces, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「遠端維護」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from remote maintenance to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「IT/OT 介面」與「遠端維護」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for it/ot interfaces and remote maintenance supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「IT/OT 介面」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for it/ot interfaces. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-12-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。","textEn":"DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-12-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「遠端維護」：維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「IT/OT 介面」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring remote maintenance: Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove it/ot interfaces passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-12-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「IT/OT 介面」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of it/ot interfaces?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「遠端維護」，便可取代「IT/OT 介面」的專屬驗證。","緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking remote maintenance alone replaces verification specific to it/ot interfaces.","DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"緩衝區降低直達性，但需明確資料交接。 相鄰的「遠端維護」有不同責任：維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"DMZs reduce direct reachability but need explicit data handoffs. Neighboring remote maintenance has a different role: Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-12"],"title":"遠端維護：架構與原理","titleEn":"Remote maintenance: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「遠端維護」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For remote maintenance, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「遠端維護」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「管理通道」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around remote maintenance, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat management conduits as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「遠端維護」與「管理通道」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for remote maintenance and management conduits supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「遠端維護」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for remote maintenance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-13-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。","textEn":"Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-13-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「管理通道」：設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「遠端維護」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring management conduits: Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove remote maintenance passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-13-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「遠端維護」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of remote maintenance?","options":["維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。","OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「管理通道」，便可取代「遠端維護」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity.","OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking management conduits alone replaces verification specific to remote maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。 相鄰的「管理通道」有不同責任：設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Neighboring management conduits has a different role: Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-13"],"title":"遠端維護：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Remote maintenance: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「遠端維護」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For remote maintenance, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「管理通道」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from management conduits to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「遠端維護」與「管理通道」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for remote maintenance and management conduits supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「遠端維護」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for remote maintenance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-14-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。","textEn":"Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-14-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「管理通道」：設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「遠端維護」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring management conduits: Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove remote maintenance passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-14-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「遠端維護」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of remote maintenance?","options":["維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。","OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「管理通道」，便可取代「遠端維護」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity.","OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking management conduits alone replaces verification specific to remote maintenance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"維護需批准、限時與可歸屬身分。 相鄰的「管理通道」有不同責任：設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Maintenance needs approval, time bounds and attributable identity. Neighboring management conduits has a different role: Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-14"],"title":"管理通道：架構與原理","titleEn":"Management conduits: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「管理通道」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For management conduits, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「管理通道」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「被動盤點」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around management conduits, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat passive inventory as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「管理通道」與「被動盤點」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for management conduits and passive inventory supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「管理通道」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for management conduits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-15-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。","textEn":"Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-15-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「被動盤點」：被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「管理通道」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring passive inventory: Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove management conduits passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-15-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-15-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 12 區原本任意雙向連通，共 12×11=132 有向關係；核准流程只需 18 關係，減少 114 個允許方向。這只衡量可達性，不能當作風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Twelve fully connected zones have 132 directed relationships; approved flows need 18, removing 114 allowed directions. This measures reachability, not a percentage risk reduction.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「管理通道」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of management conduits?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。","只檢查「被動盤點」，便可取代「管理通道」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately.","Checking passive inventory alone replaces verification specific to management conduits."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。 相鄰的「被動盤點」有不同責任：被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Neighboring passive inventory has a different role: Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-15"],"title":"管理通道：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Management conduits: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「管理通道」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For management conduits, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「被動盤點」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from passive inventory to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 比較「管理通道」與「被動盤點」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Compare whether evidence for management conduits and passive inventory supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「管理通道」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for management conduits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-16-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。","textEn":"Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-16-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「被動盤點」：被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「管理通道」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring passive inventory: Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove management conduits passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-16-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較管理與程序控制通道的權限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare management/process-control conduit permissions. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-16-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 12 區原本任意雙向連通，共 12×11=132 有向關係；核准流程只需 18 關係，減少 114 個允許方向。這只衡量可達性，不能當作風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Twelve fully connected zones have 132 directed relationships; approved flows need 18, removing 114 allowed directions. This measures reachability, not a percentage risk reduction.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「管理通道」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of management conduits?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。","只檢查「被動盤點」，便可取代「管理通道」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately.","Checking passive inventory alone replaces verification specific to management conduits."],"answer":1,"explanation":"設備管理不應混用程序控制權限。 相鄰的「被動盤點」有不同責任：被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Management should not share process-control privileges indiscriminately. Neighboring passive inventory has a different role: Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a364-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"驗證、故障與防禦邊界","titleEn":"Validation, faults and defensive boundaries","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a364-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-16"],"title":"被動盤點：架構與原理","titleEn":"Passive inventory: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「被動盤點」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For passive inventory, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「被動盤點」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「協議限制」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around passive inventory, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat protocol limitations as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「被動盤點」與「協議限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for passive inventory and protocol limitations supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「被動盤點」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for passive inventory. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-17-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。","textEn":"Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-17-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「協議限制」：舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「被動盤點」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring protocol limitations: Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove passive inventory passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-17-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「被動盤點」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of passive inventory?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「協議限制」，便可取代「被動盤點」的專屬驗證。","被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking protocol limitations alone replaces verification specific to passive inventory.","Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。 相鄰的「協議限制」有不同責任：舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Neighboring protocol limitations has a different role: Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-17"],"title":"被動盤點：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Passive inventory: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「被動盤點」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For passive inventory, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「協議限制」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from protocol limitations to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「被動盤點」與「協議限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for passive inventory and protocol limitations supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「被動盤點」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for passive inventory. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-18-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。","textEn":"Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-18-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「協議限制」：舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「被動盤點」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring protocol limitations: Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove passive inventory passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-18-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「被動盤點」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of passive inventory?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「協議限制」，便可取代「被動盤點」的專屬驗證。","被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking protocol limitations alone replaces verification specific to passive inventory.","Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets."],"answer":2,"explanation":"被動觀察減少干擾，但可能漏掉離線資產。 相鄰的「協議限制」有不同責任：舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Passive observation reduces disruption but can miss offline assets. Neighboring protocol limitations has a different role: Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-18"],"title":"協議限制：架構與原理","titleEn":"Protocol limitations: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「協議限制」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For protocol limitations, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「協議限制」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「單向資料」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around protocol limitations, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat unidirectional data as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「協議限制」與「單向資料」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for protocol limitations and unidirectional data supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「協議限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for protocol limitations. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-19-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。","textEn":"Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-19-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「單向資料」：單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「協議限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring unidirectional data: One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove protocol limitations passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-19-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「協議限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of protocol limitations?","options":["舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。","VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「單向資料」，便可取代「協議限制」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection.","Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking unidirectional data alone replaces verification specific to protocol limitations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。 相鄰的「單向資料」有不同責任：單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Neighboring unidirectional data has a different role: One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-19"],"title":"協議限制：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Protocol limitations: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「協議限制」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For protocol limitations, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「單向資料」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from unidirectional data to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「協議限制」與「單向資料」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for protocol limitations and unidirectional data supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「協議限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for protocol limitations. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-20-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。","textEn":"Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-20-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「單向資料」：單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「協議限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring unidirectional data: One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove protocol limitations passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-20-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「協議限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of protocol limitations?","options":["舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。","VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「單向資料」，便可取代「協議限制」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection.","Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking unidirectional data alone replaces verification specific to protocol limitations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊協議可能缺少身分與完整性保護。 相鄰的「單向資料」有不同責任：單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Legacy protocols may lack identity/integrity protection. Neighboring unidirectional data has a different role: One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-20"],"title":"單向資料：架構與原理","titleEn":"Unidirectional data: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「單向資料」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For unidirectional data, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「單向資料」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「變更窗口」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around unidirectional data, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat change windows as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「單向資料」與「變更窗口」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for unidirectional data and change windows supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「單向資料」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for unidirectional data. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-21-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。","textEn":"One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-21-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「變更窗口」：變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「單向資料」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring change windows: Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove unidirectional data passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-21-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「單向資料」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of unidirectional data?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。","只檢查「變更窗口」，便可取代「單向資料」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies.","Checking change windows alone replaces verification specific to unidirectional data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。 相鄰的「變更窗口」有不同責任：變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Neighboring change windows has a different role: Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-21"],"title":"單向資料：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Unidirectional data: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「單向資料」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For unidirectional data, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「變更窗口」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from change windows to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「單向資料」與「變更窗口」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for unidirectional data and change windows supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「單向資料」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for unidirectional data. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-22-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。","textEn":"One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-22-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「變更窗口」：變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「單向資料」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring change windows: Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove unidirectional data passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-22-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「單向資料」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of unidirectional data?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。","只檢查「變更窗口」，便可取代「單向資料」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies.","Checking change windows alone replaces verification specific to unidirectional data."],"answer":1,"explanation":"單向需求須檢查應用是否仍需回覆。 相鄰的「變更窗口」有不同責任：變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"One-way requirements must check application reply dependencies. Neighboring change windows has a different role: Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-22"],"title":"變更窗口：架構與原理","titleEn":"Change windows: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「變更窗口」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For change windows, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「變更窗口」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「補丁取捨」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around change windows, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat patch tradeoffs as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「變更窗口」與「補丁取捨」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for change windows and patch tradeoffs supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「變更窗口」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for change windows. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-23-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。","textEn":"Changes need approved windows and validated rollback.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-23-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「補丁取捨」：補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「變更窗口」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring patch tradeoffs: Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove change windows passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-23-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「變更窗口」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of change windows?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「補丁取捨」，便可取代「變更窗口」的專屬驗證。","變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking patch tradeoffs alone replaces verification specific to change windows.","Changes need approved windows and validated rollback."],"answer":2,"explanation":"變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。 相鄰的「補丁取捨」有不同責任：補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Neighboring patch tradeoffs has a different role: Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-23"],"title":"變更窗口：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Change windows: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「變更窗口」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For change windows, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「補丁取捨」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from patch tradeoffs to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 比較「變更窗口」與「補丁取捨」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Compare whether evidence for change windows and patch tradeoffs supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「變更窗口」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for change windows. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-24-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。","textEn":"Changes need approved windows and validated rollback.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-24-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「補丁取捨」：補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「變更窗口」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring patch tradeoffs: Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove change windows passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-24-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改維護例外期限。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary maintenance-exception expiry. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「變更窗口」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of change windows?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「補丁取捨」，便可取代「變更窗口」的專屬驗證。","變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking patch tradeoffs alone replaces verification specific to change windows.","Changes need approved windows and validated rollback."],"answer":2,"explanation":"變更需在核准窗口與已驗證回滾下進行。 相鄰的「補丁取捨」有不同責任：補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Changes need approved windows and validated rollback. Neighboring patch tradeoffs has a different role: Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a364-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"效能、復原與證據交接","titleEn":"Performance, recovery and evidence handoff","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a364-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-24"],"title":"補丁取捨：架構與原理","titleEn":"Patch tradeoffs: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「補丁取捨」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For patch tradeoffs, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「補丁取捨」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「事件保存」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around patch tradeoffs, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat event preservation as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「補丁取捨」與「事件保存」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for patch tradeoffs and event preservation supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「補丁取捨」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for patch tradeoffs. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-25-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。","textEn":"Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-25-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「事件保存」：日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「補丁取捨」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring event preservation: Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove patch tradeoffs passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-25-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「補丁取捨」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of patch tradeoffs?","options":["補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。","OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「事件保存」，便可取代「補丁取捨」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation.","OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking event preservation alone replaces verification specific to patch tradeoffs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。 相鄰的「事件保存」有不同責任：日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Neighboring event preservation has a different role: Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-25"],"title":"補丁取捨：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Patch tradeoffs: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「補丁取捨」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For patch tradeoffs, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「事件保存」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from event preservation to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「補丁取捨」與「事件保存」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for patch tradeoffs and event preservation supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「補丁取捨」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for patch tradeoffs. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-26-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。","textEn":"Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-26-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「事件保存」：日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「補丁取捨」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring event preservation: Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove patch tradeoffs passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-26-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「補丁取捨」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of patch tradeoffs?","options":["補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。","OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「事件保存」，便可取代「補丁取捨」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation.","OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking event preservation alone replaces verification specific to patch tradeoffs."],"answer":0,"explanation":"補丁需符合設備相容與程序驗證。 相鄰的「事件保存」有不同責任：日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Patches need equipment compatibility and process validation. Neighboring event preservation has a different role: Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-26"],"title":"事件保存：架構與原理","titleEn":"Event preservation: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「事件保存」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For event preservation, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「事件保存」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「安全降階」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around event preservation, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat safe degradation as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「事件保存」與「安全降階」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for event preservation and safe degradation supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「事件保存」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for event preservation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-27-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。","textEn":"Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-27-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「安全降階」：網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「事件保存」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring safe degradation: Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove event preservation passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-27-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「事件保存」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of event preservation?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。","只檢查「安全降階」，便可取代「事件保存」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations.","Checking safe degradation alone replaces verification specific to event preservation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。 相鄰的「安全降階」有不同責任：網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Neighboring safe degradation has a different role: Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-27"],"title":"事件保存：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Event preservation: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「事件保存」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For event preservation, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「安全降階」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from safe degradation to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「事件保存」與「安全降階」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for event preservation and safe degradation supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「事件保存」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for event preservation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-28-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。","textEn":"Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-28-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「安全降階」：網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「事件保存」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring safe degradation: Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove event preservation passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-28-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「事件保存」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of event preservation?","options":["VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。","只檢查「安全降階」，便可取代「事件保存」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations.","Checking safe degradation alone replaces verification specific to event preservation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"日誌應記錄區域、通道與時基限制。 相鄰的「安全降階」有不同責任：網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Logs record zones, conduits and timing limitations. Neighboring safe degradation has a different role: Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-28"],"title":"安全降階：架構與原理","titleEn":"Safe degradation: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「安全降階」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For safe degradation, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「安全降階」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「離線驗收」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around safe degradation, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat offline acceptance as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「安全降階」與「離線驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for safe degradation and offline acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「安全降階」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for safe degradation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-29-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。","textEn":"Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-29-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「離線驗收」：本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「安全降階」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring offline acceptance: This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove safe degradation passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-29-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「安全降階」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of safe degradation?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「離線驗收」，便可取代「安全降階」的專屬驗證。","網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking offline acceptance alone replaces verification specific to safe degradation.","Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design."],"answer":2,"explanation":"網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。 相鄰的「離線驗收」有不同責任：本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Neighboring offline acceptance has a different role: This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-29"],"title":"安全降階：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Safe degradation: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「安全降階」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For safe degradation, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「離線驗收」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from offline acceptance to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「安全降階」與「離線驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for safe degradation and offline acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"OT security can ignore availability and physical safety. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「安全降階」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for safe degradation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-30-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。","textEn":"Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-30-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「離線驗收」：本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「安全降階」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring offline acceptance: This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove safe degradation passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-30-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「安全降階」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of safe degradation?","options":["OT 安全可以不考慮可用性與人身安全。","只檢查「離線驗收」，便可取代「安全降階」的專屬驗證。","網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。"],"optionsEn":["OT security can ignore availability and physical safety.","Checking offline acceptance alone replaces verification specific to safe degradation.","Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design."],"answer":2,"explanation":"網路防禦不能替代正式程序安全設計。 相鄰的「離線驗收」有不同責任：本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Network defense does not replace formal process-safety design. Neighboring offline acceptance has a different role: This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-30"],"title":"離線驗收：架構與原理","titleEn":"Offline acceptance: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「離線驗收」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For offline acceptance, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「離線驗收」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「OT 資產邊界」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around offline acceptance, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat ot asset boundaries as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「離線驗收」與「OT 資產邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for offline acceptance and ot asset boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「離線驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for offline acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-31-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。","textEn":"This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-31-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「OT 資產邊界」：控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「離線驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring ot asset boundaries: Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove offline acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-31-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-31-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 12 區原本任意雙向連通，共 12×11=132 有向關係；核准流程只需 18 關係，減少 114 個允許方向。這只衡量可達性，不能當作風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Twelve fully connected zones have 132 directed relationships; approved flows need 18, removing 114 allowed directions. This measures reachability, not a percentage risk reduction.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「離線驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of offline acceptance?","options":["本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。","VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「OT 資產邊界」，便可取代「離線驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment.","Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking ot asset boundaries alone replaces verification specific to offline acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。 相鄰的「OT 資產邊界」有不同責任：控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Neighboring ot asset boundaries has a different role: Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a364-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a364-v11-31"],"title":"離線驗收：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Offline acceptance: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「離線驗收」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For offline acceptance, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「OT 資產邊界」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from ot asset boundaries to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 比較「離線驗收」與「OT 資產邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Compare whether evidence for offline acceptance and ot asset boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「離線驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for offline acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a364-v11-32-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。","textEn":"This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-32-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「OT 資產邊界」：控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「離線驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring ot asset boundaries: Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove offline acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-32-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬隔離失效與預先定義的安全降階。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model isolation failure and predefined safe degradation. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a364-v11-32-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 12 區原本任意雙向連通，共 12×11=132 有向關係；核准流程只需 18 關係，減少 114 個允許方向。這只衡量可達性，不能當作風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Twelve fully connected zones have 132 directed relationships; approved flows need 18, removing 114 allowed directions. This measures reachability, not a percentage risk reduction.","sourceIds":["v4-related-013a66fa9aff","v4-related-ecea8146f24b","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「離線驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of offline acceptance?","options":["本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。","VLAN 名稱不同即證明所有跨區流量已受控。","只檢查「OT 資產邊界」，便可取代「離線驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment.","Different VLAN names prove all interzone flows are controlled.","Checking ot asset boundaries alone replaces verification specific to offline acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本課使用流矩陣模擬，不掃描真實工控設備。 相鄰的「OT 資產邊界」有不同責任：控制器、感測與工程站有不同安全需求。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"This course simulates flow matrices without scanning live OT equipment. Neighboring ot asset boundaries has a different role: Controllers, sensing and engineering stations have different needs. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]}],"scope":"公開原理的離線／本地合成資料工程教育。只使用自行生成資料或明確獲授權的測試環境；不提供真實目標掃描、漏洞利用、惡意程式、車輛／工控注入或實際射頻發射程序。數值為原創假設，非供應商保證或現場驗收標準。","scopeEn":"Offline/local synthetic-data engineering education from public principles. Use authored data or explicitly authorized test environments only. No real-target scanning, exploitation, malware, vehicle/OT injection or live RF procedures. Numerical cases are original assumptions, not supplier guarantees or field acceptance criteria.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想量化例與限制","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative case and limits","text":"假想 12 區原本任意雙向連通，共 12×11=132 有向關係；核准流程只需 18 關係，減少 114 個允許方向。這只衡量可達性，不能當作風險降低百分比。","textEn":"Twelve fully connected zones have 132 directed relationships; approved flows need 18, removing 114 allowed directions. This measures reachability, not a percentage risk reduction.","assumptions":"只採算例中明列的教學條件；效能與安全估計須依拓撲、分布、開銷、版本與不確定度重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use only the stated teaching assumptions; recalculate for topology, distribution, overhead, versions and uncertainty.","sourceScope":"作者自行設定的教學數值；官方來源支援原理與尺寸規格，未聲稱量測此假想平台。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen teaching inputs; official sources support principles and specified material sizes, not measurements of this hypothetical platform."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["OT 資產邊界","流矩陣","被動盤點","補丁取捨"],"labelsEn":["OT asset boundaries","Flow matrices","Passive inventory","Patch tradeoffs"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a365","title":"物聯網裝置身分驗證","titleEn":"IoT device authentication","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以裝置根信任、佈建與憑據更新串連 16 個領域技術單元、32 個保存步驟；分析架構、原理、介面、故障、量化案例與防禦證據。","summaryEn":"Sixteen domain-specific technical units and 32 saved steps connect device roots of trust, provisioning and credential renewal through architecture, principles, interfaces, faults, quantitative cases and defensive evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":11,"depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a365-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求、元件與基本模型","titleEn":"Requirements, components and baseline models","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a365-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"裝置識別：架構與原理","titleEn":"Device identifiers: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「裝置識別」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For device identifiers, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「裝置識別」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「唯一憑據」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around device identifiers, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat unique credentials as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「裝置識別」與「唯一憑據」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for device identifiers and unique credentials supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「裝置識別」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for device identifiers. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-01-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。","textEn":"Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-01-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「唯一憑據」：個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「裝置識別」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring unique credentials: Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove device identifiers passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-01-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-01-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 裝置各每日驗證一次，平均 1.1574 次/s；若全於 10 min 內集中，為 166.67 次/s，平均流量不足以規劃驗證尖峰。","textEn":"100000 devices authenticating once/day average 1.1574/s; concentrating them into 10 minutes gives 166.67/s, so averages do not size authentication peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「裝置識別」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of device identifiers?","options":["序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。","所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「唯一憑據」，便可取代「裝置識別」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically.","One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking unique credentials alone replaces verification specific to device identifiers."],"answer":0,"explanation":"序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。 相鄰的「唯一憑據」有不同責任：個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Neighboring unique credentials has a different role: Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-01"],"title":"裝置識別：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Device identifiers: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「裝置識別」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For device identifiers, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「唯一憑據」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from unique credentials to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「裝置識別」與「唯一憑據」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for device identifiers and unique credentials supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「裝置識別」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for device identifiers. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-02-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。","textEn":"Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-02-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「唯一憑據」：個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「裝置識別」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring unique credentials: Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove device identifiers passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-02-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-02-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 裝置各每日驗證一次，平均 1.1574 次/s；若全於 10 min 內集中，為 166.67 次/s，平均流量不足以規劃驗證尖峰。","textEn":"100000 devices authenticating once/day average 1.1574/s; concentrating them into 10 minutes gives 166.67/s, so averages do not size authentication peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「裝置識別」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of device identifiers?","options":["序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。","所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「唯一憑據」，便可取代「裝置識別」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically.","One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking unique credentials alone replaces verification specific to device identifiers."],"answer":0,"explanation":"序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。 相鄰的「唯一憑據」有不同責任：個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Neighboring unique credentials has a different role: Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-02"],"title":"唯一憑據：架構與原理","titleEn":"Unique credentials: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「唯一憑據」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For unique credentials, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「唯一憑據」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「根信任」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around unique credentials, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat roots of trust as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「唯一憑據」與「根信任」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for unique credentials and roots of trust supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「唯一憑據」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for unique credentials. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-03-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。","textEn":"Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-03-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「根信任」：根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「唯一憑據」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring roots of trust: Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove unique credentials passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-03-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「唯一憑據」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of unique credentials?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。","只檢查「根信任」，便可取代「唯一憑據」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise.","Checking roots of trust alone replaces verification specific to unique credentials."],"answer":1,"explanation":"個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。 相鄰的「根信任」有不同責任：根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Neighboring roots of trust has a different role: Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-03"],"title":"唯一憑據：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Unique credentials: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「唯一憑據」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For unique credentials, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「根信任」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from roots of trust to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「唯一憑據」與「根信任」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for unique credentials and roots of trust supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「唯一憑據」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for unique credentials. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-04-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。","textEn":"Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-04-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「根信任」：根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「唯一憑據」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring roots of trust: Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove unique credentials passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-04-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「唯一憑據」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of unique credentials?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。","只檢查「根信任」，便可取代「唯一憑據」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise.","Checking roots of trust alone replaces verification specific to unique credentials."],"answer":1,"explanation":"個別憑據限制單裝置事故的擴散範圍。 相鄰的「根信任」有不同責任：根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Per-device credentials limit the scope of one-device compromise. Neighboring roots of trust has a different role: Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-04"],"title":"根信任：架構與原理","titleEn":"Roots of trust: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「根信任」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For roots of trust, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「根信任」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「安全佈建」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around roots of trust, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat secure provisioning as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「根信任」與「安全佈建」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for roots of trust and secure provisioning supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「根信任」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for roots of trust. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-05-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。","textEn":"Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-05-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「安全佈建」：初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「根信任」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring secure provisioning: Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove roots of trust passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-05-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「根信任」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of roots of trust?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「安全佈建」，便可取代「根信任」的專屬驗證。","根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking secure provisioning alone replaces verification specific to roots of trust.","Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。 相鄰的「安全佈建」有不同責任：初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Neighboring secure provisioning has a different role: Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-05"],"title":"根信任：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Roots of trust: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「根信任」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For roots of trust, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「安全佈建」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from secure provisioning to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「根信任」與「安全佈建」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for roots of trust and secure provisioning supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「根信任」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for roots of trust. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-06-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。","textEn":"Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-06-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「安全佈建」：初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「根信任」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring secure provisioning: Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove roots of trust passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-06-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「根信任」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of roots of trust?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「安全佈建」，便可取代「根信任」的專屬驗證。","根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking secure provisioning alone replaces verification specific to roots of trust.","Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"根信任界定最早可依據的驗證基礎。 相鄰的「安全佈建」有不同責任：初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Roots of trust define initial verifiable foundations. Neighboring secure provisioning has a different role: Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-06"],"title":"安全佈建：架構與原理","titleEn":"Secure provisioning: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「安全佈建」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For secure provisioning, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「安全佈建」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「秘密儲存」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around secure provisioning, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat secret storage as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「安全佈建」與「秘密儲存」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for secure provisioning and secret storage supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「安全佈建」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for secure provisioning. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-07-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。","textEn":"Initial identity must bind the device and owner.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-07-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「秘密儲存」：受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「安全佈建」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring secret storage: Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove secure provisioning passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-07-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「安全佈建」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of secure provisioning?","options":["初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。","遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「秘密儲存」，便可取代「安全佈建」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Initial identity must bind the device and owner.","Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking secret storage alone replaces verification specific to secure provisioning."],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。 相鄰的「秘密儲存」有不同責任：受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Neighboring secret storage has a different role: Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-07"],"title":"安全佈建：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Secure provisioning: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「安全佈建」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For secure provisioning, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「秘密儲存」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from secret storage to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 比較「安全佈建」與「秘密儲存」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Compare whether evidence for secure provisioning and secret storage supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「安全佈建」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for secure provisioning. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-08-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。","textEn":"Initial identity must bind the device and owner.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-08-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「秘密儲存」：受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「安全佈建」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring secret storage: Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove secure provisioning passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-08-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定裝置，只改憑據是否唯一。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix devices and vary credential uniqueness. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「安全佈建」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of secure provisioning?","options":["初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。","遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「秘密儲存」，便可取代「安全佈建」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Initial identity must bind the device and owner.","Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking secret storage alone replaces verification specific to secure provisioning."],"answer":0,"explanation":"初始身分需與實際裝置及所有者關聯。 相鄰的「秘密儲存」有不同責任：受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Initial identity must bind the device and owner. Neighboring secret storage has a different role: Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a365-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"介面、狀態與資源配置","titleEn":"Interfaces, states and resource allocation","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a365-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-08"],"title":"秘密儲存：架構與原理","titleEn":"Secret storage: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「秘密儲存」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For secret storage, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「秘密儲存」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「共同驗證」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around secret storage, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat mutual authentication as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「秘密儲存」與「共同驗證」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for secret storage and mutual authentication supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「秘密儲存」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for secret storage. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-09-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。","textEn":"Protected storage differs from application-read permissions.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-09-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「共同驗證」：裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「秘密儲存」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring mutual authentication: Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove secret storage passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-09-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「秘密儲存」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of secret storage?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。","只檢查「共同驗證」，便可取代「秘密儲存」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Protected storage differs from application-read permissions.","Checking mutual authentication alone replaces verification specific to secret storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。 相鄰的「共同驗證」有不同責任：裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Neighboring mutual authentication has a different role: Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-09"],"title":"秘密儲存：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Secret storage: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「秘密儲存」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For secret storage, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「共同驗證」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from mutual authentication to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「秘密儲存」與「共同驗證」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for secret storage and mutual authentication supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「秘密儲存」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for secret storage. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-10-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。","textEn":"Protected storage differs from application-read permissions.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-10-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「共同驗證」：裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「秘密儲存」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring mutual authentication: Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove secret storage passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-10-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「秘密儲存」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of secret storage?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。","只檢查「共同驗證」，便可取代「秘密儲存」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Protected storage differs from application-read permissions.","Checking mutual authentication alone replaces verification specific to secret storage."],"answer":1,"explanation":"受保護儲存與應用讀取權限須分開。 相鄰的「共同驗證」有不同責任：裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protected storage differs from application-read permissions. Neighboring mutual authentication has a different role: Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-10"],"title":"共同驗證：架構與原理","titleEn":"Mutual authentication: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「共同驗證」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For mutual authentication, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「共同驗證」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「DTLS 邊界」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around mutual authentication, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat dtls boundaries as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「共同驗證」與「DTLS 邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for mutual authentication and dtls boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「共同驗證」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for mutual authentication. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-11-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。","textEn":"Devices and services each authenticate the peer.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-11-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「DTLS 邊界」：資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「共同驗證」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring dtls boundaries: Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove mutual authentication passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-11-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「共同驗證」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of mutual authentication?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「DTLS 邊界」，便可取代「共同驗證」的專屬驗證。","裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking dtls boundaries alone replaces verification specific to mutual authentication.","Devices and services each authenticate the peer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。 相鄰的「DTLS 邊界」有不同責任：資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Neighboring dtls boundaries has a different role: Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-11"],"title":"共同驗證：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Mutual authentication: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「共同驗證」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For mutual authentication, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「DTLS 邊界」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from dtls boundaries to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「共同驗證」與「DTLS 邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for mutual authentication and dtls boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「共同驗證」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for mutual authentication. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-12-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。","textEn":"Devices and services each authenticate the peer.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-12-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「DTLS 邊界」：資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「共同驗證」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring dtls boundaries: Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove mutual authentication passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-12-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「共同驗證」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of mutual authentication?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「DTLS 邊界」，便可取代「共同驗證」的專屬驗證。","裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking dtls boundaries alone replaces verification specific to mutual authentication.","Devices and services each authenticate the peer."],"answer":2,"explanation":"裝置與服務各自確認對方身分。 相鄰的「DTLS 邊界」有不同責任：資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Devices and services each authenticate the peer. Neighboring dtls boundaries has a different role: Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-12"],"title":"DTLS 邊界：架構與原理","titleEn":"DTLS boundaries: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「DTLS 邊界」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For dtls boundaries, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「DTLS 邊界」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「時鐘限制」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around dtls boundaries, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat clock limitations as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「DTLS 邊界」與「時鐘限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for dtls boundaries and clock limitations supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「DTLS 邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for dtls boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-13-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。","textEn":"Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-13-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「時鐘限制」：低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「DTLS 邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring clock limitations: Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove dtls boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-13-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「DTLS 邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of dtls boundaries?","options":["資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。","所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「時鐘限制」，便可取代「DTLS 邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission.","One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking clock limitations alone replaces verification specific to dtls boundaries."],"answer":0,"explanation":"資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。 相鄰的「時鐘限制」有不同責任：低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Neighboring clock limitations has a different role: Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-13"],"title":"DTLS 邊界：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"DTLS boundaries: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「DTLS 邊界」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For dtls boundaries, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「時鐘限制」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from clock limitations to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「DTLS 邊界」與「時鐘限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for dtls boundaries and clock limitations supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「DTLS 邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for dtls boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-14-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。","textEn":"Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-14-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「時鐘限制」：低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「DTLS 邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring clock limitations: Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove dtls boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-14-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「DTLS 邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of dtls boundaries?","options":["資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。","所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「時鐘限制」，便可取代「DTLS 邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission.","One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking clock limitations alone replaces verification specific to dtls boundaries."],"answer":0,"explanation":"資料報安全仍需處理重排與重傳。 相鄰的「時鐘限制」有不同責任：低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Datagram security still handles reordering/retransmission. Neighboring clock limitations has a different role: Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-14"],"title":"時鐘限制：架構與原理","titleEn":"Clock limitations: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「時鐘限制」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For clock limitations, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「時鐘限制」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「新鮮挑戰」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around clock limitations, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat fresh challenges as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「時鐘限制」與「新鮮挑戰」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for clock limitations and fresh challenges supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「時鐘限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for clock limitations. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-15-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。","textEn":"Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-15-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「新鮮挑戰」：挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「時鐘限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring fresh challenges: Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove clock limitations passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-15-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-15-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 裝置各每日驗證一次，平均 1.1574 次/s；若全於 10 min 內集中，為 166.67 次/s，平均流量不足以規劃驗證尖峰。","textEn":"100000 devices authenticating once/day average 1.1574/s; concentrating them into 10 minutes gives 166.67/s, so averages do not size authentication peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「時鐘限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of clock limitations?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。","只檢查「新鮮挑戰」，便可取代「時鐘限制」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation.","Checking fresh challenges alone replaces verification specific to clock limitations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。 相鄰的「新鮮挑戰」有不同責任：挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Neighboring fresh challenges has a different role: Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-15"],"title":"時鐘限制：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Clock limitations: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「時鐘限制」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For clock limitations, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「新鮮挑戰」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from fresh challenges to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 比較「時鐘限制」與「新鮮挑戰」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Compare whether evidence for clock limitations and fresh challenges supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「時鐘限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for clock limitations. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-16-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。","textEn":"Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-16-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「新鮮挑戰」：挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「時鐘限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring fresh challenges: Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove clock limitations passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-16-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較有效與已撤銷的合成憑據。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare valid/revoked synthetic credentials. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-16-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 裝置各每日驗證一次，平均 1.1574 次/s；若全於 10 min 內集中，為 166.67 次/s，平均流量不足以規劃驗證尖峰。","textEn":"100000 devices authenticating once/day average 1.1574/s; concentrating them into 10 minutes gives 166.67/s, so averages do not size authentication peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「時鐘限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of clock limitations?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。","只檢查「新鮮挑戰」，便可取代「時鐘限制」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation.","Checking fresh challenges alone replaces verification specific to clock limitations."],"answer":1,"explanation":"低品質時鐘會影響有效期判讀。 相鄰的「新鮮挑戰」有不同責任：挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Poor clocks affect validity-window interpretation. Neighboring fresh challenges has a different role: Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a365-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"驗證、故障與防禦邊界","titleEn":"Validation, faults and defensive boundaries","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a365-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-16"],"title":"新鮮挑戰：架構與原理","titleEn":"Fresh challenges: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「新鮮挑戰」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For fresh challenges, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「新鮮挑戰」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「遠端證明」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around fresh challenges, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat remote attestation as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「新鮮挑戰」與「遠端證明」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for fresh challenges and remote attestation supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「新鮮挑戰」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for fresh challenges. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-17-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。","textEn":"Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-17-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「遠端證明」：證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「新鮮挑戰」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring remote attestation: Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove fresh challenges passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-17-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「新鮮挑戰」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of fresh challenges?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「遠端證明」，便可取代「新鮮挑戰」的專屬驗證。","挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking remote attestation alone replaces verification specific to fresh challenges.","Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values."],"answer":2,"explanation":"挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。 相鄰的「遠端證明」有不同責任：證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Neighboring remote attestation has a different role: Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-17"],"title":"新鮮挑戰：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Fresh challenges: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「新鮮挑戰」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For fresh challenges, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「遠端證明」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from remote attestation to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「新鮮挑戰」與「遠端證明」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for fresh challenges and remote attestation supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「新鮮挑戰」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for fresh challenges. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-18-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。","textEn":"Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-18-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「遠端證明」：證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「新鮮挑戰」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring remote attestation: Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove fresh challenges passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-18-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「新鮮挑戰」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of fresh challenges?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「遠端證明」，便可取代「新鮮挑戰」的專屬驗證。","挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking remote attestation alone replaces verification specific to fresh challenges.","Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values."],"answer":2,"explanation":"挑戰回應應證明當下參與而非重播舊值。 相鄰的「遠端證明」有不同責任：證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Challenge responses prove current participation, not replayed values. Neighboring remote attestation has a different role: Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-18"],"title":"遠端證明：架構與原理","titleEn":"Remote attestation: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「遠端證明」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For remote attestation, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「遠端證明」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「佈建角色」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around remote attestation, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat provisioning roles as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「遠端證明」與「佈建角色」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for remote attestation and provisioning roles supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「遠端證明」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for remote attestation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-19-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。","textEn":"Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-19-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「佈建角色」：製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「遠端證明」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring provisioning roles: Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove remote attestation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-19-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「遠端證明」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of remote attestation?","options":["證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。","遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「佈建角色」，便可取代「遠端證明」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements.","Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking provisioning roles alone replaces verification specific to remote attestation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。 相鄰的「佈建角色」有不同責任：製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Neighboring provisioning roles has a different role: Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-19"],"title":"遠端證明：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Remote attestation: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「遠端證明」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For remote attestation, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「佈建角色」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from provisioning roles to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「遠端證明」與「佈建角色」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for remote attestation and provisioning roles supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「遠端證明」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for remote attestation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-20-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。","textEn":"Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-20-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「佈建角色」：製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「遠端證明」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring provisioning roles: Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove remote attestation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-20-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「遠端證明」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of remote attestation?","options":["證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。","遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「佈建角色」，便可取代「遠端證明」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements.","Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking provisioning roles alone replaces verification specific to remote attestation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"證明報告須檢驗新鮮度及預期測量。 相鄰的「佈建角色」有不同責任：製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Attestation checks freshness and expected measurements. Neighboring provisioning roles has a different role: Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-20"],"title":"佈建角色：架構與原理","titleEn":"Provisioning roles: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「佈建角色」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For provisioning roles, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「佈建角色」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「憑據輪替」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around provisioning roles, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat credential rotation as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「佈建角色」與「憑據輪替」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for provisioning roles and credential rotation supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「佈建角色」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for provisioning roles. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-21-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。","textEn":"Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-21-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「憑據輪替」：更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「佈建角色」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring credential rotation: Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove provisioning roles passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-21-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「佈建角色」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of provisioning roles?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。","只檢查「憑據輪替」，便可取代「佈建角色」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners.","Checking credential rotation alone replaces verification specific to provisioning roles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。 相鄰的「憑據輪替」有不同責任：更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Neighboring credential rotation has a different role: Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-21"],"title":"佈建角色：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Provisioning roles: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「佈建角色」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For provisioning roles, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「憑據輪替」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from credential rotation to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「佈建角色」與「憑據輪替」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for provisioning roles and credential rotation supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「佈建角色」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for provisioning roles. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-22-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。","textEn":"Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-22-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「憑據輪替」：更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「佈建角色」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring credential rotation: Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove provisioning roles passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-22-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「佈建角色」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of provisioning roles?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。","只檢查「憑據輪替」，便可取代「佈建角色」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners.","Checking credential rotation alone replaces verification specific to provisioning roles."],"answer":1,"explanation":"製造、部署與維運可能由不同責任人完成。 相鄰的「憑據輪替」有不同責任：更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Manufacturing, deployment and operations may have different owners. Neighboring credential rotation has a different role: Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-22"],"title":"憑據輪替：架構與原理","titleEn":"Credential rotation: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「憑據輪替」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For credential rotation, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「憑據輪替」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「撤銷傳播」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around credential rotation, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat revocation propagation as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「憑據輪替」與「撤銷傳播」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for credential rotation and revocation propagation supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「憑據輪替」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for credential rotation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-23-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。","textEn":"Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-23-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「撤銷傳播」：離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「憑據輪替」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring revocation propagation: Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove credential rotation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-23-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「憑據輪替」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of credential rotation?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「撤銷傳播」，便可取代「憑據輪替」的專屬驗證。","更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking revocation propagation alone replaces verification specific to credential rotation.","Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。 相鄰的「撤銷傳播」有不同責任：離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Neighboring revocation propagation has a different role: Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-23"],"title":"憑據輪替：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Credential rotation: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「憑據輪替」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For credential rotation, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「撤銷傳播」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from revocation propagation to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 比較「憑據輪替」與「撤銷傳播」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Compare whether evidence for credential rotation and revocation propagation supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「憑據輪替」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for credential rotation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-24-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。","textEn":"Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-24-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「撤銷傳播」：離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「憑據輪替」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring revocation propagation: Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove credential rotation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-24-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留算法，只改裝置可用時鐘品質。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix algorithms and vary device-clock quality. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「憑據輪替」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of credential rotation?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「撤銷傳播」，便可取代「憑據輪替」的專屬驗證。","更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking revocation propagation alone replaces verification specific to credential rotation.","Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更新需考慮離線裝置與雙版本過渡。 相鄰的「撤銷傳播」有不同責任：離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Renewal considers offline devices and dual-version transitions. Neighboring revocation propagation has a different role: Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a365-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"效能、復原與證據交接","titleEn":"Performance, recovery and evidence handoff","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a365-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-24"],"title":"撤銷傳播：架構與原理","titleEn":"Revocation propagation: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「撤銷傳播」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For revocation propagation, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「撤銷傳播」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「裝置群峰值」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around revocation propagation, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat fleet bursts as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「撤銷傳播」與「裝置群峰值」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for revocation propagation and fleet bursts supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「撤銷傳播」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for revocation propagation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-25-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。","textEn":"Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-25-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「裝置群峰值」：集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「撤銷傳播」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring fleet bursts: Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove revocation propagation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-25-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「撤銷傳播」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of revocation propagation?","options":["離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。","所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「裝置群峰值」，便可取代「撤銷傳播」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data.","One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking fleet bursts alone replaces verification specific to revocation propagation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。 相鄰的「裝置群峰值」有不同責任：集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Neighboring fleet bursts has a different role: Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-25"],"title":"撤銷傳播：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Revocation propagation: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「撤銷傳播」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For revocation propagation, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「裝置群峰值」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from fleet bursts to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「撤銷傳播」與「裝置群峰值」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for revocation propagation and fleet bursts supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「撤銷傳播」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for revocation propagation. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-26-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。","textEn":"Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-26-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「裝置群峰值」：集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「撤銷傳播」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring fleet bursts: Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove revocation propagation passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-26-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「撤銷傳播」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of revocation propagation?","options":["離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。","所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「裝置群峰值」，便可取代「撤銷傳播」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data.","One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking fleet bursts alone replaces verification specific to revocation propagation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"離線狀態會延後裝置取得撤銷資訊。 相鄰的「裝置群峰值」有不同責任：集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Offline states delay device receipt of revocation data. Neighboring fleet bursts has a different role: Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-26"],"title":"裝置群峰值：架構與原理","titleEn":"Fleet bursts: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「裝置群峰值」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For fleet bursts, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「裝置群峰值」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「退役處置」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around fleet bursts, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat decommissioning as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「裝置群峰值」與「退役處置」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for fleet bursts and decommissioning supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「裝置群峰值」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for fleet bursts. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-27-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。","textEn":"Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-27-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「退役處置」：轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「裝置群峰值」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring decommissioning: Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove fleet bursts passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-27-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「裝置群峰值」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of fleet bursts?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。","只檢查「退役處置」，便可取代「裝置群峰值」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load.","Checking decommissioning alone replaces verification specific to fleet bursts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。 相鄰的「退役處置」有不同責任：轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Neighboring decommissioning has a different role: Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-27"],"title":"裝置群峰值：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Fleet bursts: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「裝置群峰值」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For fleet bursts, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「退役處置」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from decommissioning to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「裝置群峰值」與「退役處置」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for fleet bursts and decommissioning supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「裝置群峰值」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for fleet bursts. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-28-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。","textEn":"Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-28-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「退役處置」：轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「裝置群峰值」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring decommissioning: Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove fleet bursts passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-28-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「裝置群峰值」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of fleet bursts?","options":["遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。","只檢查「退役處置」，便可取代「裝置群峰值」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load.","Checking decommissioning alone replaces verification specific to fleet bursts."],"answer":1,"explanation":"集中開機造成驗證尖峰而非平均負載。 相鄰的「退役處置」有不同責任：轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Synchronized boot creates authentication bursts, not average load. Neighboring decommissioning has a different role: Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-28"],"title":"退役處置：架構與原理","titleEn":"Decommissioning: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「退役處置」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For decommissioning, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「退役處置」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「證據驗收」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around decommissioning, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat evidence acceptance as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「退役處置」與「證據驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for decommissioning and evidence acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「退役處置」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for decommissioning. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-29-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。","textEn":"Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-29-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「證據驗收」：唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「退役處置」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring evidence acceptance: Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove decommissioning passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-29-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「退役處置」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of decommissioning?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「證據驗收」，便可取代「退役處置」的專屬驗證。","轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking evidence acceptance alone replaces verification specific to decommissioning.","Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。 相鄰的「證據驗收」有不同責任：唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Neighboring evidence acceptance has a different role: Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-29"],"title":"退役處置：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Decommissioning: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「退役處置」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For decommissioning, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「證據驗收」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from evidence acceptance to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「退役處置」與「證據驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for decommissioning and evidence acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「退役處置」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for decommissioning. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-30-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。","textEn":"Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-30-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「證據驗收」：唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「退役處置」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring evidence acceptance: Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove decommissioning passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-30-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「退役處置」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of decommissioning?","options":["所有裝置共用一把秘密最容易稽核且無風險。","只檢查「證據驗收」，便可取代「退役處置」的專屬驗證。","轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。"],"optionsEn":["One shared fleet secret is easily audited and risk-free.","Checking evidence acceptance alone replaces verification specific to decommissioning.","Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"轉移所有權需移除舊秘密與綁定。 相鄰的「證據驗收」有不同責任：唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Ownership transfer removes old secrets/bindings. Neighboring evidence acceptance has a different role: Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-30"],"title":"證據驗收：架構與原理","titleEn":"Evidence acceptance: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「證據驗收」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For evidence acceptance, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「證據驗收」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「裝置識別」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around evidence acceptance, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat device identifiers as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「證據驗收」與「裝置識別」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for evidence acceptance and device identifiers supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「證據驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for evidence acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-31-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。","textEn":"Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-31-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「裝置識別」：序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「證據驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring device identifiers: Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove evidence acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-31-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-31-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 裝置各每日驗證一次，平均 1.1574 次/s；若全於 10 min 內集中，為 166.67 次/s，平均流量不足以規劃驗證尖峰。","textEn":"100000 devices authenticating once/day average 1.1574/s; concentrating them into 10 minutes gives 166.67/s, so averages do not size authentication peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「證據驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of evidence acceptance?","options":["唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。","遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「裝置識別」，便可取代「證據驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery.","Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking device identifiers alone replaces verification specific to evidence acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。 相鄰的「裝置識別」有不同責任：序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Neighboring device identifiers has a different role: Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a365-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"prerequisiteIds":["a365-v11-31"],"title":"證據驗收：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Evidence acceptance: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「證據驗收」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For evidence acceptance, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「裝置識別」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from device identifiers to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 比較「證據驗收」與「裝置識別」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Compare whether evidence for evidence acceptance and device identifiers supports the same inference.","failure":"遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「證據驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for evidence acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a365-v11-32-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。","textEn":"Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-32-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「裝置識別」：序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「證據驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring device identifiers: Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove evidence acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-32-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬離線期間續期與受控恢復。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model renewal during offline periods and controlled recovery. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"]},{"id":"a365-v11-32-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想 100000 裝置各每日驗證一次，平均 1.1574 次/s；若全於 10 min 內集中，為 166.67 次/s，平均流量不足以規劃驗證尖峰。","textEn":"100000 devices authenticating once/day average 1.1574/s; concentrating them into 10 minutes gives 166.67/s, so averages do not size authentication peaks.","sourceIds":["v11b-identity","v11b-dtls","v11b-keys","v11b-rats"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「證據驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of evidence acceptance?","options":["唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。","遠端證明可直接取代所有應用授權。","只檢查「裝置識別」，便可取代「證據驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery.","Remote attestation directly replaces every application authorization.","Checking device identifiers alone replaces verification specific to evidence acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"唯一性、時效、拒絕與復原都須測試。 相鄰的「裝置識別」有不同責任：序號是識別，不一定提供密碼學驗證。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Test uniqueness, freshness, rejection and recovery. Neighboring device identifiers has a different role: Serial numbers identify devices but need not authenticate cryptographically. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]}],"scope":"公開原理的離線／本地合成資料工程教育。只使用自行生成資料或明確獲授權的測試環境；不提供真實目標掃描、漏洞利用、惡意程式、車輛／工控注入或實際射頻發射程序。數值為原創假設，非供應商保證或現場驗收標準。","scopeEn":"Offline/local synthetic-data engineering education from public principles. Use authored data or explicitly authorized test environments only. No real-target scanning, exploitation, malware, vehicle/OT injection or live RF procedures. Numerical cases are original assumptions, not supplier guarantees or field acceptance criteria.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想量化例與限制","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative case and limits","text":"假想 100000 裝置各每日驗證一次，平均 1.1574 次/s；若全於 10 min 內集中，為 166.67 次/s，平均流量不足以規劃驗證尖峰。","textEn":"100000 devices authenticating once/day average 1.1574/s; concentrating them into 10 minutes gives 166.67/s, so averages do not size authentication peaks.","assumptions":"只採算例中明列的教學條件；效能與安全估計須依拓撲、分布、開銷、版本與不確定度重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use only the stated teaching assumptions; recalculate for topology, distribution, overhead, versions and uncertainty.","sourceScope":"作者自行設定的教學數值；官方來源支援原理與尺寸規格，未聲稱量測此假想平台。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen teaching inputs; official sources support principles and specified material sizes, not measurements of this hypothetical platform."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["裝置識別","秘密儲存","新鮮挑戰","撤銷傳播"],"labelsEn":["Device identifiers","Secret storage","Fresh challenges","Revocation propagation"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a366","title":"車用網路安全監測","titleEn":"Vehicle-network security monitoring","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以車載訊息、被動觀測與安全責任串連 16 個領域技術單元、32 個保存步驟；分析架構、原理、介面、故障、量化案例與防禦證據。","summaryEn":"Sixteen domain-specific technical units and 32 saved steps connect vehicle messages, passive observation and safety responsibility through architecture, principles, interfaces, faults, quantitative cases and defensive evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":11,"depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a366-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求、元件與基本模型","titleEn":"Requirements, components and baseline models","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a366-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"車載功能圖：架構與原理","titleEn":"Vehicle function maps: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「車載功能圖」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For vehicle function maps, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「車載功能圖」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「訊息識別」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around vehicle function maps, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat message identifiers as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「車載功能圖」與「訊息識別」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for vehicle function maps and message identifiers supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「車載功能圖」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for vehicle function maps. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-01-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。","textEn":"Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-01-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「訊息識別」：訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「車載功能圖」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring message identifiers: Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove vehicle function maps passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-01-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-01-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想每秒 5000 訊框、每框平均含 160 bit（含教學開銷假設），在 1 Mbit/s 匯流排佔 80%；這不是所有 CAN 訊框長度，實際 bit stuffing 與仲裁需另計。","textEn":"Assume 5000 frames/s at 160 bits/frame including teaching overhead: load on 1 Mbit/s bus=80%; actual CAN frame lengths, stuffing and arbitration need separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「車載功能圖」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of vehicle function maps?","options":["動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。","看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「訊息識別」，便可取代「車載功能圖」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines.","A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking message identifiers alone replaces verification specific to vehicle function maps."],"answer":0,"explanation":"動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。 相鄰的「訊息識別」有不同責任：訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Neighboring message identifiers has a different role: Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-01"],"title":"車載功能圖：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Vehicle function maps: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「車載功能圖」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For vehicle function maps, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「訊息識別」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from message identifiers to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「車載功能圖」與「訊息識別」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for vehicle function maps and message identifiers supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「車載功能圖」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for vehicle function maps. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-02-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。","textEn":"Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-02-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「訊息識別」：訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「車載功能圖」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring message identifiers: Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove vehicle function maps passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-02-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-02-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想每秒 5000 訊框、每框平均含 160 bit（含教學開銷假設），在 1 Mbit/s 匯流排佔 80%；這不是所有 CAN 訊框長度，實際 bit stuffing 與仲裁需另計。","textEn":"Assume 5000 frames/s at 160 bits/frame including teaching overhead: load on 1 Mbit/s bus=80%; actual CAN frame lengths, stuffing and arbitration need separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「車載功能圖」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of vehicle function maps?","options":["動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。","看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「訊息識別」，便可取代「車載功能圖」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines.","A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking message identifiers alone replaces verification specific to vehicle function maps."],"answer":0,"explanation":"動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。 相鄰的「訊息識別」有不同責任：訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Neighboring message identifiers has a different role: Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-02"],"title":"訊息識別：架構與原理","titleEn":"Message identifiers: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「訊息識別」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For message identifiers, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「訊息識別」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「仲裁與優先」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around message identifiers, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat arbitration and priority as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「訊息識別」與「仲裁與優先」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for message identifiers and arbitration and priority supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「訊息識別」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for message identifiers. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-03-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。","textEn":"Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-03-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「仲裁與優先」：優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「訊息識別」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring arbitration and priority: Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove message identifiers passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-03-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「訊息識別」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of message identifiers?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。","只檢查「仲裁與優先」，便可取代「訊息識別」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders.","Checking arbitration and priority alone replaces verification specific to message identifiers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。 相鄰的「仲裁與優先」有不同責任：優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Neighboring arbitration and priority has a different role: Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-03"],"title":"訊息識別：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Message identifiers: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「訊息識別」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For message identifiers, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「仲裁與優先」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from arbitration and priority to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「訊息識別」與「仲裁與優先」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for message identifiers and arbitration and priority supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「訊息識別」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for message identifiers. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-04-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。","textEn":"Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-04-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「仲裁與優先」：優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「訊息識別」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring arbitration and priority: Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove message identifiers passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-04-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「訊息識別」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of message identifiers?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。","只檢查「仲裁與優先」，便可取代「訊息識別」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders.","Checking arbitration and priority alone replaces verification specific to message identifiers."],"answer":1,"explanation":"訊息 ID 通常表示類別而非密碼學發送身分。 相鄰的「仲裁與優先」有不同責任：優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Message IDs usually identify message classes, not cryptographic senders. Neighboring arbitration and priority has a different role: Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-04"],"title":"仲裁與優先：架構與原理","titleEn":"Arbitration and priority: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「仲裁與優先」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For arbitration and priority, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「仲裁與優先」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「匯流排負載」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around arbitration and priority, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat bus load as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「仲裁與優先」與「匯流排負載」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for arbitration and priority and bus load supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「仲裁與優先」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for arbitration and priority. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-05-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。","textEn":"Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-05-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「匯流排負載」：負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「仲裁與優先」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring bus load: Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove arbitration and priority passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-05-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「仲裁與優先」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of arbitration and priority?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「匯流排負載」，便可取代「仲裁與優先」的專屬驗證。","優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking bus load alone replaces verification specific to arbitration and priority.","Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization."],"answer":2,"explanation":"優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。 相鄰的「匯流排負載」有不同責任：負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization. Neighboring bus load has a different role: Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-05"],"title":"仲裁與優先：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Arbitration and priority: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「仲裁與優先」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For arbitration and priority, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「匯流排負載」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from bus load to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「仲裁與優先」與「匯流排負載」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for arbitration and priority and bus load supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「仲裁與優先」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for arbitration and priority. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-06-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"優先規則影響等待，不等於身份授權。","textEn":"Priority affects waiting, not identity authorization.","sour