l.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「匯流排負載」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「週期基線」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around bus load, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat periodic baselines as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「匯流排負載」與「週期基線」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for bus load and periodic baselines supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「匯流排負載」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for bus load. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-07-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。","textEn":"Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-07-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「週期基線」：正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「匯流排負載」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring periodic baselines: Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove bus load passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-07-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「匯流排負載」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of bus load?","options":["負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。","資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「週期基線」，便可取代「匯流排負載」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead.","Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking periodic baselines alone replaces verification specific to bus load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。 相鄰的「週期基線」有不同責任：正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead. Neighboring periodic baselines has a different role: Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-07"],"title":"匯流排負載：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Bus load: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「匯流排負載」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For bus load, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「週期基線」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from periodic baselines to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 比較「匯流排負載」與「週期基線」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Compare whether evidence for bus load and periodic baselines supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「匯流排負載」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for bus load. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-08-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。","textEn":"Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-08-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「週期基線」：正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「匯流排負載」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring periodic baselines: Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove bus load passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-08-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定訊框，只改時間間隔模式。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix frames and vary interarrival patterns. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「匯流排負載」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of bus load?","options":["負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。","資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「週期基線」，便可取代「匯流排負載」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead.","Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking periodic baselines alone replaces verification specific to bus load."],"answer":0,"explanation":"負載估計需含訊框與協議開銷。 相鄰的「週期基線」有不同責任：正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Load estimates include frames and protocol overhead. Neighboring periodic baselines has a different role: Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a366-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"介面、狀態與資源配置","titleEn":"Interfaces, states and resource allocation","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a366-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-08"],"title":"週期基線：架構與原理","titleEn":"Periodic baselines: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「週期基線」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For periodic baselines, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「週期基線」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「數值範圍」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around periodic baselines, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat value ranges as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 比較「週期基線」與「數值範圍」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Compare whether evidence for periodic baselines and value ranges supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「週期基線」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for periodic baselines. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-09-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。","textEn":"Normal periods change with driving/operational modes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-09-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「數值範圍」：超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「週期基線」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring value ranges: Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove periodic baselines passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-09-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「週期基線」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of periodic baselines?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。","只檢查「數值範圍」，便可取代「週期基線」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Normal periods change with driving/operational modes.","Checking value ranges alone replaces verification specific to periodic baselines."],"answer":1,"explanation":"正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。 相鄰的「數值範圍」有不同責任：超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Neighboring value ranges has a different role: Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-09"],"title":"週期基線：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Periodic baselines: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「週期基線」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For periodic baselines, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「數值範圍」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from value ranges to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 比較「週期基線」與「數值範圍」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Compare whether evidence for periodic baselines and value ranges supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「週期基線」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for periodic baselines. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-10-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。","textEn":"Normal periods change with driving/operational modes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-10-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「數值範圍」：超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「週期基線」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring value ranges: Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove periodic baselines passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-10-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「週期基線」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of periodic baselines?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。","只檢查「數值範圍」，便可取代「週期基線」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Normal periods change with driving/operational modes.","Checking value ranges alone replaces verification specific to periodic baselines."],"answer":1,"explanation":"正常週期會隨驾驶與模式變化。 相鄰的「數值範圍」有不同責任：超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Normal periods change with driving/operational modes. Neighboring value ranges has a different role: Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-10"],"title":"數值範圍：架構與原理","titleEn":"Value ranges: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「數值範圍」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For value ranges, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「數值範圍」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「跨信號關系」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around value ranges, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat cross-signal relations as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 比較「數值範圍」與「跨信號關系」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Compare whether evidence for value ranges and cross-signal relations supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「數值範圍」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for value ranges. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-11-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。","textEn":"Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-11-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「跨信號關系」：相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「數值範圍」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring cross-signal relations: Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove value ranges passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-11-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「數值範圍」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of value ranges?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「跨信號關系」，便可取代「數值範圍」的專屬驗證。","超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking cross-signal relations alone replaces verification specific to value ranges.","Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。 相鄰的「跨信號關系」有不同責任：相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Neighboring cross-signal relations has a different role: Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-11"],"title":"數值範圍：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Value ranges: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「數值範圍」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For value ranges, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「跨信號關系」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from cross-signal relations to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 比較「數值範圍」與「跨信號關系」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Compare whether evidence for value ranges and cross-signal relations supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「數值範圍」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for value ranges. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-12-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。","textEn":"Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-12-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「跨信號關系」：相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「數值範圍」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring cross-signal relations: Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove value ranges passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-12-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「數值範圍」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of value ranges?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「跨信號關系」，便可取代「數值範圍」的專屬驗證。","超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking cross-signal relations alone replaces verification specific to value ranges.","Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"超範圍與不合物理變化率是不同證據。 相鄰的「跨信號關系」有不同責任：相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Out-of-range values differ from implausible change rates. Neighboring cross-signal relations has a different role: Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-12"],"title":"跨信號關系：架構與原理","titleEn":"Cross-signal relations: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「跨信號關系」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For cross-signal relations, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「跨信號關系」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「閘道邊界」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around cross-signal relations, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat gateway boundaries as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 比較「跨信號關系」與「閘道邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Compare whether evidence for cross-signal relations and gateway boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「跨信號關系」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for cross-signal relations. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-13-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。","textEn":"Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-13-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「閘道邊界」：跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「跨信號關系」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring gateway boundaries: Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove cross-signal relations passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-13-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「跨信號關系」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of cross-signal relations?","options":["相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。","看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「閘道邊界」，便可取代「跨信號關系」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear.","A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking gateway boundaries alone replaces verification specific to cross-signal relations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。 相鄰的「閘道邊界」有不同責任：跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear. Neighboring gateway boundaries has a different role: Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-13"],"title":"跨信號關系：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Cross-signal relations: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「跨信號關系」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For cross-signal relations, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertai