":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「閘道邊界」：跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「跨信號關系」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring gateway boundaries: Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove cross-signal relations passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-14-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「跨信號關系」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of cross-signal relations?","options":["相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。","看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「閘道邊界」，便可取代「跨信號關系」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear.","A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking gateway boundaries alone replaces verification specific to cross-signal relations."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相關訊號可互證但不能假定永久線性。 相鄰的「閘道邊界」有不同責任：跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Related signals corroborate but need not be permanently linear. Neighboring gateway boundaries has a different role: Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-14"],"title":"閘道邊界：架構與原理","titleEn":"Gateway boundaries: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「閘道邊界」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For gateway boundaries, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「閘道邊界」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「診斷權限」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around gateway boundaries, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat diagnostic permissions as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 比較「閘道邊界」與「診斷權限」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Compare whether evidence for gateway boundaries and diagnostic permissions supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「閘道邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for gateway boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-15-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。","textEn":"Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-15-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「診斷權限」：診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「閘道邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring diagnostic permissions: Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove gateway boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-15-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-15-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想每秒 5000 訊框、每框平均含 160 bit（含教學開銷假設），在 1 Mbit/s 匯流排佔 80%；這不是所有 CAN 訊框長度，實際 bit stuffing 與仲裁需另計。","textEn":"Assume 5000 frames/s at 160 bits/frame including teaching overhead: load on 1 Mbit/s bus=80%; actual CAN frame lengths, stuffing and arbitration need separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「閘道邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of gateway boundaries?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。","只檢查「診斷權限」，便可取代「閘道邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles.","Checking diagnostic permissions alone replaces verification specific to gateway boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。 相鄰的「診斷權限」有不同責任：診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Neighboring diagnostic permissions has a different role: Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-15"],"title":"閘道邊界：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Gateway boundaries: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「閘道邊界」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For gateway boundaries, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「診斷權限」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from diagnostic permissions to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 比較「閘道邊界」與「診斷權限」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Compare whether evidence for gateway boundaries and diagnostic permissions supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「閘道邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for gateway boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-16-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。","textEn":"Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-16-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「診斷權限」：診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「閘道邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring diagnostic permissions: Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove gateway boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-16-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較正常診斷與未批准診斷的合成事件。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare authorized/unauthorized synthetic diagnostic events. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-16-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想每秒 5000 訊框、每框平均含 160 bit（含教學開銷假設），在 1 Mbit/s 匯流排佔 80%；這不是所有 CAN 訊框長度，實際 bit stuffing 與仲裁需另計。","textEn":"Assume 5000 frames/s at 160 bits/frame including teaching overhead: load on 1 Mbit/s bus=80%; actual CAN frame lengths, stuffing and arbitration need separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「閘道邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of gateway boundaries?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。","只檢查「診斷權限」，便可取代「閘道邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles.","Checking diagnostic permissions alone replaces verification specific to gateway boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"跨域閘道應限制可轉送訊息與角色。 相鄰的「診斷權限」有不同責任：診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Domain gateways constrain forwarded messages/roles. Neighboring diagnostic permissions has a different role: Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a366-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"驗證、故障與防禦邊界","titleEn":"Validation, faults and defensive boundaries","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a366-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-16"],"title":"診斷權限：架構與原理","titleEn":"Diagnostic permissions: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「診斷權限」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For diagnostic permissions, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「診斷權限」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「OTA 完整性」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around diagnostic permissions, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary bus load. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat ota integrity as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「診斷權限」與「OTA 完整性」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for diagnostic permissions and ota integrity supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「診斷權限」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for diagnostic permissions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-17-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。","textEn":"Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-17-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「OTA 完整性」：更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「診斷權限」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring ota integrity: Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove diagnostic permissions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-17-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「診斷權限」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of diagnostic permissions?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「OTA 完整性」，便可取代「診斷權限」的專屬驗證。","診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking ota integrity alone replaces verification specific to diagnostic permissions.","Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。 相鄰的「OTA 完整性」有不同責任：更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Neighboring ota integrity has a different role: Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-17"],"title":"診斷權限：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Diagnostic permissions: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「診斷權限」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For diagnostic permissions, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「OTA 完整性」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary bus load. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from ota integrity to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「診斷權限」與「OTA 完整性」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for diagnostic permissions and ota integrity supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「診斷權限」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for diagnostic permissions. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-18-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。","textEn":"Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-18-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「OTA 完整性」：更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「診斷權限」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring ota integrity: Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove diagnostic permissions passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-18-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「診斷權限」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of diagnostic permissions?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「OTA 完整性」，便可取代「診斷權限」的專屬驗證。","診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking ota integrity alone replaces verification specific to diagnostic permissions.","Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints."],"answer":2,"explanation":"診斷服務有授權、時限與狀態要求。 相鄰的「OTA 完整性」有不同責任：更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Diagnostics need authorization, timing and state constraints. Neighboring ota integrity has a different role: Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-18"],"title":"OTA 完整性：架構與原理","titleEn":"OTA integrity: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「OTA 完整性」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For ota integrity, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「OTA 完整性」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「記錄與隱私」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around ota integrity, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary bus load. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat logs and privacy as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「OTA 完整性」與「記錄與隱私」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for ota integrity and logs and privacy supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「OTA 完整性」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for ota integrity. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-19-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。","textEn":"Update origin/version verification differs from download success.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-19-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「記錄與隱私」：行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「OTA 完整性」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring logs and privacy: Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove ota integrity passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-19-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「OTA 完整性」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of ota integrity?","options":["更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。","資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「記錄與隱私」，便可取代「OTA 完整性」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Update origin/version verification differs from download success.","Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking logs and privacy alone replaces verification specific to ota integrity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。 相鄰的「記錄與隱私」有不同責任：行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Neighboring logs and privacy has a different role: Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-19"],"title":"OTA 完整性：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"OTA integrity: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「OTA 完整性」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For ota integrity, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「記錄與隱私」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary bus load. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from logs and privacy to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「OTA 完整性」與「記錄與隱私」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for ota integrity and logs and privacy supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「OTA 完整性」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for ota integrity. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-20-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。","textEn":"Update origin/version verification differs from download success.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-20-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「記錄與隱私」：行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「OTA 完整性」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring logs and privacy: Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove ota integrity passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-20-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「OTA 完整性」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of ota integrity?","options":["更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。","資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「記錄與隱私」，便可取代「OTA 完整性」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Update origin/version verification differs from download success.","Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking logs and privacy alone replaces verification specific to ota integrity."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更新來源與版本驗證不同於下載成功。 相鄰的「記錄與隱私」有不同責任：行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Update origin/version verification differs from download success. Neighboring logs and privacy has a different role: Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-20"],"title":"記錄與隱私：架構與原理","titleEn":"Logs and privacy: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「記錄與隱私」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For logs and privacy, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「記錄與隱私」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「告警延遲」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around logs and privacy, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary bus load. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat alert latency as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「記錄與隱私」與「告警延遲」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for logs and privacy and alert latency supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「記錄與隱私」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for logs and privacy. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-21-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。","textEn":"Minimize and control access to journey/identity data.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-21-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「告警延遲」：告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「記錄與隱私」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring alert latency: Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove logs and privacy passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-21-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「記錄與隱私」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of logs and privacy?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。","只檢查「告警延遲」，便可取代「記錄與隱私」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Minimize and control access to journey/identity data.","Checking alert latency alone replaces verification specific to logs and privacy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。 相鄰的「告警延遲」有不同責任：告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Neighboring alert latency has a different role: Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-21"],"title":"記錄與隱私：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Logs and privacy: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「記錄與隱私」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For logs and privacy, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「告警延遲」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary bus load. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from alert latency to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「記錄與隱私」與「告警延遲」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for logs and privacy and alert latency supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「記錄與隱私」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for logs and privacy. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-22-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。","textEn":"Minimize and control access to journey/identity data.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-22-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「告警延遲」：告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「記錄與隱私」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring alert latency: Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove logs and privacy passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-22-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「記錄與隱私」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of logs and privacy?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。","只檢查「告警延遲」，便可取代「記錄與隱私」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Minimize and control access to journey/identity data.","Checking alert latency alone replaces verification specific to logs and privacy."],"answer":1,"explanation":"行程與識別資料需最小化與受控存取。 相鄰的「告警延遲」有不同責任：告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Minimize and control access to journey/identity data. Neighboring alert latency has a different role: Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-22"],"title":"告警延遲：架構與原理","titleEn":"Alert latency: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「告警延遲」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For alert latency, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「告警延遲」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「誤報處置」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around alert latency, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix rules and vary bus load. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat false-alert handling as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「告警延遲」與「誤報處置」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for alert latency and false-alert handling supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「告警延遲」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for alert latency. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-23-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。","textEn":"Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-23-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「誤報處置」：錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「告警延遲」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring false-alert handling: False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove alert latency passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-23-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「告警延遲」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of alert latency?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「誤報處置」，便可取代「告警延遲」的專屬驗證。","告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking false-alert handling alone replaces verification specific to alert latency.","Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。 相鄰的「誤報處置」有不同責任：錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Neighboring false-alert handling has a different role: False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-23"],"title":"告警延遲：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Alert latency: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「告警延遲」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For alert latency, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「誤報處置」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix rules and vary bus load. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from false-alert handling to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 比較「告警延遲」與「誤報處置」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Compare whether evidence for alert latency and false-alert handling supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「告警延遲」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for alert latency. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-24-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。","textEn":"Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-24-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「誤報處置」：錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「告警延遲」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring false-alert handling: False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove alert latency passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-24-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留規則，只改匯流排負載。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix rules and vary bus load. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「告警延遲」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of alert latency?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「誤報處置」，便可取代「告警延遲」的專屬驗證。","告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking false-alert handling alone replaces verification specific to alert latency.","Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"告警延遲應低於情境需要而非只看平均。 相鄰的「誤報處置」有不同責任：錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Alert delay should satisfy context, not only average performance. Neighboring false-alert handling has a different role: False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a366-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"效能、復原與證據交接","titleEn":"Performance, recovery and evidence handoff","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a366-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-24"],"title":"誤報處置：架構與原理","titleEn":"False-alert handling: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「誤報處置」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For false-alert handling, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「誤報處置」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「安全責任」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around false-alert handling, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat safety responsibilities as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「誤報處置」與「安全責任」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for false-alert handling and safety responsibilities supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「誤報處置」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for false-alert handling. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-25-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。","textEn":"False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-25-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「安全責任」：資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「誤報處置」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring safety responsibilities: Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove false-alert handling passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-25-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「誤報處置」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of false-alert handling?","options":["錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。","看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「安全責任」，便可取代「誤報處置」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally.","A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking safety responsibilities alone replaces verification specific to false-alert handling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。 相鄰的「安全責任」有不同責任：資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Neighboring safety responsibilities has a different role: Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-25"],"title":"誤報處置：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"False-alert handling: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「誤報處置」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For false-alert handling, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「安全責任」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from safety responsibilities to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「誤報處置」與「安全責任」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for false-alert handling and safety responsibilities supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「誤報處置」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for false-alert handling. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-26-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。","textEn":"False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-26-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「安全責任」：資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「誤報處置」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring safety responsibilities: Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove false-alert handling passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-26-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「誤報處置」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of false-alert handling?","options":["錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。","看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「安全責任」，便可取代「誤報處置」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally.","A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking safety responsibilities alone replaces verification specific to false-alert handling."],"answer":0,"explanation":"錯誤阻斷可能影響安全，回應須经設計審查。 相鄰的「安全責任」有不同責任：資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"False blocking can affect safety; review responses formally. Neighboring safety responsibilities has a different role: Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-26"],"title":"安全責任：架構與原理","titleEn":"Safety responsibilities: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「安全責任」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For safety responsibilities, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「安全責任」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「管理系統」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around safety responsibilities, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat management systems as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「安全責任」與「管理系統」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for safety responsibilities and management systems supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「安全責任」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for safety responsibilities. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-27-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。","textEn":"Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-27-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「管理系統」：R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「安全責任」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring management systems: R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove safety responsibilities passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-27-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「安全責任」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of safety responsibilities?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。","只檢查「管理系統」，便可取代「安全責任」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other.","Checking management systems alone replaces verification specific to safety responsibilities."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。 相鄰的「管理系統」有不同責任：R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Neighboring management systems has a different role: R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-27"],"title":"安全責任：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Safety responsibilities: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「安全責任」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For safety responsibilities, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「管理系統」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from management systems to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「安全責任」與「管理系統」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for safety responsibilities and management systems supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「安全責任」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for safety responsibilities. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-28-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。","textEn":"Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-28-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「管理系統」：R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「安全責任」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring management systems: R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove safety responsibilities passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-28-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「安全責任」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of safety responsibilities?","options":["資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。","只檢查「管理系統」，便可取代「安全責任」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other.","Checking management systems alone replaces verification specific to safety responsibilities."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資安與功能安全交互但不能互相替代。 相鄰的「管理系統」有不同責任：R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Cybersecurity and functional safety interact without replacing each other. Neighboring management systems has a different role: R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-28"],"title":"管理系統：架構與原理","titleEn":"Management systems: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「管理系統」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For management systems, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「管理系統」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「合成驗收」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around management systems, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat synthetic acceptance as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「管理系統」與「合成驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for management systems and synthetic acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「管理系統」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for management systems. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-29-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。","textEn":"R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-29-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「合成驗收」：本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「管理系統」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring synthetic acceptance: This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove management systems passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-29-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「管理系統」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of management systems?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「合成驗收」，便可取代「管理系統」的專屬驗證。","R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking synthetic acceptance alone replaces verification specific to management systems.","R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。 相鄰的「合成驗收」有不同責任：本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Neighboring synthetic acceptance has a different role: This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-29"],"title":"管理系統：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Management systems: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「管理系統」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For management systems, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「合成驗收」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from synthetic acceptance to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「管理系統」與「合成驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for management systems and synthetic acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「管理系統」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for management systems. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-30-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。","textEn":"R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-30-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「合成驗收」：本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「管理系統」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring synthetic acceptance: This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove management systems passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-30-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「管理系統」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of management systems?","options":["看到 CAN ID 就能證明發送裝置身分。","只檢查「合成驗收」，便可取代「管理系統」的專屬驗證。","R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。"],"optionsEn":["A CAN ID proves the transmitting device identity.","Checking synthetic acceptance alone replaces verification specific to management systems.","R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification."],"answer":2,"explanation":"R155 管理要求不是單一感測器產品规格。 相鄰的「合成驗收」有不同責任：本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"R155 management requirements are not a single-sensor specification. Neighboring synthetic acceptance has a different role: This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-30"],"title":"合成驗收：架構與原理","titleEn":"Synthetic acceptance: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「合成驗收」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For synthetic acceptance, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「合成驗收」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「車載功能圖」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around synthetic acceptance, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat vehicle function maps as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「合成驗收」與「車載功能圖」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for synthetic acceptance and vehicle function maps supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「合成驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for synthetic acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-31-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。","textEn":"This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-31-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「車載功能圖」：動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「合成驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring vehicle function maps: Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove synthetic acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-31-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-31-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想每秒 5000 訊框、每框平均含 160 bit（含教學開銷假設），在 1 Mbit/s 匯流排佔 80%；這不是所有 CAN 訊框長度，實際 bit stuffing 與仲裁需另計。","textEn":"Assume 5000 frames/s at 160 bits/frame including teaching overhead: load on 1 Mbit/s bus=80%; actual CAN frame lengths, stuffing and arbitration need separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「合成驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of synthetic acceptance?","options":["本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。","資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「車載功能圖」，便可取代「合成驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles.","Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking vehicle function maps alone replaces verification specific to synthetic acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。 相鄰的「車載功能圖」有不同責任：動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Neighboring vehicle function maps has a different role: Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a366-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"prerequisiteIds":["a366-v11-31"],"title":"合成驗收：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Synthetic acceptance: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「合成驗收」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For synthetic acceptance, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「車載功能圖」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from vehicle function maps to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 比較「合成驗收」與「車載功能圖」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Compare whether evidence for synthetic acceptance and vehicle function maps supports the same inference.","failure":"資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「合成驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for synthetic acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a366-v11-32-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。","textEn":"This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-32-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「車載功能圖」：動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「合成驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring vehicle function maps: Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove synthetic acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-32-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬監測器失效對告警覆蓋的影響。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model monitor failure and alert-coverage effects. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"]},{"id":"a366-v11-32-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想每秒 5000 訊框、每框平均含 160 bit（含教學開銷假設），在 1 Mbit/s 匯流排佔 80%；這不是所有 CAN 訊框長度，實際 bit stuffing 與仲裁需另計。","textEn":"Assume 5000 frames/s at 160 bits/frame including teaching overhead: load on 1 Mbit/s bus=80%; actual CAN frame lengths, stuffing and arbitration need separate treatment.","sourceIds":["v11b-vehicle","v11b-r155","v11b-logs"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「合成驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of synthetic acceptance?","options":["本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。","資安監測可取代全部功能安全驗證。","只檢查「車載功能圖」，便可取代「合成驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles.","Cybersecurity monitoring replaces all functional-safety validation.","Checking vehicle function maps alone replaces verification specific to synthetic acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"本課只分析自製記錄，不連接或注入真實車輛。 相鄰的「車載功能圖」有不同責任：動力、車身與資訊娛樂具不同風險與時限。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"This course analyzes authored records without connecting/injecting into vehicles. Neighboring vehicle function maps has a different role: Powertrain, body and infotainment have different risks/deadlines. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]}],"scope":"公開原理的離線／本地合成資料工程教育。只使用自行生成資料或明確獲授權的測試環境；不提供真實目標掃描、漏洞利用、惡意程式、車輛／工控注入或實際射頻發射程序。數值為原創假設，非供應商保證或現場驗收標準。","scopeEn":"Offline/local synthetic-data engineering education from public principles. Use authored data or explicitly authorized test environments only. No real-target scanning, exploitation, malware, vehicle/OT injection or live RF procedures. Numerical cases are original assumptions, not supplier guarantees or field acceptance criteria.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想量化例與限制","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative case and limits","text":"假想每秒 5000 訊框、每框平均含 160 bit（含教學開銷假設），在 1 Mbit/s 匯流排佔 80%；這不是所有 CAN 訊框長度，實際 bit stuffing 與仲裁需另計。","textEn":"Assume 5000 frames/s at 160 bits/frame including teaching overhead: load on 1 Mbit/s bus=80%; actual CAN frame lengths, stuffing and arbitration need separate treatment.","assumptions":"只採算例中明列的教學條件；效能與安全估計須依拓撲、分布、開銷、版本與不確定度重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use only the stated teaching assumptions; recalculate for topology, distribution, overhead, versions and uncertainty.","sourceScope":"作者自行設定的教學數值；官方來源支援原理與尺寸規格，未聲稱量測此假想平台。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen teaching inputs; official sources support principles and specified material sizes, not measurements of this hypothetical platform."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["車載功能圖","週期基線","診斷權限","誤報處置"],"labelsEn":["Vehicle function maps","Periodic baselines","Diagnostic permissions","False-alert handling"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a367","title":"機密運算與可信執行環境","titleEn":"Confidential computing and trusted execution environments","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以記憶體保護、遠端證明與秘密釋放串連 16 個領域技術單元、32 個保存步驟；分析架構、原理、介面、故障、量化案例與防禦證據。","summaryEn":"Sixteen domain-specific technical units and 32 saved steps connect memory protection, remote attestation and secret release through architecture, principles, interfaces, faults, quantitative cases and defensive evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","curriculumVersion":11,"depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a367-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"需求、元件與基本模型","titleEn":"Requirements, components and baseline models","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a367-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"威胁模型：架構與原理","titleEn":"Threat models: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「威胁模型」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For threat models, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「威胁模型」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「保護邊界」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around threat models, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat protection boundaries as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「威胁模型」與「保護邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for threat models and protection boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「威胁模型」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for threat models. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-01-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。","textEn":"Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-01-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「保護邊界」：保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「威胁模型」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring protection boundaries: Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove threat models passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-01-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-01-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想證明 15 ms、驗證 5 ms、秘密傳送 10 ms，串行初始化合 30 ms；若每秒 100 次初始作業且不可並行，每秒需 3 s 處理，單通道不足。","textEn":"Assumed attestation=15 ms, verification=5 ms and secret transfer=10 ms give 30 ms serial initialization; 100 starts/s require 3 processing-seconds/s, exceeding one serial channel.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「威胁模型」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of threat models?","options":["先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。","機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「保護邊界」，便可取代「威胁模型」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first.","Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking protection boundaries alone replaces verification specific to threat models."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。 相鄰的「保護邊界」有不同責任：保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Neighboring protection boundaries has a different role: Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-01"],"title":"威胁模型：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Threat models: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「威胁模型」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For threat models, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「保護邊界」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from protection boundaries to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「威胁模型」與「保護邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for threat models and protection boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「威胁模型」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for threat models. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-02-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。","textEn":"Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-02-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「保護邊界」：保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「威胁模型」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring protection boundaries: Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove threat models passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-02-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-02-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想證明 15 ms、驗證 5 ms、秘密傳送 10 ms，串行初始化合 30 ms；若每秒 100 次初始作業且不可並行，每秒需 3 s 處理，單通道不足。","textEn":"Assumed attestation=15 ms, verification=5 ms and secret transfer=10 ms give 30 ms serial initialization; 100 starts/s require 3 processing-seconds/s, exceeding one serial channel.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「威胁模型」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of threat models?","options":["先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。","機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「保護邊界」，便可取代「威胁模型」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first.","Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking protection boundaries alone replaces verification specific to threat models."],"answer":0,"explanation":"先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。 相鄰的「保護邊界」有不同責任：保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Neighboring protection boundaries has a different role: Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-02"],"title":"保護邊界：架構與原理","titleEn":"Protection boundaries: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「保護邊界」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For protection boundaries, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「保護邊界」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「記憶體加密」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around protection boundaries, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat memory encryption as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「保護邊界」與「記憶體加密」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for protection boundaries and memory encryption supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「保護邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for protection boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-03-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。","textEn":"Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-03-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「記憶體加密」：加密與完整性保護是不同性質。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「保護邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring memory encryption: Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove protection boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-03-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「保護邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of protection boundaries?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。","只檢查「記憶體加密」，便可取代「保護邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path.","Checking memory encryption alone replaces verification specific to protection boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。 相鄰的「記憶體加密」有不同責任：加密與完整性保護是不同性質。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Neighboring memory encryption has a different role: Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-03"],"title":"保護邊界：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Protection boundaries: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「保護邊界」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For protection boundaries, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「記憶體加密」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from memory encryption to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「保護邊界」與「記憶體加密」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for protection boundaries and memory encryption supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「保護邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for protection boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-04-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。","textEn":"Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-04-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「記憶體加密」：加密與完整性保護是不同性質。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「保護邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring memory encryption: Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove protection boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-04-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「保護邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of protection boundaries?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。","只檢查「記憶體加密」，便可取代「保護邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path.","Checking memory encryption alone replaces verification specific to protection boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護來宾記憶體不等於保護所有外部 I/O。 相鄰的「記憶體加密」有不同責任：加密與完整性保護是不同性質。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protecting guest memory does not protect every external I/O path. Neighboring memory encryption has a different role: Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-04"],"title":"記憶體加密：架構與原理","titleEn":"Memory encryption: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「記憶體加密」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For memory encryption, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「記憶體加密」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：加密與完整性保護是不同性質。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「受測工作負載」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around memory encryption, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat measured workloads as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「記憶體加密」與「受測工作負載」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for memory encryption and measured workloads supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「記憶體加密」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for memory encryption. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-05-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"加密與完整性保護是不同性質。","textEn":"Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-05-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「受測工作負載」：測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「記憶體加密」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring measured workloads: Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove memory encryption passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-05-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「記憶體加密」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of memory encryption?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「受測工作負載」，便可取代「記憶體加密」的專屬驗證。","加密與完整性保護是不同性質。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking measured workloads alone replaces verification specific to memory encryption.","Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties."],"answer":2,"explanation":"加密與完整性保護是不同性質。 相鄰的「受測工作負載」有不同責任：測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Neighboring measured workloads has a different role: Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-05"],"title":"記憶體加密：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Memory encryption: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「記憶體加密」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For memory encryption, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「加密與完整性保護是不同性質。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「受測工作負載」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from measured workloads to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「記憶體加密」與「受測工作負載」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for memory encryption and measured workloads supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「記憶體加密」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for memory encryption. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-06-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"加密與完整性保護是不同性質。","textEn":"Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-06-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「受測工作負載」：測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「記憶體加密」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring measured workloads: Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove memory encryption passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-06-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「記憶體加密」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of memory encryption?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「受測工作負載」，便可取代「記憶體加密」的專屬驗證。","加密與完整性保護是不同性質。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking measured workloads alone replaces verification specific to memory encryption.","Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties."],"answer":2,"explanation":"加密與完整性保護是不同性質。 相鄰的「受測工作負載」有不同責任：測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Encryption and integrity protection are distinct properties. Neighboring measured workloads has a different role: Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-06"],"title":"受測工作負載：架構與原理","titleEn":"Measured workloads: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「受測工作負載」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For measured workloads, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「受測工作負載」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「Attester」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around measured workloads, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat attesters as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「受測工作負載」與「Attester」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for measured workloads and attesters supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「受測工作負載」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for measured workloads. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-07-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。","textEn":"Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-07-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「Attester」：產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「受測工作負載」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring attesters: Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove measured workloads passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-07-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「受測工作負載」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of measured workloads?","options":["測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。","證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「Attester」，便可取代「受測工作負載」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations.","The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking attesters alone replaces verification specific to measured workloads."],"answer":0,"explanation":"測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。 相鄰的「Attester」有不同責任：產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Neighboring attesters has a different role: Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-07"],"title":"受測工作負載：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Measured workloads: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「受測工作負載」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For measured workloads, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「Attester」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from attesters to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 比較「受測工作負載」與「Attester」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Compare whether evidence for measured workloads and attesters supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「受測工作負載」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for measured workloads. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-08-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。","textEn":"Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-08-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「Attester」：產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「受測工作負載」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring attesters: Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove measured workloads passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-08-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"固定工作負載，只改預期測量值。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix workloads and vary expected measurements. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「受測工作負載」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of measured workloads?","options":["測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。","證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「Attester」，便可取代「受測工作負載」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations.","The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking attesters alone replaces verification specific to measured workloads."],"answer":0,"explanation":"測量值須代表可審查版本及配置。 相鄰的「Attester」有不同責任：產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Measurements represent reviewable versions/configurations. Neighboring attesters has a different role: Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a367-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"介面、狀態與資源配置","titleEn":"Interfaces, states and resource allocation","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a367-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-08"],"title":"Attester：架構與原理","titleEn":"Attesters: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「Attester」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For attesters, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「Attester」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「Verifier」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around attesters, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat verifiers as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「Attester」與「Verifier」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for attesters and verifiers supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「Attester」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for attesters. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-09-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。","textEn":"Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-09-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「Verifier」：驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「Attester」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring verifiers: Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove attesters passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-09-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「Attester」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of attesters?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。","只檢查「Verifier」，便可取代「Attester」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation.","Checking verifiers alone replaces verification specific to attesters."],"answer":1,"explanation":"產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。 相鄰的「Verifier」有不同責任：驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Neighboring verifiers has a different role: Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-09"],"title":"Attester：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Attesters: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「Attester」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For attesters, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「Verifier」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from verifiers to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「Attester」與「Verifier」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for attesters and verifiers supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「Attester」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for attesters. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-10-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。","textEn":"Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-10-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「Verifier」：驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「Attester」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring verifiers: Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove attesters passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-10-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「Attester」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of attesters?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。","只檢查「Verifier」，便可取代「Attester」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation.","Checking verifiers alone replaces verification specific to attesters."],"answer":1,"explanation":"產生證據的角色與判斷可信的角色不同。 相鄰的「Verifier」有不同責任：驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Evidence generation differs from trust evaluation. Neighboring verifiers has a different role: Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-10"],"title":"Verifier：架構與原理","titleEn":"Verifiers: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「Verifier」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For verifiers, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「Verifier」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「Relying party」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around verifiers, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat relying parties as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「Verifier」與「Relying party」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for verifiers and relying parties supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「Verifier」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for verifiers. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-11-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。","textEn":"Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-11-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「Relying party」：依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「Verifier」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring relying parties: Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove verifiers passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-11-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「Verifier」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of verifiers?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「Relying party」，便可取代「Verifier」的專屬驗證。","驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking relying parties alone replaces verification specific to verifiers.","Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。 相鄰的「Relying party」有不同責任：依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Neighboring relying parties has a different role: Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-11"],"title":"Verifier：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Verifiers: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「Verifier」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For verifiers, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「Relying party」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from relying parties to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「Verifier」與「Relying party」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for verifiers and relying parties supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「Verifier」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for verifiers. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-12-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。","textEn":"Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-12-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「Relying party」：依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「Verifier」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring relying parties: Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove verifiers passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-12-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「Verifier」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of verifiers?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「Relying party」，便可取代「Verifier」的專屬驗證。","驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking relying parties alone replaces verification specific to verifiers.","Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"驗證器依背書、參考值及策略評估證據。 相鄰的「Relying party」有不同責任：依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Verifiers assess evidence using endorsements, references and policy. Neighboring relying parties has a different role: Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-12"],"title":"Relying party：架構與原理","titleEn":"Relying parties: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「Relying party」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For relying parties, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「Relying party」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「新鮮性」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around relying parties, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat freshness as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「Relying party」與「新鮮性」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for relying parties and freshness supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「Relying party」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for relying parties. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-13-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。","textEn":"Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-13-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「新鮮性」：nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「Relying party」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring freshness: Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove relying parties passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-13-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「Relying party」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of relying parties?","options":["依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。","機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「新鮮性」，便可取代「Relying party」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization.","Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking freshness alone replaces verification specific to relying parties."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。 相鄰的「新鮮性」有不同責任：nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Neighboring freshness has a different role: Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-13"],"title":"Relying party：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Relying parties: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「Relying party」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For relying parties, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「新鮮性」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from freshness to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「Relying party」與「新鮮性」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for relying parties and freshness supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「Relying party」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for relying parties. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-14-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。","textEn":"Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-14-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「新鮮性」：nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「Relying party」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring freshness: Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove relying parties passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-14-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「Relying party」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of relying parties?","options":["依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。","機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「新鮮性」，便可取代「Relying party」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization.","Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking freshness alone replaces verification specific to relying parties."],"answer":0,"explanation":"依賴方使用驗證結果做具體授權。 相鄰的「新鮮性」有不同責任：nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Relying parties use appraisal results for concrete authorization. Neighboring freshness has a different role: Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-14"],"title":"新鮮性：架構與原理","titleEn":"Freshness: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「新鮮性」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For freshness, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「新鮮性」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「背書鏈」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around freshness, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat endorsement chains as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「新鮮性」與「背書鏈」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for freshness and endorsement chains supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「新鮮性」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for freshness. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-15-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。","textEn":"Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-15-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「背書鏈」：廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「新鮮性」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring endorsement chains: Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove freshness passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-15-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-15-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想證明 15 ms、驗證 5 ms、秘密傳送 10 ms，串行初始化合 30 ms；若每秒 100 次初始作業且不可並行，每秒需 3 s 處理，單通道不足。","textEn":"Assumed attestation=15 ms, verification=5 ms and secret transfer=10 ms give 30 ms serial initialization; 100 starts/s require 3 processing-seconds/s, exceeding one serial channel.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「新鮮性」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of freshness?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。","只檢查「背書鏈」，便可取代「新鮮性」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions.","Checking endorsement chains alone replaces verification specific to freshness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。 相鄰的「背書鏈」有不同責任：廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Neighboring endorsement chains has a different role: Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-15"],"title":"新鮮性：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Freshness: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「新鮮性」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For freshness, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「背書鏈」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from endorsement chains to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 比較「新鮮性」與「背書鏈」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Compare whether evidence for freshness and endorsement chains supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「新鮮性」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for freshness. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-16-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。","textEn":"Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-16-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「背書鏈」：廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「新鮮性」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring endorsement chains: Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove freshness passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-16-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"比較新鲜與重放的證明記錄。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Compare fresh/replayed attestation records. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-16-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想證明 15 ms、驗證 5 ms、秘密傳送 10 ms，串行初始化合 30 ms；若每秒 100 次初始作業且不可並行，每秒需 3 s 處理，單通道不足。","textEn":"Assumed attestation=15 ms, verification=5 ms and secret transfer=10 ms give 30 ms serial initialization; 100 starts/s require 3 processing-seconds/s, exceeding one serial channel.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「新鮮性」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of freshness?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。","只檢查「背書鏈」，便可取代「新鮮性」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions.","Checking endorsement chains alone replaces verification specific to freshness."],"answer":1,"explanation":"nonce 或可靠時间把報告關聯當前會话。 相鄰的「背書鏈」有不同責任：廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Nonces/reliable time bind reports to current sessions. Neighboring endorsement chains has a different role: Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a367-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"驗證、故障與防禦邊界","titleEn":"Validation, faults and defensive boundaries","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a367-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-16"],"title":"背書鏈：架構與原理","titleEn":"Endorsement chains: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「背書鏈」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For endorsement chains, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「背書鏈」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「參考值」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around endorsement chains, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat reference values as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「背書鏈」與「參考值」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for endorsement chains and reference values supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「背書鏈」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for endorsement chains. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-17-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。","textEn":"Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-17-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「參考值」：合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「背書鏈」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring reference values: Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove endorsement chains passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-17-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「背書鏈」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of endorsement chains?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「參考值」，便可取代「背書鏈」的專屬驗證。","廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking reference values alone replaces verification specific to endorsement chains.","Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。 相鄰的「參考值」有不同責任：合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Neighboring reference values has a different role: Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-17"],"title":"背書鏈：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Endorsement chains: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「背書鏈」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For endorsement chains, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「參考值」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from reference values to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「背書鏈」與「參考值」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for endorsement chains and reference values supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「背書鏈」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for endorsement chains. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-18-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。","textEn":"Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-18-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「參考值」：合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「背書鏈」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring reference values: Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove endorsement chains passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-18-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「背書鏈」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of endorsement chains?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「參考值」，便可取代「背書鏈」的專屬驗證。","廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking reference values alone replaces verification specific to endorsement chains.","Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"廠商背書鏈須與受支持硬體版本匹配。 相鄰的「參考值」有不同責任：合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Vendor endorsement chains must match supported hardware versions. Neighboring reference values has a different role: Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-18"],"title":"參考值：架構與原理","titleEn":"Reference values: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「參考值」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For reference values, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「參考值」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「秘密釋放」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around reference values, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat secret release as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「參考值」與「秘密釋放」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for reference values and secret release supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「參考值」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for reference values. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-19-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。","textEn":"Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-19-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「秘密釋放」：只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「參考值」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring secret release: Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove reference values passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-19-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「參考值」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of reference values?","options":["合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。","證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「秘密釋放」，便可取代「參考值」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration.","The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking secret release alone replaces verification specific to reference values."],"answer":0,"explanation":"合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。 相鄰的「秘密釋放」有不同責任：只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Neighboring secret release has a different role: Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-19"],"title":"參考值：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Reference values: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「參考值」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For reference values, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「秘密釋放」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from secret release to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「參考值」與「秘密釋放」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for reference values and secret release supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「參考值」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for reference values. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-20-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。","textEn":"Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-20-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「秘密釋放」：只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「參考值」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring secret release: Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove reference values passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-20-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「參考值」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of reference values?","options":["合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。","證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「秘密釋放」，便可取代「參考值」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration.","The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking secret release alone replaces verification specific to reference values."],"answer":0,"explanation":"合法測量值來自核准發行，不由報告自行宣告。 相鄰的「秘密釋放」有不同責任：只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Approved releases define trusted measurements, not self-declaration. Neighboring secret release has a different role: Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-20"],"title":"秘密釋放：架構與原理","titleEn":"Secret release: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「秘密釋放」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For secret release, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「秘密釋放」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「軟體更新」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around secret release, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat software updates as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「秘密釋放」與「軟體更新」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for secret release and software updates supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「秘密釋放」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for secret release. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-21-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。","textEn":"Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-21-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「軟體更新」：新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「秘密釋放」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring software updates: New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove secret release passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-21-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「秘密釋放」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of secret release?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。","只檢查「軟體更新」，便可取代「秘密釋放」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels.","Checking software updates alone replaces verification specific to secret release."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。 相鄰的「軟體更新」有不同責任：新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Neighboring software updates has a different role: New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-21"],"title":"秘密釋放：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Secret release: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「秘密釋放」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For secret release, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「軟體更新」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from software updates to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「秘密釋放」與「軟體更新」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for secret release and software updates supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「秘密釋放」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for secret release. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-22-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。","textEn":"Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-22-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「軟體更新」：新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「秘密釋放」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring software updates: New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove secret release passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-22-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「秘密釋放」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of secret release?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。","只檢查「軟體更新」，便可取代「秘密釋放」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels.","Checking software updates alone replaces verification specific to secret release."],"answer":1,"explanation":"只對滿足策略且建立安全通道的工作負載釋放。 相鄰的「軟體更新」有不同責任：新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Release secrets only to policy-compliant workloads over secure channels. Neighboring software updates has a different role: New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-22"],"title":"軟體更新：架構與原理","titleEn":"Software updates: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「軟體更新」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For software updates, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「軟體更新」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「回滾限制」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around software updates, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat rollback limits as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「軟體更新」與「回滾限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for software updates and rollback limits supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「軟體更新」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for software updates. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-23-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。","textEn":"New-version measurements need reference-policy updates.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-23-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「回滾限制」：舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「軟體更新」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring rollback limits: Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove software updates passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-23-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「軟體更新」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of software updates?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「回滾限制」，便可取代「軟體更新」的專屬驗證。","新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking rollback limits alone replaces verification specific to software updates.","New-version measurements need reference-policy updates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。 相鄰的「回滾限制」有不同責任：舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Neighboring rollback limits has a different role: Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-23"],"title":"軟體更新：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Software updates: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「軟體更新」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For software updates, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「回滾限制」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from rollback limits to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 比較「軟體更新」與「回滾限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Compare whether evidence for software updates and rollback limits supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「軟體更新」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for software updates. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-24-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。","textEn":"New-version measurements need reference-policy updates.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-24-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「回滾限制」：舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「軟體更新」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring rollback limits: Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove software updates passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-24-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"保留證據，只改信任策略版本。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Fix evidence and vary trust-policy version. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「軟體更新」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of software updates?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「回滾限制」，便可取代「軟體更新」的專屬驗證。","新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking rollback limits alone replaces verification specific to software updates.","New-version measurements need reference-policy updates."],"answer":2,"explanation":"新版本測量改變需要同步更新參考政策。 相鄰的「回滾限制」有不同責任：舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"New-version measurements need reference-policy updates. Neighboring rollback limits has a different role: Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]},{"id":"a367-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"效能、復原與證據交接","titleEn":"Performance, recovery and evidence handoff","description":"四個領域技術單元各完成原理建模與對照證據，共八項可個別保存的作業。","descriptionEn":"Four domain units each pair principle modeling with controlled evidence, producing eight separately saved tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a367-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-24"],"title":"回滾限制：架構與原理","titleEn":"Rollback limits: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「回滾限制」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For rollback limits, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「回滾限制」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「I/O 邊界」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around rollback limits, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat i/o boundaries as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「回滾限制」與「I/O 邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for rollback limits and i/o boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「回滾限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for rollback limits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-25-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。","textEn":"Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-25-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「I/O 邊界」：資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「回滾限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring i/o boundaries: Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove rollback limits passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-25-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「回滾限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of rollback limits?","options":["舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。","機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「I/O 邊界」，便可取代「回滾限制」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities.","Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking i/o boundaries alone replaces verification specific to rollback limits."],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。 相鄰的「I/O 邊界」有不同責任：資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Neighboring i/o boundaries has a different role: Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-25"],"title":"回滾限制：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Rollback limits: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「回滾限制」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For rollback limits, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「I/O 邊界」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from i/o boundaries to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「回滾限制」與「I/O 邊界」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for rollback limits and i/o boundaries supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「回滾限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for rollback limits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-26-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。","textEn":"Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-26-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「I/O 邊界」：資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「回滾限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring i/o boundaries: Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove rollback limits passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-26-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「回滾限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of rollback limits?","options":["舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。","機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「I/O 邊界」，便可取代「回滾限制」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities.","Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking i/o boundaries alone replaces verification specific to rollback limits."],"answer":0,"explanation":"舊版本雖曾合法，也可能因漏洞不再獲准。 相鄰的「I/O 邊界」有不同責任：資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Once-approved old versions may later be prohibited for vulnerabilities. Neighboring i/o boundaries has a different role: Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-26"],"title":"I/O 邊界：架構與原理","titleEn":"I/O boundaries: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「I/O 邊界」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For i/o boundaries, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「I/O 邊界」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「側信道限制」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around i/o boundaries, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat side-channel limits as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「I/O 邊界」與「側信道限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for i/o boundaries and side-channel limits supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「I/O 邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for i/o boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-27-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。","textEn":"Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-27-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「側信道限制」：保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「I/O 邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring side-channel limits: Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove i/o boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-27-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「I/O 邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of i/o boundaries?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。","只檢查「側信道限制」，便可取代「I/O 邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection.","Checking side-channel limits alone replaces verification specific to i/o boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。 相鄰的「側信道限制」有不同責任：保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Neighboring side-channel limits has a different role: Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-27"],"title":"I/O 邊界：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"I/O boundaries: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「I/O 邊界」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For i/o boundaries, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「側信道限制」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from side-channel limits to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「I/O 邊界」與「側信道限制」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for i/o boundaries and side-channel limits supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「I/O 邊界」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for i/o boundaries. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-28-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。","textEn":"Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-28-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「側信道限制」：保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「I/O 邊界」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring side-channel limits: Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove i/o boundaries passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-28-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「I/O 邊界」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of i/o boundaries?","options":["證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。","只檢查「側信道限制」，便可取代「I/O 邊界」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection.","Checking side-channel limits alone replaces verification specific to i/o boundaries."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資料離開保護記憶體後仍需通道與應用保護。 相鄰的「側信道限制」有不同責任：保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Data leaving protected memory still needs channel/application protection. Neighboring side-channel limits has a different role: Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-28"],"title":"側信道限制：架構與原理","titleEn":"Side-channel limits: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「側信道限制」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For side-channel limits, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「側信道限制」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「部署驗收」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around side-channel limits, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat deployment acceptance as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「側信道限制」與「部署驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for side-channel limits and deployment acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「側信道限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for side-channel limits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-29-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。","textEn":"Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-29-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「部署驗收」：需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「側信道限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring deployment acceptance: Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove side-channel limits passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-29-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「側信道限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of side-channel limits?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「部署驗收」，便可取代「側信道限制」的專屬驗證。","保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking deployment acceptance alone replaces verification specific to side-channel limits.","Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。 相鄰的「部署驗收」有不同責任：需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Neighboring deployment acceptance has a different role: Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-29"],"title":"側信道限制：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Side-channel limits: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「側信道限制」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For side-channel limits, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「部署驗收」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from deployment acceptance to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「側信道限制」與「部署驗收」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for side-channel limits and deployment acceptance supports the same inference.","failure":"機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「側信道限制」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for side-channel limits. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-30-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。","textEn":"Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-30-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「部署驗收」：需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「側信道限制」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring deployment acceptance: Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove side-channel limits passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-30-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「側信道限制」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of side-channel limits?","options":["機密運算使應用自身所有錯誤自動消失。","只檢查「部署驗收」，便可取代「側信道限制」的專屬驗證。","保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。"],"optionsEn":["Confidential computing automatically removes every application bug.","Checking deployment acceptance alone replaces verification specific to side-channel limits.","Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保護模型不能自動涵盖所有時间與流量泄漏。 相鄰的「部署驗收」有不同責任：需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Protection models do not automatically cover all timing/traffic leakage. Neighboring deployment acceptance has a different role: Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":30,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-30"],"title":"部署驗收：架構與原理","titleEn":"Deployment acceptance: architecture and principle","objective":"針對「部署驗收」建立有邊界、可反駁的系統模型。","objectiveEn":"For deployment acceptance, construct a bounded falsifiable system model.","instruction":"觀看師傅的功能示意後，以「部署驗收」為中心標出輸入、輸出、信任或資源邊界，並在學徒工作台排列資料流或元件。原理是：需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。 使用自行編寫的兩組小型資料或試算表，建立基準與一次只改一項的對照：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 先寫出可被反駁的預測；把「威胁模型」視為相鄰問題，說明它如何影響模型而不能混同。數值只採本課假想算例或自訂並列明單位；本步保存架構圖、假設表與預測。","instructionEn":"After the mentor functional diagram, mark inputs, outputs and trust/resource boundaries around deployment acceptance, then arrange components or data flows in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Create two small authored datasets or spreadsheet cases: a baseline and a one-variable change. Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Predict a falsifiable outcome before evaluating it. Treat threat models as a neighboring issue and explain its influence without conflating them. Use only the stated hypothetical case or declared assumed inputs/units. Save the architecture, assumptions and prediction.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「部署驗收」與「威胁模型」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for deployment acceptance and threat models supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「部署驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for deployment acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-31-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。","textEn":"Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-31-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「威胁模型」：先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「部署驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring threat models: Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove deployment acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-31-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-31-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想證明 15 ms、驗證 5 ms、秘密傳送 10 ms，串行初始化合 30 ms；若每秒 100 次初始作業且不可並行，每秒需 3 s 處理，單通道不足。","textEn":"Assumed attestation=15 ms, verification=5 ms and secret transfer=10 ms give 30 ms serial initialization; 100 starts/s require 3 processing-seconds/s, exceeding one serial channel.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「部署驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of deployment acceptance?","options":["需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。","證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「威胁模型」，便可取代「部署驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection.","The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking threat models alone replaces verification specific to deployment acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。 相鄰的「威胁模型」有不同責任：先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Neighboring threat models has a different role: Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}},{"id":"a367-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":40,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"prerequisiteIds":["a367-v11-31"],"title":"部署驗收：對照試驗與證據","titleEn":"Deployment acceptance: controlled experiment and evidence","objective":"針對「部署驗收」完成含競爭原因及不確定度的驗收紀錄。","objectiveEn":"For deployment acceptance, complete acceptance evidence with competing causes and uncertainty.","instruction":"重播本單元示意，讀取自製的基準與擾動紀錄，不接觸未授權目標。對照「需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。」，執行下列紙上或本地合成資料試驗：模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 分開記錄預測、觀察與不確定度，再提出至少兩個可能原因；利用「威胁模型」的獨立證據排除一個原因。若結果只來自模型，標記為模擬，不能當作真實設備量測。最後說明目前應接受、保留或拒絕哪一項要求，並保存可重算資料。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit diagram and inspect your authored baseline/perturbed records without accessing unauthorized targets. Evaluate the principle: Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Conduct this paper or local synthetic-data experiment: Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Record prediction, observation and uncertainty separately, propose two competing causes and use independent evidence from threat models to exclude one. Model outputs must remain labeled simulation, not physical measurements. Explain which requirement to accept, hold or reject and retain recomputable records.","observation":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 比較「部署驗收」與「威胁模型」的證據是否支持相同推論。","observationEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Compare whether evidence for deployment acceptance and threat models supports the same inference.","failure":"證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。 這是本課要排除的誤判；先核對模型邊界、來源版本及缺失證據。","failureEn":"The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted. This is a misconception to reject; check boundaries, source versions and missing evidence.","check":"提交「部署驗收」的功能草圖、基準／擾動表、單位或欄位定義、可反駁預測及接受／保留理由。需能重算本課假想例，並說明相鄰機制不可取代的驗證。","checkEn":"Submit a functional sketch, baseline/perturbation table, unit/field definitions, falsifiable prediction and accept/hold rationale for deployment acceptance. Recompute the course case and explain verification that the neighboring mechanism cannot replace.","knowledge":[{"id":"a367-v11-32-k1","title":"原理、架構與適用邊界","titleEn":"Principle, architecture and applicability","text":"需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。","textEn":"Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-32-k2","title":"相鄰機制與不可混同處","titleEn":"Neighboring mechanism and separation","text":"相鄰的「威胁模型」：先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。 必須另列其證據，不能把這項機制的通過當作「部署驗收」已通過。","textEn":"Neighboring threat models: Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Record its evidence separately; its success does not prove deployment acceptance passes.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-32-k3","title":"受控對照與證據品質","titleEn":"Controlled comparison and evidence quality","text":"模擬 host 攻击面之外的應用授權缺陷。 只變一個條件，保留相同資料格式、時間範圍及分母；模型估計與實測證據要分別標記。","textEn":"Model application authorization flaws beyond the host-protection scope. Change one condition and retain comparable formats, intervals and denominators; label estimates separately from measured evidence.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"]},{"id":"a367-v11-32-k4","title":"可重算的原創假想例","titleEn":"Recomputable original hypothetical case","text":"假想證明 15 ms、驗證 5 ms、秘密傳送 10 ms，串行初始化合 30 ms；若每秒 100 次初始作業且不可並行，每秒需 3 s 處理，單通道不足。","textEn":"Assumed attestation=15 ms, verification=5 ms and secret transfer=10 ms give 30 ms serial initialization; 100 starts/s require 3 processing-seconds/s, exceeding one serial channel.","sourceIds":["v11b-sev","v11b-rats","v11b-keys"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"針對「部署驗收」的原理與可觀測性，哪項最直接成立？","questionEn":"Which statement most directly explains the principle/observability of deployment acceptance?","options":["需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。","證明報告存在便證明其測量值得信任。","只檢查「威胁模型」，便可取代「部署驗收」的專屬驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection.","The existence of an attestation report proves its measurements trusted.","Checking threat models alone replaces verification specific to deployment acceptance."],"answer":0,"explanation":"需測試錯誤測量、過期證明與授權拒絕。 相鄰的「威胁模型」有不同責任：先定義不信任 host 的哪些能力與保護目標。因此不能用該項通過或課內誤判取代本單元證據。","explanationEn":"Test wrong measurements, stale reports and authorization rejection. Neighboring threat models has a different role: Define distrusted-host capabilities and protection goals first. Its success or the stated misconception cannot replace unit-specific evidence."}}]}],"scope":"公開原理的離線／本地合成資料工程教育。只使用自行生成資料或明確獲授權的測試環境；不提供真實目標掃描、漏洞利用、惡意程式、車輛／工控注入或實際射頻發射程序。數值為原創假設，非供應商保證或現場驗收標準。","scopeEn":"Offline/local synthetic-data engineering education from public principles. Use authored data or explicitly authorized test environments only. No real-target scanning, exploitation, malware, vehicle/OT injection or live RF procedures. Numerical cases are original assumptions, not supplier guarantees or field acceptance criteria.","workedExample":{"title":"原創假想量化例與限制","titleEn":"Original hypothetical quantitative case and limits","text":"假想證明 15 ms、驗證 5 ms、秘密傳送 10 ms，串行初始化合 30 ms；若每秒 100 次初始作業且不可並行，每秒需 3 s 處理，單通道不足。","textEn":"Assumed attestation=15 ms, verification=5 ms and secret transfer=10 ms give 30 ms serial initialization; 100 starts/s require 3 processing-seconds/s, exceeding one serial channel.","assumptions":"只採算例中明列的教學條件；效能與安全估計須依拓撲、分布、開銷、版本與不確定度重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use only the stated teaching assumptions; recalculate for topology, distribution, overhead, versions and uncertainty.","sourceScope":"作者自行設定的教學數值；官方來源支援原理與尺寸規格，未聲稱量測此假想平台。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen teaching inputs; official sources support principles and specified material sizes, not measurements of this hypothetical platform."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["威胁模型","Attester","背書鏈","回滾限制"],"labelsEn":["Threat models","Attesters","Endorsement chains","Rollback limits"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a368","title":"軟體弱點管理流程","titleEn":"Software vulnerability-management workflows","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以弱點風險、相依圖與修補放行串連 16 個原創技術單元、32 步；涵蓋原理解析、架構圖、假想量化、合成資料實驗、競爭失效原因及可重算驗收。","summaryEn":"Sixteen original technical units and 32 tasks connect vulnerability risk, dependency graphs and patch acceptance with principles, architectures, assumed calculations, synthetic experiments, competing failure causes and reproducible acceptance.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a368-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"資產與風險","titleEn":"Assets and risk","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「資產與風險」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop assets and risk through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a368-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"資產識別：原理與架構","titleEn":"Asset identity: principles and architecture","objective":"以「資產識別」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for asset identity.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「資產識別」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：同一主機的版本、角色與責任人須以穩定識別串連。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for asset identity. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Stable identifiers connect version, role and accountable owner. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：主機名稱相同便必然是同一資產。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal hostnames necessarily mean equal assets. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「資產識別」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for asset identity; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-01-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"同一主機的版本、角色與責任人須以穩定識別串連。","textEn":"Stable identifiers connect version, role and accountable owner.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-01-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a368-v11-01-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 200 個受影響資產中完成 170 個，覆蓋率為 85%；若另有 10 個盤點遺漏資產，真正分母為 210，覆蓋率降至 80.95%。覆蓋不是風險消除率，例子不使用實際弱點或目標。","textEn":"In a synthetic inventory, 170 of 200 affected assets gives 85% coverage. Ten missing assets change the denominator to 210 and coverage to 80.95%. Coverage is not risk-elimination probability; no real vulnerability or target is used.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「資產識別」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for asset identity?","options":["主機名稱相同便必然是同一資產。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「資產識別」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","同一主機的版本、角色與責任人須以穩定識別串連。"],"optionsEn":["Equal hostnames necessarily mean equal assets.","One matching output proves asset identity for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Stable identifiers connect version, role and accountable owner."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一主機的版本、角色與責任人須以穩定識別串連。 以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。 因此「主機名稱相同便必然是同一資產。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Stable identifiers connect version, role and accountable owner. Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. The alternative \"Equal hostnames necessarily mean equal assets.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-01"],"title":"資產識別：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Asset identity: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「資產識別」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for asset identity.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。」；將結果與「同一主機的版本、角色與責任人須以穩定識別串連。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. Compare results against: Stable identifiers connect version, role and accountable owner. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：主機名稱相同便必然是同一資產。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal hostnames necessarily mean equal assets. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「資產識別」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「主機名稱相同便必然是同一資產。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for asset identity; explain why this claim fails: Equal hostnames necessarily mean equal assets.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-02-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"同一主機的版本、角色與責任人須以穩定識別串連。","textEn":"Stable identifiers connect version, role and accountable owner.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-02-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a368-v11-02-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 200 個受影響資產中完成 170 個，覆蓋率為 85%；若另有 10 個盤點遺漏資產，真正分母為 210，覆蓋率降至 80.95%。覆蓋不是風險消除率，例子不使用實際弱點或目標。","textEn":"In a synthetic inventory, 170 of 200 affected assets gives 85% coverage. Ten missing assets change the denominator to 210 and coverage to 80.95%. Coverage is not risk-elimination probability; no real vulnerability or target is used.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「資產識別」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for asset identity?","options":["以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。","主機名稱相同便必然是同一資產。","先把「資產識別」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory.","Equal hostnames necessarily mean equal assets.","Tune the displayed asset identity result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一主機的版本、角色與責任人須以穩定識別串連。 以合成清單找出重複名稱與缺漏責任人。 因此「主機名稱相同便必然是同一資產。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Stable identifiers connect version, role and accountable owner. Find duplicate names and missing owners in a synthetic inventory. The alternative \"Equal hostnames necessarily mean equal assets.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-02"],"title":"軟體物料：原理與架構","titleEn":"Software inventory: principles and architecture","objective":"以「軟體物料」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for software inventory.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「軟體物料」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：應用程式版本不能代表所有內含函式庫版本。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for software inventory. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Application versions do not identify every bundled dependency. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只盤點最上層應用程式即可。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Inventorying only the top application is sufficient. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「軟體物料」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for software inventory; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-03-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"應用程式版本不能代表所有內含函式庫版本。","textEn":"Application versions do not identify every bundled dependency.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-03-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「軟體物料」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for software inventory?","options":["只盤點最上層應用程式即可。","應用程式版本不能代表所有內含函式庫版本。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「軟體物料」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Inventorying only the top application is sufficient.","Application versions do not identify every bundled dependency.","One matching output proves software inventory for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"應用程式版本不能代表所有內含函式庫版本。 比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。 因此「只盤點最上層應用程式即可。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Application versions do not identify every bundled dependency. Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. The alternative \"Inventorying only the top application is sufficient.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-03"],"title":"軟體物料：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Software inventory: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「軟體物料」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for software inventory.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。」；將結果與「應用程式版本不能代表所有內含函式庫版本。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. Compare results against: Application versions do not identify every bundled dependency. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只盤點最上層應用程式即可。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Inventorying only the top application is sufficient. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「軟體物料」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「只盤點最上層應用程式即可。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for software inventory; explain why this claim fails: Inventorying only the top application is sufficient.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-04-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"應用程式版本不能代表所有內含函式庫版本。","textEn":"Application versions do not identify every bundled dependency.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-04-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「軟體物料」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for software inventory?","options":["只盤點最上層應用程式即可。","先把「軟體物料」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。"],"optionsEn":["Inventorying only the top application is sufficient.","Tune the displayed software inventory result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Compare direct and transitive dependency versions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"應用程式版本不能代表所有內含函式庫版本。 比較直接與傳遞相依的版本圖。 因此「只盤點最上層應用程式即可。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Application versions do not identify every bundled dependency. Compare direct and transitive dependency versions. The alternative \"Inventorying only the top application is sufficient.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-04"],"title":"暴露面：原理與架構","titleEn":"Exposure surface: principles and architecture","objective":"以「暴露面」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for exposure surface.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「暴露面」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：可達性與許可權前提會改變同一弱點的情境風險。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for exposure surface. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Reachability and privilege prerequisites change contextual risk. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：分數相同的弱點都有相同營運風險。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal scores imply equal operational risk. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「暴露面」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for exposure surface; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-05-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可達性與許可權前提會改變同一弱點的情境風險。","textEn":"Reachability and privilege prerequisites change contextual risk.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-05-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「暴露面」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for exposure surface?","options":["可達性與許可權前提會改變同一弱點的情境風險。","分數相同的弱點都有相同營運風險。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「暴露面」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Reachability and privilege prerequisites change contextual risk.","Equal scores imply equal operational risk.","One matching output proves exposure surface for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可達性與許可權前提會改變同一弱點的情境風險。 在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。 因此「分數相同的弱點都有相同營運風險。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reachability and privilege prerequisites change contextual risk. Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. The alternative \"Equal scores imply equal operational risk.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-05"],"title":"暴露面：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Exposure surface: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「暴露面」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for exposure surface.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。」；將結果與「可達性與許可權前提會改變同一弱點的情境風險。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. Compare results against: Reachability and privilege prerequisites change contextual risk. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：分數相同的弱點都有相同營運風險。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal scores imply equal operational risk. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「暴露面」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「分數相同的弱點都有相同營運風險。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for exposure surface; explain why this claim fails: Equal scores imply equal operational risk.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-06-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可達性與許可權前提會改變同一弱點的情境風險。","textEn":"Reachability and privilege prerequisites change contextual risk.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-06-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「暴露面」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for exposure surface?","options":["分數相同的弱點都有相同營運風險。","在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。","先把「暴露面」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Equal scores imply equal operational risk.","Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram.","Tune the displayed exposure surface result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可達性與許可權前提會改變同一弱點的情境風險。 在本地假想網路圖分開外部、內部及離線資產。 因此「分數相同的弱點都有相同營運風險。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reachability and privilege prerequisites change contextual risk. Separate external, internal and offline assets on a local diagram. The alternative \"Equal scores imply equal operational risk.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-06"],"title":"優先序：原理與架構","titleEn":"Prioritization: principles and architecture","objective":"以「優先序」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for prioritization.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「優先序」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：利用證據、重要性與可補償控制共同決定順序。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for prioritization. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Evidence, criticality and compensating controls jointly inform priority. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有低分專案可永久略過。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: All low-score items can be ignored permanently. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「優先序」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for prioritization; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-07-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"利用證據、重要性與可補償控制共同決定順序。","textEn":"Evidence, criticality and compensating controls jointly inform priority.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-07-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「優先序」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for prioritization?","options":["所有低分專案可永久略過。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「優先序」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","利用證據、重要性與可補償控制共同決定順序。"],"optionsEn":["All low-score items can be ignored permanently.","One matching output proves prioritization for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Evidence, criticality and compensating controls jointly inform priority."],"answer":2,"explanation":"利用證據、重要性與可補償控制共同決定順序。 用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。 因此「所有低分專案可永久略過。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Evidence, criticality and compensating controls jointly inform priority. Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. The alternative \"All low-score items can be ignored permanently.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-07"],"title":"優先序：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Prioritization: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「優先序」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for prioritization.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。」；將結果與「利用證據、重要性與可補償控制共同決定順序。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. Compare results against: Evidence, criticality and compensating controls jointly inform priority. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有低分專案可永久略過。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: All low-score items can be ignored permanently. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「優先序」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「所有低分專案可永久略過。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for prioritization; explain why this claim fails: All low-score items can be ignored permanently.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-08-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"利用證據、重要性與可補償控制共同決定順序。","textEn":"Evidence, criticality and compensating controls jointly inform priority.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-08-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「優先序」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for prioritization?","options":["用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。","所有低分專案可永久略過。","先把「優先序」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure.","All low-score items can be ignored permanently.","Tune the displayed prioritization result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"利用證據、重要性與可補償控制共同決定順序。 用匿名情境比較同分不同暴露面的排序。 因此「所有低分專案可永久略過。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Evidence, criticality and compensating controls jointly inform priority. Rank anonymous equal-score cases with different exposure. The alternative \"All low-score items can be ignored permanently.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a368-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"修補與相依","titleEn":"Patches and dependencies","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「修補與相依」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop patches and dependencies through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a368-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-08"],"title":"供應來源：原理與架構","titleEn":"Update provenance: principles and architecture","objective":"以「供應來源」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for update provenance.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「供應來源」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：更新檔的完整性與供應者身分是不同檢查。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for update provenance. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Update integrity and publisher identity are distinct checks. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：雜湊吻合便證明供應者可信。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A matching hash proves the publisher is trusted. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「供應來源」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for update provenance; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-09-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"更新檔的完整性與供應者身分是不同檢查。","textEn":"Update integrity and publisher identity are distinct checks.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-09-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「供應來源」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for update provenance?","options":["雜湊吻合便證明供應者可信。","更新檔的完整性與供應者身分是不同檢查。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「供應來源」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["A matching hash proves the publisher is trusted.","Update integrity and publisher identity are distinct checks.","One matching output proves update provenance for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"更新檔的完整性與供應者身分是不同檢查。 對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。 因此「雜湊吻合便證明供應者可信。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Update integrity and publisher identity are distinct checks. Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. The alternative \"A matching hash proves the publisher is trusted.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-09"],"title":"供應來源：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Update provenance: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「供應來源」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for update provenance.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。」；將結果與「更新檔的完整性與供應者身分是不同檢查。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. Compare results against: Update integrity and publisher identity are distinct checks. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：雜湊吻合便證明供應者可信。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A matching hash proves the publisher is trusted. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「供應來源」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「雜湊吻合便證明供應者可信。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for update provenance; explain why this claim fails: A matching hash proves the publisher is trusted.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-10-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"更新檔的完整性與供應者身分是不同檢查。","textEn":"Update integrity and publisher identity are distinct checks.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-10-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「供應來源」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for update provenance?","options":["雜湊吻合便證明供應者可信。","先把「供應來源」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。"],"optionsEn":["A matching hash proves the publisher is trusted.","Tune the displayed update provenance result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更新檔的完整性與供應者身分是不同檢查。 對自製測試包核對雜湊與簽章信任根。 因此「雜湊吻合便證明供應者可信。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Update integrity and publisher identity are distinct checks. Check hashes and signature trust roots on a self-made package. The alternative \"A matching hash proves the publisher is trusted.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-10"],"title":"版本相依：原理與架構","titleEn":"Version dependencies: principles and architecture","objective":"以「版本相依」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for version dependencies.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「版本相依」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：修補一個元件可能使相依介面不相容。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for version dependencies. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Patching one component may break dependent interfaces. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：安全更新不可能改變功能介面。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Security updates cannot change interfaces. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「版本相依」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for version dependencies; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-11-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"修補一個元件可能使相依介面不相容。","textEn":"Patching one component may break dependent interfaces.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-11-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「版本相依」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for version dependencies?","options":["修補一個元件可能使相依介面不相容。","安全更新不可能改變功能介面。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「版本相依」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Patching one component may break dependent interfaces.","Security updates cannot change interfaces.","One matching output proves version dependencies for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"修補一個元件可能使相依介面不相容。 將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。 因此「安全更新不可能改變功能介面。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Patching one component may break dependent interfaces. Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. The alternative \"Security updates cannot change interfaces.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-11"],"title":"版本相依：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Version dependencies: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「版本相依」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for version dependencies.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。」；將結果與「修補一個元件可能使相依介面不相容。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. Compare results against: Patching one component may break dependent interfaces. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：安全更新不可能改變功能介面。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Security updates cannot change interfaces. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「版本相依」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「安全更新不可能改變功能介面。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for version dependencies; explain why this claim fails: Security updates cannot change interfaces.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-12-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"修補一個元件可能使相依介面不相容。","textEn":"Patching one component may break dependent interfaces.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-12-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「版本相依」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for version dependencies?","options":["安全更新不可能改變功能介面。","將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。","先把「版本相依」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Security updates cannot change interfaces.","Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies.","Tune the displayed version dependencies result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"修補一個元件可能使相依介面不相容。 將假想 API 版本變更傳播到相依圖。 因此「安全更新不可能改變功能介面。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Patching one component may break dependent interfaces. Propagate a synthetic API change through dependencies. The alternative \"Security updates cannot change interfaces.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-12"],"title":"變更視窗：原理與架構","titleEn":"Change windows: principles and architecture","objective":"以「變更視窗」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for change windows.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「變更視窗」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：可用性與風險會共同約束部署時間。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for change windows. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Availability and risk jointly constrain deployment timing. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：最短部署時間必然最安全。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: The shortest deployment is necessarily safest. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「變更視窗」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for change windows; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-13-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可用性與風險會共同約束部署時間。","textEn":"Availability and risk jointly constrain deployment timing.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-13-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「變更視窗」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for change windows?","options":["最短部署時間必然最安全。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「變更視窗」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","可用性與風險會共同約束部署時間。"],"optionsEn":["The shortest deployment is necessarily safest.","One matching output proves change windows for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Availability and risk jointly constrain deployment timing."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可用性與風險會共同約束部署時間。 比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。 因此「最短部署時間必然最安全。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Availability and risk jointly constrain deployment timing. Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. The alternative \"The shortest deployment is necessarily safest.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-13"],"title":"變更視窗：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Change windows: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「變更視窗」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for change windows.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。」；將結果與「可用性與風險會共同約束部署時間。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. Compare results against: Availability and risk jointly constrain deployment timing. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：最短部署時間必然最安全。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: The shortest deployment is necessarily safest. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「變更視窗」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「最短部署時間必然最安全。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for change windows; explain why this claim fails: The shortest deployment is necessarily safest.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-14-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可用性與風險會共同約束部署時間。","textEn":"Availability and risk jointly constrain deployment timing.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-14-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「變更視窗」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for change windows?","options":["比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。","最短部署時間必然最安全。","先把「變更視窗」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy.","The shortest deployment is necessarily safest.","Tune the displayed change windows result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可用性與風險會共同約束部署時間。 比較有備援與單節點的停機預算。 因此「最短部署時間必然最安全。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Availability and risk jointly constrain deployment timing. Compare downtime budgets with and without redundancy. The alternative \"The shortest deployment is necessarily safest.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-14"],"title":"回退資產：原理與架構","titleEn":"Rollback assets: principles and architecture","objective":"以「回退資產」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for rollback assets.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「回退資產」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：回退需儲存資料格式、設定及舊版依賴。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for rollback assets. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Rollback needs data-format, configuration and dependency compatibility. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：保留舊執行檔就保證可回退。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Keeping an old executable guarantees rollback. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「回退資產」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for rollback assets; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-15-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"回退需儲存資料格式、設定及舊版依賴。","textEn":"Rollback needs data-format, configuration and dependency compatibility.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-15-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「回退資產」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for rollback assets?","options":["保留舊執行檔就保證可回退。","回退需儲存資料格式、設定及舊版依賴。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「回退資產」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Keeping an old executable guarantees rollback.","Rollback needs data-format, configuration and dependency compatibility.","One matching output proves rollback assets for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"回退需儲存資料格式、設定及舊版依賴。 模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。 因此「保留舊執行檔就保證可回退。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Rollback needs data-format, configuration and dependency compatibility. Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. The alternative \"Keeping an old executable guarantees rollback.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-15"],"title":"回退資產：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Rollback assets: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「回退資產」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for rollback assets.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。」；將結果與「回退需儲存資料格式、設定及舊版依賴。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. Compare results against: Rollback needs data-format, configuration and dependency compatibility. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：保留舊執行檔就保證可回退。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Keeping an old executable guarantees rollback. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「回退資產」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「保留舊執行檔就保證可回退。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for rollback assets; explain why this claim fails: Keeping an old executable guarantees rollback.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-16-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"回退需儲存資料格式、設定及舊版依賴。","textEn":"Rollback needs data-format, configuration and dependency compatibility.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-16-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「回退資產」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for rollback assets?","options":["保留舊執行檔就保證可回退。","先把「回退資產」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。"],"optionsEn":["Keeping an old executable guarantees rollback.","Tune the displayed rollback assets result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Simulate new data unreadable by an old version."],"answer":2,"explanation":"回退需儲存資料格式、設定及舊版依賴。 模擬新版資料無法被舊版讀取的回退。 因此「保留舊執行檔就保證可回退。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Rollback needs data-format, configuration and dependency compatibility. Simulate new data unreadable by an old version. The alternative \"Keeping an old executable guarantees rollback.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a368-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"測試與部署","titleEn":"Testing and deployment","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「測試與部署」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop testing and deployment through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a368-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-16"],"title":"測試矩陣：原理與架構","titleEn":"Test matrix: principles and architecture","objective":"以「測試矩陣」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for test matrix.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「測試矩陣」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：安全、功能與負載回歸應各有可觀測條件。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for test matrix. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Security, functional and load regression need separate criteria. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：能啟動便等於回歸測試透過。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Starting successfully equals passing regression. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「測試矩陣」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for test matrix; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-17-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"安全、功能與負載回歸應各有可觀測條件。","textEn":"Security, functional and load regression need separate criteria.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-17-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「測試矩陣」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for test matrix?","options":["安全、功能與負載回歸應各有可觀測條件。","能啟動便等於回歸測試透過。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「測試矩陣」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Security, functional and load regression need separate criteria.","Starting successfully equals passing regression.","One matching output proves test matrix for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"安全、功能與負載回歸應各有可觀測條件。 在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。 因此「能啟動便等於回歸測試透過。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Security, functional and load regression need separate criteria. List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. The alternative \"Starting successfully equals passing regression.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-17"],"title":"測試矩陣：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Test matrix: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「測試矩陣」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for test matrix.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。」；將結果與「安全、功能與負載回歸應各有可觀測條件。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. Compare results against: Security, functional and load regression need separate criteria. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：能啟動便等於回歸測試透過。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Starting successfully equals passing regression. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「測試矩陣」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「能啟動便等於回歸測試透過。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for test matrix; explain why this claim fails: Starting successfully equals passing regression.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-18-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"安全、功能與負載回歸應各有可觀測條件。","textEn":"Security, functional and load regression need separate criteria.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-18-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「測試矩陣」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for test matrix?","options":["能啟動便等於回歸測試透過。","在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。","先把「測試矩陣」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Starting successfully equals passing regression.","List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service.","Tune the displayed test matrix result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"安全、功能與負載回歸應各有可觀測條件。 在玩具服務列出三類測試與預期輸出。 因此「能啟動便等於回歸測試透過。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Security, functional and load regression need separate criteria. List three test classes and expected outputs for a toy service. The alternative \"Starting successfully equals passing regression.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-18"],"title":"金絲雀部署：原理與架構","titleEn":"Canary rollout: principles and architecture","objective":"以「金絲雀部署」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for canary rollout.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「金絲雀部署」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：少量先行部署降低影響範圍但不代表所有負載。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for canary rollout. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: A small canary limits impact but may not represent all workloads. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：金絲雀無錯便可略過後續監測。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: An error-free canary removes further monitoring needs. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「金絲雀部署」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for canary rollout; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-19-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"少量先行部署降低影響範圍但不代表所有負載。","textEn":"A small canary limits impact but may not represent all workloads.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-19-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「金絲雀部署」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for canary rollout?","options":["金絲雀無錯便可略過後續監測。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「金絲雀部署」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","少量先行部署降低影響範圍但不代表所有負載。"],"optionsEn":["An error-free canary removes further monitoring needs.","One matching output proves canary rollout for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","A small canary limits impact but may not represent all workloads."],"answer":2,"explanation":"少量先行部署降低影響範圍但不代表所有負載。 比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。 因此「金絲雀無錯便可略過後續監測。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"A small canary limits impact but may not represent all workloads. Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. The alternative \"An error-free canary removes further monitoring needs.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-19"],"title":"金絲雀部署：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Canary rollout: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「金絲雀部署」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for canary rollout.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。」；將結果與「少量先行部署降低影響範圍但不代表所有負載。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. Compare results against: A small canary limits impact but may not represent all workloads. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：金絲雀無錯便可略過後續監測。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: An error-free canary removes further monitoring needs. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「金絲雀部署」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「金絲雀無錯便可略過後續監測。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for canary rollout; explain why this claim fails: An error-free canary removes further monitoring needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-20-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"少量先行部署降低影響範圍但不代表所有負載。","textEn":"A small canary limits impact but may not represent all workloads.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-20-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「金絲雀部署」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for canary rollout?","options":["比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。","金絲雀無錯便可略過後續監測。","先把「金絲雀部署」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions.","An error-free canary removes further monitoring needs.","Tune the displayed canary rollout result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"少量先行部署降低影響範圍但不代表所有負載。 比較合成金絲雀與全量流量分佈。 因此「金絲雀無錯便可略過後續監測。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"A small canary limits impact but may not represent all workloads. Compare synthetic canary and full traffic distributions. The alternative \"An error-free canary removes further monitoring needs.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-20"],"title":"健康閘門：原理與架構","titleEn":"Health gates: principles and architecture","objective":"以「健康閘門」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for health gates.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「健康閘門」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：部署閘門需含錯誤率、延遲及資料一致性。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for health gates. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Rollout gates include errors, latency and data consistency. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只監測平均延遲即可放行。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Mean latency alone is enough for acceptance. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「健康閘門」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for health gates; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-21-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"部署閘門需含錯誤率、延遲及資料一致性。","textEn":"Rollout gates include errors, latency and data consistency.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-21-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「健康閘門」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for health gates?","options":["只監測平均延遲即可放行。","部署閘門需含錯誤率、延遲及資料一致性。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「健康閘門」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Mean latency alone is enough for acceptance.","Rollout gates include errors, latency and data consistency.","One matching output proves health gates for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"部署閘門需含錯誤率、延遲及資料一致性。 故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。 因此「只監測平均延遲即可放行。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Rollout gates include errors, latency and data consistency. Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. The alternative \"Mean latency alone is enough for acceptance.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-21"],"title":"健康閘門：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Health gates: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「健康閘門」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for health gates.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。」；將結果與「部署閘門需含錯誤率、延遲及資料一致性。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. Compare results against: Rollout gates include errors, latency and data consistency. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只監測平均延遲即可放行。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Mean latency alone is enough for acceptance. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「健康閘門」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「只監測平均延遲即可放行。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for health gates; explain why this claim fails: Mean latency alone is enough for acceptance.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-22-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"部署閘門需含錯誤率、延遲及資料一致性。","textEn":"Rollout gates include errors, latency and data consistency.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-22-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「健康閘門」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for health gates?","options":["只監測平均延遲即可放行。","先把「健康閘門」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。"],"optionsEn":["Mean latency alone is enough for acceptance.","Tune the displayed health gates result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency."],"answer":2,"explanation":"部署閘門需含錯誤率、延遲及資料一致性。 故意提供低錯誤率但高尾延遲的假想報告。 因此「只監測平均延遲即可放行。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Rollout gates include errors, latency and data consistency. Inspect a report with low errors but high tail latency. The alternative \"Mean latency alone is enough for acceptance.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-22"],"title":"分批節奏：原理與架構","titleEn":"Batch pacing: principles and architecture","objective":"以「分批節奏」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for batch pacing.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「分批節奏」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：同時失去多個故障域可能耗盡備援。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for batch pacing. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Concurrent changes across fault domains can exhaust redundancy. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每批數量相同便有相同故障風險。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal batch sizes imply equal failure risk. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「分批節奏」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for batch pacing; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-23-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"同時失去多個故障域可能耗盡備援。","textEn":"Concurrent changes across fault domains can exhaust redundancy.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-23-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分批節奏」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for batch pacing?","options":["同時失去多個故障域可能耗盡備援。","每批數量相同便有相同故障風險。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「分批節奏」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Concurrent changes across fault domains can exhaust redundancy.","Equal batch sizes imply equal failure risk.","One matching output proves batch pacing for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同時失去多個故障域可能耗盡備援。 在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。 因此「每批數量相同便有相同故障風險。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Concurrent changes across fault domains can exhaust redundancy. Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. The alternative \"Equal batch sizes imply equal failure risk.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-23"],"title":"分批節奏：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Batch pacing: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「分批節奏」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for batch pacing.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。」；將結果與「同時失去多個故障域可能耗盡備援。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. Compare results against: Concurrent changes across fault domains can exhaust redundancy. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每批數量相同便有相同故障風險。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal batch sizes imply equal failure risk. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「分批節奏」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「每批數量相同便有相同故障風險。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for batch pacing; explain why this claim fails: Equal batch sizes imply equal failure risk.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-24-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"同時失去多個故障域可能耗盡備援。","textEn":"Concurrent changes across fault domains can exhaust redundancy.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-24-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「分批節奏」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for batch pacing?","options":["每批數量相同便有相同故障風險。","在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。","先把「分批節奏」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Equal batch sizes imply equal failure risk.","Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains.","Tune the displayed batch pacing result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"同時失去多個故障域可能耗盡備援。 在三域圖中計算每批剩餘副本數。 因此「每批數量相同便有相同故障風險。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Concurrent changes across fault domains can exhaust redundancy. Count surviving replicas per batch across three domains. The alternative \"Equal batch sizes imply equal failure risk.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a368-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗證與復原","titleEn":"Verification and recovery","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「驗證與復原」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop verification and recovery through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a368-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-24"],"title":"修補證據：原理與架構","titleEn":"Patch evidence: principles and architecture","objective":"以「修補證據」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for patch evidence.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「修補證據」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：更新成功日誌還需與執行版本交叉核對。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for patch evidence. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Update-success logs require running-version cross-checks. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare installation records and post-restart versions. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare installation records and post-restart versions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：安裝成功訊息等於執行中已修補。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Installation success means the running process is patched. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「修補證據」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for patch evidence; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-25-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"更新成功日誌還需與執行版本交叉核對。","textEn":"Update-success logs require running-version cross-checks.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-25-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare installation records and post-restart versions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「修補證據」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for patch evidence?","options":["安裝成功訊息等於執行中已修補。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「修補證據」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","更新成功日誌還需與執行版本交叉核對。"],"optionsEn":["Installation success means the running process is patched.","One matching output proves patch evidence for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Update-success logs require running-version cross-checks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"更新成功日誌還需與執行版本交叉核對。 比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。 因此「安裝成功訊息等於執行中已修補。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Update-success logs require running-version cross-checks. Compare installation records and post-restart versions. The alternative \"Installation success means the running process is patched.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-25"],"title":"修補證據：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Patch evidence: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「修補證據」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for patch evidence.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。」；將結果與「更新成功日誌還需與執行版本交叉核對。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare installation records and post-restart versions. Compare results against: Update-success logs require running-version cross-checks. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare installation records and post-restart versions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：安裝成功訊息等於執行中已修補。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Installation success means the running process is patched. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「修補證據」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「安裝成功訊息等於執行中已修補。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for patch evidence; explain why this claim fails: Installation success means the running process is patched.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-26-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"更新成功日誌還需與執行版本交叉核對。","textEn":"Update-success logs require running-version cross-checks.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-26-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare installation records and post-restart versions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「修補證據」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for patch evidence?","options":["比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。","安裝成功訊息等於執行中已修補。","先把「修補證據」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Compare installation records and post-restart versions.","Installation success means the running process is patched.","Tune the displayed patch evidence result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"更新成功日誌還需與執行版本交叉核對。 比較假想安裝紀錄與重新啟動後版本。 因此「安裝成功訊息等於執行中已修補。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Update-success logs require running-version cross-checks. Compare installation records and post-restart versions. The alternative \"Installation success means the running process is patched.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-26"],"title":"例外到期：原理與架構","titleEn":"Exception expiry: principles and architecture","objective":"以「例外到期」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for exception expiry.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「例外到期」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：暫時例外需責任人、到期日與補償措施。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for exception expiry. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Temporary exceptions need owners, expiry and compensating controls. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：核准一次的例外永不需重新審查。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: One approval makes an exception permanent. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「例外到期」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for exception expiry; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-27-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"暫時例外需責任人、到期日與補償措施。","textEn":"Temporary exceptions need owners, expiry and compensating controls.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-27-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「例外到期」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for exception expiry?","options":["核准一次的例外永不需重新審查。","暫時例外需責任人、到期日與補償措施。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「例外到期」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["One approval makes an exception permanent.","Temporary exceptions need owners, expiry and compensating controls.","One matching output proves exception expiry for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"暫時例外需責任人、到期日與補償措施。 模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。 因此「核准一次的例外永不需重新審查。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Temporary exceptions need owners, expiry and compensating controls. Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. The alternative \"One approval makes an exception permanent.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-27"],"title":"例外到期：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Exception expiry: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「例外到期」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for exception expiry.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。」；將結果與「暫時例外需責任人、到期日與補償措施。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. Compare results against: Temporary exceptions need owners, expiry and compensating controls. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：核准一次的例外永不需重新審查。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: One approval makes an exception permanent. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「例外到期」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「核准一次的例外永不需重新審查。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for exception expiry; explain why this claim fails: One approval makes an exception permanent.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-28-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"暫時例外需責任人、到期日與補償措施。","textEn":"Temporary exceptions need owners, expiry and compensating controls.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-28-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「例外到期」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for exception expiry?","options":["核准一次的例外永不需重新審查。","先把「例外到期」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。"],"optionsEn":["One approval makes an exception permanent.","Tune the displayed exception expiry result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue."],"answer":2,"explanation":"暫時例外需責任人、到期日與補償措施。 模擬到期例外重新進入修補佇列。 因此「核准一次的例外永不需重新審查。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Temporary exceptions need owners, expiry and compensating controls. Return expired synthetic exceptions to the queue. The alternative \"One approval makes an exception permanent.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-28"],"title":"覆蓋分母：原理與架構","titleEn":"Coverage denominators: principles and architecture","objective":"以「覆蓋分母」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for coverage denominators.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「覆蓋分母」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：盤點遺漏會使修補率看似過高。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for coverage denominators. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Missing assets can inflate measured patch coverage. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：未知資產不應計入任何風險討論。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unknown assets need no risk consideration. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「覆蓋分母」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for coverage denominators; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-29-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"盤點遺漏會使修補率看似過高。","textEn":"Missing assets can inflate measured patch coverage.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-29-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「覆蓋分母」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for coverage denominators?","options":["盤點遺漏會使修補率看似過高。","未知資產不應計入任何風險討論。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「覆蓋分母」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Missing assets can inflate measured patch coverage.","Unknown assets need no risk consideration.","One matching output proves coverage denominators for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"盤點遺漏會使修補率看似過高。 以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。 因此「未知資產不應計入任何風險討論。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Missing assets can inflate measured patch coverage. Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. The alternative \"Unknown assets need no risk consideration.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-29"],"title":"覆蓋分母：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Coverage denominators: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「覆蓋分母」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for coverage denominators.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。」；將結果與「盤點遺漏會使修補率看似過高。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. Compare results against: Missing assets can inflate measured patch coverage. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：未知資產不應計入任何風險討論。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unknown assets need no risk consideration. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「覆蓋分母」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「未知資產不應計入任何風險討論。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for coverage denominators; explain why this claim fails: Unknown assets need no risk consideration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-30-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"盤點遺漏會使修補率看似過高。","textEn":"Missing assets can inflate measured patch coverage.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-30-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「覆蓋分母」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for coverage denominators?","options":["未知資產不應計入任何風險討論。","以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。","先把「覆蓋分母」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Unknown assets need no risk consideration.","Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets.","Tune the displayed coverage denominators result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"盤點遺漏會使修補率看似過高。 以本課算例重算納入遺漏後的覆蓋率。 因此「未知資產不應計入任何風險討論。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Missing assets can inflate measured patch coverage. Recalculate coverage after adding missing assets. The alternative \"Unknown assets need no risk consideration.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-30"],"title":"復原回顧：原理與架構","titleEn":"Recovery review: principles and architecture","objective":"以「復原回顧」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for recovery review.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「復原回顧」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：故障原因、版本與驗收證據應可重建。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for recovery review. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Causes, versions and acceptance evidence must be reconstructable. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：復原成功表示不需保留失敗資料。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Successful recovery removes the need to retain failure evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復原回顧」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for recovery review; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-31-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"故障原因、版本與驗收證據應可重建。","textEn":"Causes, versions and acceptance evidence must be reconstructable.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-31-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a368-v11-31-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 200 個受影響資產中完成 170 個，覆蓋率為 85%；若另有 10 個盤點遺漏資產，真正分母為 210，覆蓋率降至 80.95%。覆蓋不是風險消除率，例子不使用實際弱點或目標。","textEn":"In a synthetic inventory, 170 of 200 affected assets gives 85% coverage. Ten missing assets change the denominator to 210 and coverage to 80.95%. Coverage is not risk-elimination probability; no real vulnerability or target is used.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復原回顧」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for recovery review?","options":["復原成功表示不需保留失敗資料。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「復原回顧」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","故障原因、版本與驗收證據應可重建。"],"optionsEn":["Successful recovery removes the need to retain failure evidence.","One matching output proves recovery review for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Causes, versions and acceptance evidence must be reconstructable."],"answer":2,"explanation":"故障原因、版本與驗收證據應可重建。 用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。 因此「復原成功表示不需保留失敗資料。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Causes, versions and acceptance evidence must be reconstructable. Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. The alternative \"Successful recovery removes the need to retain failure evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a368-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"prerequisiteIds":["a368-v11-31"],"title":"復原回顧：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Recovery review: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「復原回顧」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for recovery review.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。」；將結果與「故障原因、版本與驗收證據應可重建。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. Compare results against: Causes, versions and acceptance evidence must be reconstructable. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：復原成功表示不需保留失敗資料。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Successful recovery removes the need to retain failure evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復原回顧」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「復原成功表示不需保留失敗資料。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for recovery review; explain why this claim fails: Successful recovery removes the need to retain failure evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a368-v11-32-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"故障原因、版本與驗收證據應可重建。","textEn":"Causes, versions and acceptance evidence must be reconstructable.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a368-v11-32-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a368-v11-32-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 200 個受影響資產中完成 170 個，覆蓋率為 85%；若另有 10 個盤點遺漏資產，真正分母為 210，覆蓋率降至 80.95%。覆蓋不是風險消除率，例子不使用實際弱點或目標。","textEn":"In a synthetic inventory, 170 of 200 affected assets gives 85% coverage. Ten missing assets change the denominator to 210 and coverage to 80.95%. Coverage is not risk-elimination probability; no real vulnerability or target is used.","sourceIds":["v11c-patch","v11c-patchcase"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復原回顧」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for recovery review?","options":["用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。","復原成功表示不需保留失敗資料。","先把「復原回顧」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline.","Successful recovery removes the need to retain failure evidence.","Tune the displayed recovery review result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"故障原因、版本與驗收證據應可重建。 用離線時間線重現失敗批次與回退決策。 因此「復原成功表示不需保留失敗資料。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Causes, versions and acceptance evidence must be reconstructable. Reconstruct a failed batch and rollback decision offline. The alternative \"Successful recovery removes the need to retain failure evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]}],"curriculumVersion":11,"scope":"公開原理的本地科教模擬與工程判讀。只使用自製、合成或明確授權的資料；不操作真實受害主機、他人帳號、工業控制或超算設施。數值不代表廠商規格或實測效能，完成課程不是專業資格、真實裝置操作經歷或生產部署認證。","scopeEn":"Local educational simulation and engineering interpretation of public principles. Use self-made, synthetic or explicitly licensed data only; do not operate real victim hosts, other accounts, industrial control or supercomputing facilities. Values are not product specifications or measured performance. Completion is not a qualification, real-equipment experience or production-deployment certification.","workedExample":{"title":"含假設的可重算工程例","titleEn":"Reproducible assumed engineering case","text":"假想 200 個受影響資產中完成 170 個，覆蓋率為 85%；若另有 10 個盤點遺漏資產，真正分母為 210，覆蓋率降至 80.95%。覆蓋不是風險消除率，例子不使用實際弱點或目標。","textEn":"In a synthetic inventory, 170 of 200 affected assets gives 85% coverage. Ten missing assets change the denominator to 210 and coverage to 80.95%. Coverage is not risk-elimination probability; no real vulnerability or target is used.","assumptions":"使用算例明列的單位、分佈、精度、拓撲與理想化條件；改變鄰接、位寬、取樣或系統邊界必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use the stated units, distributions, precision, topology and idealizations; recompute after changing adjacency, width, sampling or boundaries.","sourceScope":"作者獨立設定的假想數值例，非引用機構的實測資料；來源支援領域定義與架構。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen hypothetical values, not institutional measurements; sources support definitions and architecture."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["資產與風險","修補與相依","測試與部署","驗證與復原"],"labelsEn":["Assets and risk","Patches and dependencies","Testing and deployment","Verification and recovery"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a369","title":"資安事件應變演練","titleEn":"Cybersecurity incident-response exercises","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以偵測、遏止與業務復原的協調串連 16 個原創技術單元、32 步；涵蓋原理解析、架構圖、假想量化、合成資料實驗、競爭失效原因及可重算驗收。","summaryEn":"Sixteen original technical units and 32 tasks connect coordination of detection, containment and business recovery with principles, architectures, assumed calculations, synthetic experiments, competing failure causes and reproducible acceptance.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a369-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"準備與演練","titleEn":"Preparation and exercises","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「準備與演練」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop preparation and exercises through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a369-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"授權範圍：原理與架構","titleEn":"Exercise authority: principles and architecture","objective":"以「授權範圍」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for exercise authority.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「授權範圍」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：演練的系統、資料與處置許可權應事先確定。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for exercise authority. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Systems, data and response authority are defined before exercises. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有測試帳號都有正式系統處置權。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: All test accounts have production-response authority. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「授權範圍」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for exercise authority; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-01-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"演練的系統、資料與處置許可權應事先確定。","textEn":"Systems, data and response authority are defined before exercises.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-01-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a369-v11-01-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 12 起演練事件的偵測總時間 180 分鐘，平均 MTTD=15 分鐘；若一事件耗 90 分鐘，剩餘 11 起平均僅 8.18 分鐘。平均不能替代最慢事件與分位數，也不是服務保證。","textEn":"Twelve synthetic incidents detected over 180 minutes give mean MTTD=15 minutes. If one takes 90 minutes, the other eleven average 8.18 minutes. Report tails as well as means; these are not service guarantees.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「授權範圍」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for exercise authority?","options":["演練的系統、資料與處置許可權應事先確定。","所有測試帳號都有正式系統處置權。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「授權範圍」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Systems, data and response authority are defined before exercises.","All test accounts have production-response authority.","One matching output proves exercise authority for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"演練的系統、資料與處置許可權應事先確定。 以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。 因此「所有測試帳號都有正式系統處置權。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Systems, data and response authority are defined before exercises. Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. The alternative \"All test accounts have production-response authority.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-01"],"title":"授權範圍：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Exercise authority: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「授權範圍」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for exercise authority.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。」；將結果與「演練的系統、資料與處置許可權應事先確定。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. Compare results against: Systems, data and response authority are defined before exercises. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有測試帳號都有正式系統處置權。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: All test accounts have production-response authority. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「授權範圍」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「所有測試帳號都有正式系統處置權。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for exercise authority; explain why this claim fails: All test accounts have production-response authority.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-02-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"演練的系統、資料與處置許可權應事先確定。","textEn":"Systems, data and response authority are defined before exercises.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-02-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a369-v11-02-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 12 起演練事件的偵測總時間 180 分鐘，平均 MTTD=15 分鐘；若一事件耗 90 分鐘，剩餘 11 起平均僅 8.18 分鐘。平均不能替代最慢事件與分位數，也不是服務保證。","textEn":"Twelve synthetic incidents detected over 180 minutes give mean MTTD=15 minutes. If one takes 90 minutes, the other eleven average 8.18 minutes. Report tails as well as means; these are not service guarantees.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「授權範圍」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for exercise authority?","options":["所有測試帳號都有正式系統處置權。","以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。","先把「授權範圍」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["All test accounts have production-response authority.","Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment.","Tune the displayed exercise authority result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"演練的系統、資料與處置許可權應事先確定。 以玩具環境寫出允許和禁止的處置。 因此「所有測試帳號都有正式系統處置權。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Systems, data and response authority are defined before exercises. Specify allowed and prohibited actions in a toy environment. The alternative \"All test accounts have production-response authority.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-02"],"title":"角色交接：原理與架構","titleEn":"Role handoff: principles and architecture","objective":"以「角色交接」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for role handoff.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「角色交接」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：指揮、分析與業務決策需有交接介面。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for role handoff. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Command, analysis and business decisions need handoff interfaces. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：技術分析人員可自行代表所有業務決策。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Analysts automatically own all business decisions. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「角色交接」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for role handoff; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-03-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"指揮、分析與業務決策需有交接介面。","textEn":"Command, analysis and business decisions need handoff interfaces.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-03-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「角色交接」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for role handoff?","options":["技術分析人員可自行代表所有業務決策。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「角色交接」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","指揮、分析與業務決策需有交接介面。"],"optionsEn":["Analysts automatically own all business decisions.","One matching output proves role handoff for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Command, analysis and business decisions need handoff interfaces."],"answer":2,"explanation":"指揮、分析與業務決策需有交接介面。 畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。 因此「技術分析人員可自行代表所有業務決策。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Command, analysis and business decisions need handoff interfaces. Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. The alternative \"Analysts automatically own all business decisions.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-03"],"title":"角色交接：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Role handoff: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「角色交接」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for role handoff.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。」；將結果與「指揮、分析與業務決策需有交接介面。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. Compare results against: Command, analysis and business decisions need handoff interfaces. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：技術分析人員可自行代表所有業務決策。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Analysts automatically own all business decisions. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「角色交接」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「技術分析人員可自行代表所有業務決策。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for role handoff; explain why this claim fails: Analysts automatically own all business decisions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-04-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"指揮、分析與業務決策需有交接介面。","textEn":"Command, analysis and business decisions need handoff interfaces.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-04-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「角色交接」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for role handoff?","options":["畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。","技術分析人員可自行代表所有業務決策。","先把「角色交接」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident.","Analysts automatically own all business decisions.","Tune the displayed role handoff result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"指揮、分析與業務決策需有交接介面。 畫出合成事件的責任分工與批准路徑。 因此「技術分析人員可自行代表所有業務決策。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Command, analysis and business decisions need handoff interfaces. Map responsibility and approvals for a synthetic incident. The alternative \"Analysts automatically own all business decisions.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-04"],"title":"事件模型：原理與架構","titleEn":"Incident model: principles and architecture","objective":"以「事件模型」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for incident model.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「事件模型」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：訊號、事件與已確認事件不能混為一談。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for incident model. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Signals, events and confirmed incidents are distinct. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每個告警都是已確認入侵。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Every alert is a confirmed intrusion. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「事件模型」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for incident model; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-05-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"訊號、事件與已確認事件不能混為一談。","textEn":"Signals, events and confirmed incidents are distinct.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-05-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「事件模型」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for incident model?","options":["每個告警都是已確認入侵。","訊號、事件與已確認事件不能混為一談。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「事件模型」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Every alert is a confirmed intrusion.","Signals, events and confirmed incidents are distinct.","One matching output proves incident model for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"訊號、事件與已確認事件不能混為一談。 分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。 因此「每個告警都是已確認入侵。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Signals, events and confirmed incidents are distinct. Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. The alternative \"Every alert is a confirmed intrusion.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-05"],"title":"事件模型：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Incident model: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「事件模型」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for incident model.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。」；將結果與「訊號、事件與已確認事件不能混為一談。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. Compare results against: Signals, events and confirmed incidents are distinct. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每個告警都是已確認入侵。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Every alert is a confirmed intrusion. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「事件模型」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「每個告警都是已確認入侵。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for incident model; explain why this claim fails: Every alert is a confirmed intrusion.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-06-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"訊號、事件與已確認事件不能混為一談。","textEn":"Signals, events and confirmed incidents are distinct.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-06-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「事件模型」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for incident model?","options":["每個告警都是已確認入侵。","先把「事件模型」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。"],"optionsEn":["Every alert is a confirmed intrusion.","Tune the displayed incident model result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs."],"answer":2,"explanation":"訊號、事件與已確認事件不能混為一談。 分類本地產生的正常與異常日誌。 因此「每個告警都是已確認入侵。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Signals, events and confirmed incidents are distinct. Classify locally generated normal and abnormal logs. The alternative \"Every alert is a confirmed intrusion.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-06"],"title":"演練注入：原理與架構","titleEn":"Exercise injects: principles and architecture","objective":"以「演練注入」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for exercise injects.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「演練注入」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：注入情境需分開預期行為與不可預知分支。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for exercise injects. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Injects distinguish expected behavior and uncertain branches. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：演練指令碼完全成功便代表所有事件可處理。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A successful script proves all incidents are manageable. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「演練注入」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for exercise injects; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-07-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"注入情境需分開預期行為與不可預知分支。","textEn":"Injects distinguish expected behavior and uncertain branches.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-07-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「演練注入」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for exercise injects?","options":["注入情境需分開預期行為與不可預知分支。","演練指令碼完全成功便代表所有事件可處理。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「演練注入」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Injects distinguish expected behavior and uncertain branches.","A successful script proves all incidents are manageable.","One matching output proves exercise injects for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"注入情境需分開預期行為與不可預知分支。 設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。 因此「演練指令碼完全成功便代表所有事件可處理。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Injects distinguish expected behavior and uncertain branches. Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. The alternative \"A successful script proves all incidents are manageable.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-07"],"title":"演練注入：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Exercise injects: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「演練注入」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for exercise injects.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。」；將結果與「注入情境需分開預期行為與不可預知分支。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. Compare results against: Injects distinguish expected behavior and uncertain branches. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：演練指令碼完全成功便代表所有事件可處理。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A successful script proves all incidents are manageable. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「演練注入」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「演練指令碼完全成功便代表所有事件可處理。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for exercise injects; explain why this claim fails: A successful script proves all incidents are manageable.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-08-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"注入情境需分開預期行為與不可預知分支。","textEn":"Injects distinguish expected behavior and uncertain branches.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-08-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「演練注入」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for exercise injects?","options":["演練指令碼完全成功便代表所有事件可處理。","設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。","先把「演練注入」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A successful script proves all incidents are manageable.","Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems.","Tune the displayed exercise injects result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"注入情境需分開預期行為與不可預知分支。 設計假想服務中斷而不執行真實攻擊。 因此「演練指令碼完全成功便代表所有事件可處理。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Injects distinguish expected behavior and uncertain branches. Design fictional service disruption without attacking systems. The alternative \"A successful script proves all incidents are manageable.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a369-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"辨識與判斷","titleEn":"Identification and decisions","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「辨識與判斷」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop identification and decisions through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a369-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-08"],"title":"時間基準：原理與架構","titleEn":"Time references: principles and architecture","objective":"以「時間基準」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for time references.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「時間基準」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：不同日誌時鐘誤差會改變事件排序。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for time references. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Clock errors across logs can change event ordering. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：排序文字時間戳就保證因果順序。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Sorting textual timestamps guarantees causality. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「時間基準」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for time references; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-09-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"不同日誌時鐘誤差會改變事件排序。","textEn":"Clock errors across logs can change event ordering.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-09-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「時間基準」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for time references?","options":["排序文字時間戳就保證因果順序。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「時間基準」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","不同日誌時鐘誤差會改變事件排序。"],"optionsEn":["Sorting textual timestamps guarantees causality.","One matching output proves time references for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Clock errors across logs can change event ordering."],"answer":2,"explanation":"不同日誌時鐘誤差會改變事件排序。 加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。 因此「排序文字時間戳就保證因果順序。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Clock errors across logs can change event ordering. Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. The alternative \"Sorting textual timestamps guarantees causality.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-09"],"title":"時間基準：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Time references: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「時間基準」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for time references.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。」；將結果與「不同日誌時鐘誤差會改變事件排序。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. Compare results against: Clock errors across logs can change event ordering. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：排序文字時間戳就保證因果順序。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Sorting textual timestamps guarantees causality. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「時間基準」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「排序文字時間戳就保證因果順序。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for time references; explain why this claim fails: Sorting textual timestamps guarantees causality.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-10-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"不同日誌時鐘誤差會改變事件排序。","textEn":"Clock errors across logs can change event ordering.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-10-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「時間基準」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for time references?","options":["加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。","排序文字時間戳就保證因果順序。","先把「時間基準」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets.","Sorting textual timestamps guarantees causality.","Tune the displayed time references result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"不同日誌時鐘誤差會改變事件排序。 加入已知偏差後重建帶誤差範圍的時間線。 因此「排序文字時間戳就保證因果順序。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Clock errors across logs can change event ordering. Reconstruct a timeline after adding known clock offsets. The alternative \"Sorting textual timestamps guarantees causality.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-10"],"title":"證據可信：原理與架構","titleEn":"Evidence confidence: principles and architecture","objective":"以「證據可信」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for evidence confidence.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「證據可信」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：來源、完整性與觀測缺口共同影響結論。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for evidence confidence. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Provenance, integrity and blind spots affect conclusions. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：兩條重複日誌便是兩個獨立證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Duplicate logs are independent evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「證據可信」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for evidence confidence; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-11-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"來源、完整性與觀測缺口共同影響結論。","textEn":"Provenance, integrity and blind spots affect conclusions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-11-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「證據可信」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for evidence confidence?","options":["兩條重複日誌便是兩個獨立證據。","來源、完整性與觀測缺口共同影響結論。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「證據可信」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Duplicate logs are independent evidence.","Provenance, integrity and blind spots affect conclusions.","One matching output proves evidence confidence for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"來源、完整性與觀測缺口共同影響結論。 給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。 因此「兩條重複日誌便是兩個獨立證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Provenance, integrity and blind spots affect conclusions. Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. The alternative \"Duplicate logs are independent evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-11"],"title":"證據可信：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Evidence confidence: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「證據可信」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for evidence confidence.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。」；將結果與「來源、完整性與觀測缺口共同影響結論。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. Compare results against: Provenance, integrity and blind spots affect conclusions. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：兩條重複日誌便是兩個獨立證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Duplicate logs are independent evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「證據可信」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「兩條重複日誌便是兩個獨立證據。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for evidence confidence; explain why this claim fails: Duplicate logs are independent evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-12-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"來源、完整性與觀測缺口共同影響結論。","textEn":"Provenance, integrity and blind spots affect conclusions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-12-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「證據可信」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for evidence confidence?","options":["兩條重複日誌便是兩個獨立證據。","先把「證據可信」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。"],"optionsEn":["Duplicate logs are independent evidence.","Tune the displayed evidence confidence result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations."],"answer":2,"explanation":"來源、完整性與觀測缺口共同影響結論。 給每項合成觀測標示可信度與缺口。 因此「兩條重複日誌便是兩個獨立證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Provenance, integrity and blind spots affect conclusions. Label confidence and gaps for synthetic observations. The alternative \"Duplicate logs are independent evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-12"],"title":"事件分級：原理與架構","titleEn":"Incident severity: principles and architecture","objective":"以「事件分級」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for incident severity.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「事件分級」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：分級需同時考慮影響與確定度。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for incident severity. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Severity accounts for impact and confidence. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有確定度最高事件值得處置。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Only the most certain incident merits action. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「事件分級」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for incident severity; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-13-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"分級需同時考慮影響與確定度。","textEn":"Severity accounts for impact and confidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-13-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「事件分級」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for incident severity?","options":["分級需同時考慮影響與確定度。","只有確定度最高事件值得處置。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「事件分級」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Severity accounts for impact and confidence.","Only the most certain incident merits action.","One matching output proves incident severity for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"分級需同時考慮影響與確定度。 比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。 因此「只有確定度最高事件值得處置。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Severity accounts for impact and confidence. Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. The alternative \"Only the most certain incident merits action.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-13"],"title":"事件分級：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Incident severity: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「事件分級」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for incident severity.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。」；將結果與「分級需同時考慮影響與確定度。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. Compare results against: Severity accounts for impact and confidence. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有確定度最高事件值得處置。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Only the most certain incident merits action. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「事件分級」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「只有確定度最高事件值得處置。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for incident severity; explain why this claim fails: Only the most certain incident merits action.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-14-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"分級需同時考慮影響與確定度。","textEn":"Severity accounts for impact and confidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-14-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「事件分級」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for incident severity?","options":["只有確定度最高事件值得處置。","比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。","先把「事件分級」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Only the most certain incident merits action.","Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases.","Tune the displayed incident severity result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"分級需同時考慮影響與確定度。 比較高影響低確定度與低影響高確定度。 因此「只有確定度最高事件值得處置。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Severity accounts for impact and confidence. Compare high-impact uncertain and low-impact certain cases. The alternative \"Only the most certain incident merits action.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-14"],"title":"競爭解釋：原理與架構","titleEn":"Competing hypotheses: principles and architecture","objective":"以「競爭解釋」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for competing hypotheses.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「競爭解釋」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：異常可能來自故障、變更或濫用。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for competing hypotheses. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Anomalies may result from failures, changes or misuse. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：異常行為只有惡意活動一種原因。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Malicious activity is the only cause of anomalies. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「競爭解釋」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for competing hypotheses; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-15-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"異常可能來自故障、變更或濫用。","textEn":"Anomalies may result from failures, changes or misuse.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-15-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「競爭解釋」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for competing hypotheses?","options":["異常行為只有惡意活動一種原因。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「競爭解釋」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","異常可能來自故障、變更或濫用。"],"optionsEn":["Malicious activity is the only cause of anomalies.","One matching output proves competing hypotheses for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Anomalies may result from failures, changes or misuse."],"answer":2,"explanation":"異常可能來自故障、變更或濫用。 為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。 因此「異常行為只有惡意活動一種原因。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Anomalies may result from failures, changes or misuse. Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. The alternative \"Malicious activity is the only cause of anomalies.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-15"],"title":"競爭解釋：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Competing hypotheses: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「競爭解釋」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for competing hypotheses.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。」；將結果與「異常可能來自故障、變更或濫用。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. Compare results against: Anomalies may result from failures, changes or misuse. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：異常行為只有惡意活動一種原因。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Malicious activity is the only cause of anomalies. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「競爭解釋」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「異常行為只有惡意活動一種原因。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for competing hypotheses; explain why this claim fails: Malicious activity is the only cause of anomalies.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-16-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"異常可能來自故障、變更或濫用。","textEn":"Anomalies may result from failures, changes or misuse.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-16-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「競爭解釋」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for competing hypotheses?","options":["為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。","異常行為只有惡意活動一種原因。","先把「競爭解釋」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike.","Malicious activity is the only cause of anomalies.","Tune the displayed competing hypotheses result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"異常可能來自故障、變更或濫用。 為玩具登入尖峰提出兩個非攻擊解釋。 因此「異常行為只有惡意活動一種原因。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Anomalies may result from failures, changes or misuse. Propose two nonattack explanations for a toy login spike. The alternative \"Malicious activity is the only cause of anomalies.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a369-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"遏止與復原","titleEn":"Containment and recovery","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「遏止與復原」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop containment and recovery through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a369-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-16"],"title":"遏止代價：原理與架構","titleEn":"Containment cost: principles and architecture","objective":"以「遏止代價」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for containment cost.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「遏止代價」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：隔離能限制擴散但可能中斷關鍵依賴。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for containment cost. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Isolation limits propagation but may break critical dependencies. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：隔離越多裝置業務損失必然越小。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: More isolation necessarily reduces business loss. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「遏止代價」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for containment cost; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-17-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"隔離能限制擴散但可能中斷關鍵依賴。","textEn":"Isolation limits propagation but may break critical dependencies.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-17-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「遏止代價」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for containment cost?","options":["隔離越多裝置業務損失必然越小。","隔離能限制擴散但可能中斷關鍵依賴。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「遏止代價」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["More isolation necessarily reduces business loss.","Isolation limits propagation but may break critical dependencies.","One matching output proves containment cost for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"隔離能限制擴散但可能中斷關鍵依賴。 在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。 因此「隔離越多裝置業務損失必然越小。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Isolation limits propagation but may break critical dependencies. Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. The alternative \"More isolation necessarily reduces business loss.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-17"],"title":"遏止代價：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Containment cost: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「遏止代價」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for containment cost.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。」；將結果與「隔離能限制擴散但可能中斷關鍵依賴。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. Compare results against: Isolation limits propagation but may break critical dependencies. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：隔離越多裝置業務損失必然越小。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: More isolation necessarily reduces business loss. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「遏止代價」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「隔離越多裝置業務損失必然越小。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for containment cost; explain why this claim fails: More isolation necessarily reduces business loss.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-18-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"隔離能限制擴散但可能中斷關鍵依賴。","textEn":"Isolation limits propagation but may break critical dependencies.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-18-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「遏止代價」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for containment cost?","options":["隔離越多裝置業務損失必然越小。","先把「遏止代價」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。"],"optionsEn":["More isolation necessarily reduces business loss.","Tune the displayed containment cost result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隔離能限制擴散但可能中斷關鍵依賴。 在離線相依圖預測隔離對業務的影響。 因此「隔離越多裝置業務損失必然越小。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Isolation limits propagation but may break critical dependencies. Predict isolation impact on an offline dependency graph. The alternative \"More isolation necessarily reduces business loss.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-18"],"title":"證據與復原：原理與架構","titleEn":"Evidence and recovery: principles and architecture","objective":"以「證據與復原」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for evidence and recovery.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「證據與復原」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：急速復原可能改寫尚未儲存的證據。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for evidence and recovery. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Rapid recovery can overwrite unpreserved evidence. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：重新啟動不可能影響可用證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Restarting cannot affect available evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「證據與復原」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for evidence and recovery; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-19-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"急速復原可能改寫尚未儲存的證據。","textEn":"Rapid recovery can overwrite unpreserved evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-19-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「證據與復原」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for evidence and recovery?","options":["急速復原可能改寫尚未儲存的證據。","重新啟動不可能影響可用證據。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「證據與復原」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Rapid recovery can overwrite unpreserved evidence.","Restarting cannot affect available evidence.","One matching output proves evidence and recovery for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"急速復原可能改寫尚未儲存的證據。 比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。 因此「重新啟動不可能影響可用證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Rapid recovery can overwrite unpreserved evidence. Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. The alternative \"Restarting cannot affect available evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-19"],"title":"證據與復原：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Evidence and recovery: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「證據與復原」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for evidence and recovery.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。」；將結果與「急速復原可能改寫尚未儲存的證據。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. Compare results against: Rapid recovery can overwrite unpreserved evidence. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：重新啟動不可能影響可用證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Restarting cannot affect available evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「證據與復原」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「重新啟動不可能影響可用證據。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for evidence and recovery; explain why this claim fails: Restarting cannot affect available evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-20-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"急速復原可能改寫尚未儲存的證據。","textEn":"Rapid recovery can overwrite unpreserved evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-20-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「證據與復原」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for evidence and recovery?","options":["重新啟動不可能影響可用證據。","比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。","先把「證據與復原」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Restarting cannot affect available evidence.","Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention.","Tune the displayed evidence and recovery result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"急速復原可能改寫尚未儲存的證據。 比較先取樣與先重啟的資料保留情境。 因此「重新啟動不可能影響可用證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Rapid recovery can overwrite unpreserved evidence. Compare sampling-first and restart-first evidence retention. The alternative \"Restarting cannot affect available evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-20"],"title":"復原順序：原理與架構","titleEn":"Recovery ordering: principles and architecture","objective":"以「復原順序」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for recovery ordering.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「復原順序」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：相依服務需依健康與信任條件依序復原。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for recovery ordering. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Dependencies restore according to health and trust conditions. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有節點同時恢復必然最快且安全。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Restoring all nodes together is always fastest and safest. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復原順序」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for recovery ordering; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-21-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"相依服務需依健康與信任條件依序復原。","textEn":"Dependencies restore according to health and trust conditions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-21-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復原順序」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for recovery ordering?","options":["所有節點同時恢復必然最快且安全。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「復原順序」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","相依服務需依健康與信任條件依序復原。"],"optionsEn":["Restoring all nodes together is always fastest and safest.","One matching output proves recovery ordering for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Dependencies restore according to health and trust conditions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"相依服務需依健康與信任條件依序復原。 用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。 因此「所有節點同時恢復必然最快且安全。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Dependencies restore according to health and trust conditions. Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. The alternative \"Restoring all nodes together is always fastest and safest.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-21"],"title":"復原順序：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Recovery ordering: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「復原順序」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for recovery ordering.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。」；將結果與「相依服務需依健康與信任條件依序復原。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. Compare results against: Dependencies restore according to health and trust conditions. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有節點同時恢復必然最快且安全。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Restoring all nodes together is always fastest and safest. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復原順序」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「所有節點同時恢復必然最快且安全。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for recovery ordering; explain why this claim fails: Restoring all nodes together is always fastest and safest.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-22-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"相依服務需依健康與信任條件依序復原。","textEn":"Dependencies restore according to health and trust conditions.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-22-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復原順序」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for recovery ordering?","options":["用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。","所有節點同時恢復必然最快且安全。","先把「復原順序」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph.","Restoring all nodes together is always fastest and safest.","Tune the displayed recovery ordering result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"相依服務需依健康與信任條件依序復原。 用玩具服務圖排序身分、資料與應用層。 因此「所有節點同時恢復必然最快且安全。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Dependencies restore according to health and trust conditions. Order identity, data and applications on a toy graph. The alternative \"Restoring all nodes together is always fastest and safest.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-22"],"title":"復原驗證：原理與架構","titleEn":"Recovery validation: principles and architecture","objective":"以「復原驗證」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for recovery validation.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「復原驗證」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：能回應請求不能證明資料正確及風險解除。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for recovery validation. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Serving requests does not prove correct data or removed risk. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：HTTP 成功狀態即可結案。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: An HTTP success status closes the incident. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復原驗證」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for recovery validation; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-23-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"能回應請求不能證明資料正確及風險解除。","textEn":"Serving requests does not prove correct data or removed risk.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-23-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復原驗證」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for recovery validation?","options":["HTTP 成功狀態即可結案。","能回應請求不能證明資料正確及風險解除。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「復原驗證」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["An HTTP success status closes the incident.","Serving requests does not prove correct data or removed risk.","One matching output proves recovery validation for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"能回應請求不能證明資料正確及風險解除。 比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。 因此「HTTP 成功狀態即可結案。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Serving requests does not prove correct data or removed risk. Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. The alternative \"An HTTP success status closes the incident.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-23"],"title":"復原驗證：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Recovery validation: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「復原驗證」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for recovery validation.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。」；將結果與「能回應請求不能證明資料正確及風險解除。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. Compare results against: Serving requests does not prove correct data or removed risk. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：HTTP 成功狀態即可結案。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: An HTTP success status closes the incident. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復原驗證」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「HTTP 成功狀態即可結案。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for recovery validation; explain why this claim fails: An HTTP success status closes the incident.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-24-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"能回應請求不能證明資料正確及風險解除。","textEn":"Serving requests does not prove correct data or removed risk.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-24-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復原驗證」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for recovery validation?","options":["HTTP 成功狀態即可結案。","先把「復原驗證」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。"],"optionsEn":["An HTTP success status closes the incident.","Tune the displayed recovery validation result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline."],"answer":2,"explanation":"能回應請求不能證明資料正確及風險解除。 比較功能、資料與安全三類離線驗收。 因此「HTTP 成功狀態即可結案。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Serving requests does not prove correct data or removed risk. Compare functional, data and security acceptance offline. The alternative \"An HTTP success status closes the incident.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a369-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"學習與驗收","titleEn":"Learning and acceptance","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「學習與驗收」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop learning and acceptance through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a369-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-24"],"title":"通知紀錄：原理與架構","titleEn":"Communication records: principles and architecture","objective":"以「通知紀錄」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for communication records.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「通知紀錄」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：通知應依已確認事實、時點與責任角色。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for communication records. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Communication follows confirmed facts, timing and accountable roles. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：未確認推測可直接當作正式事件結論。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unconfirmed speculation can be a formal conclusion. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「通知紀錄」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for communication records; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-25-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"通知應依已確認事實、時點與責任角色。","textEn":"Communication follows confirmed facts, timing and accountable roles.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-25-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「通知紀錄」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for communication records?","options":["通知應依已確認事實、時點與責任角色。","未確認推測可直接當作正式事件結論。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「通知紀錄」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Communication follows confirmed facts, timing and accountable roles.","Unconfirmed speculation can be a formal conclusion.","One matching output proves communication records for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"通知應依已確認事實、時點與責任角色。 撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。 因此「未確認推測可直接當作正式事件結論。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Communication follows confirmed facts, timing and accountable roles. Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. The alternative \"Unconfirmed speculation can be a formal conclusion.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-25"],"title":"通知紀錄：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Communication records: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「通知紀錄」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for communication records.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。」；將結果與「通知應依已確認事實、時點與責任角色。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. Compare results against: Communication follows confirmed facts, timing and accountable roles. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：未確認推測可直接當作正式事件結論。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unconfirmed speculation can be a formal conclusion. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「通知紀錄」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「未確認推測可直接當作正式事件結論。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for communication records; explain why this claim fails: Unconfirmed speculation can be a formal conclusion.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-26-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"通知應依已確認事實、時點與責任角色。","textEn":"Communication follows confirmed facts, timing and accountable roles.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-26-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「通知紀錄」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for communication records?","options":["未確認推測可直接當作正式事件結論。","撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。","先把「通知紀錄」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Unconfirmed speculation can be a formal conclusion.","Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked.","Tune the displayed communication records result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"通知應依已確認事實、時點與責任角色。 撰寫匿名演練摘要並標示未證實項。 因此「未確認推測可直接當作正式事件結論。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Communication follows confirmed facts, timing and accountable roles. Write an anonymous exercise brief with unconfirmed items marked. The alternative \"Unconfirmed speculation can be a formal conclusion.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-26"],"title":"偵測指標：原理與架構","titleEn":"Detection metrics: principles and architecture","objective":"以「偵測指標」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for detection metrics.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「偵測指標」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：平均偵測時間可能隱藏長尾事件。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for detection metrics. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Mean detection time can hide long-tail incidents. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：平均改善便代表每個事件都改善。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: An improved average means every incident improved. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「偵測指標」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for detection metrics; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-27-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"平均偵測時間可能隱藏長尾事件。","textEn":"Mean detection time can hide long-tail incidents.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-27-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「偵測指標」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for detection metrics?","options":["平均改善便代表每個事件都改善。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「偵測指標」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","平均偵測時間可能隱藏長尾事件。"],"optionsEn":["An improved average means every incident improved.","One matching output proves detection metrics for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Mean detection time can hide long-tail incidents."],"answer":2,"explanation":"平均偵測時間可能隱藏長尾事件。 以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。 因此「平均改善便代表每個事件都改善。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Mean detection time can hide long-tail incidents. Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. The alternative \"An improved average means every incident improved.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-27"],"title":"偵測指標：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Detection metrics: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「偵測指標」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for detection metrics.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。」；將結果與「平均偵測時間可能隱藏長尾事件。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. Compare results against: Mean detection time can hide long-tail incidents. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：平均改善便代表每個事件都改善。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: An improved average means every incident improved. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「偵測指標」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「平均改善便代表每個事件都改善。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for detection metrics; explain why this claim fails: An improved average means every incident improved.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-28-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"平均偵測時間可能隱藏長尾事件。","textEn":"Mean detection time can hide long-tail incidents.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-28-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「偵測指標」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for detection metrics?","options":["以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。","平均改善便代表每個事件都改善。","先把「偵測指標」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example.","An improved average means every incident improved.","Tune the displayed detection metrics result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"平均偵測時間可能隱藏長尾事件。 以本課算例另列最慢值及事件數。 因此「平均改善便代表每個事件都改善。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Mean detection time can hide long-tail incidents. Report the slowest value and sample size alongside the example. The alternative \"An improved average means every incident improved.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-28"],"title":"復盤因果：原理與架構","titleEn":"Review causality: principles and architecture","objective":"以「復盤因果」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for review causality.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「復盤因果」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：復盤需分開時間相關與可驗證原因。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for review causality. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Reviews separate temporal association from verified causes. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：故障後最後一個變更必然是原因。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: The last preceding change is necessarily the cause. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復盤因果」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for review causality; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-29-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"復盤需分開時間相關與可驗證原因。","textEn":"Reviews separate temporal association from verified causes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-29-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復盤因果」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for review causality?","options":["故障後最後一個變更必然是原因。","復盤需分開時間相關與可驗證原因。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「復盤因果」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["The last preceding change is necessarily the cause.","Reviews separate temporal association from verified causes.","One matching output proves review causality for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"復盤需分開時間相關與可驗證原因。 在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。 因此「故障後最後一個變更必然是原因。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reviews separate temporal association from verified causes. Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. The alternative \"The last preceding change is necessarily the cause.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-29"],"title":"復盤因果：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Review causality: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「復盤因果」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for review causality.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。」；將結果與「復盤需分開時間相關與可驗證原因。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. Compare results against: Reviews separate temporal association from verified causes. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：故障後最後一個變更必然是原因。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: The last preceding change is necessarily the cause. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「復盤因果」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「故障後最後一個變更必然是原因。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for review causality; explain why this claim fails: The last preceding change is necessarily the cause.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-30-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"復盤需分開時間相關與可驗證原因。","textEn":"Reviews separate temporal association from verified causes.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-30-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「復盤因果」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for review causality?","options":["故障後最後一個變更必然是原因。","先把「復盤因果」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。"],"optionsEn":["The last preceding change is necessarily the cause.","Tune the displayed review causality result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline."],"answer":2,"explanation":"復盤需分開時間相關與可驗證原因。 在合成時間線標示哪些因果仍需驗證。 因此「故障後最後一個變更必然是原因。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reviews separate temporal association from verified causes. Mark causal claims still needing evidence on a synthetic timeline. The alternative \"The last preceding change is necessarily the cause.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-30"],"title":"修正追蹤：原理與架構","titleEn":"Corrective-action tracking: principles and architecture","objective":"以「修正追蹤」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for corrective-action tracking.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「修正追蹤」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：改善事項需負責人、到期與重演證據。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for corrective-action tracking. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Actions need owners, deadlines and re-exercise evidence. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：寫下改善建議便等於風險已降低。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Writing a recommendation means risk is reduced. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「修正追蹤」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for corrective-action tracking; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-31-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"改善事項需負責人、到期與重演證據。","textEn":"Actions need owners, deadlines and re-exercise evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-31-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a369-v11-31-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 12 起演練事件的偵測總時間 180 分鐘，平均 MTTD=15 分鐘；若一事件耗 90 分鐘，剩餘 11 起平均僅 8.18 分鐘。平均不能替代最慢事件與分位數，也不是服務保證。","textEn":"Twelve synthetic incidents detected over 180 minutes give mean MTTD=15 minutes. If one takes 90 minutes, the other eleven average 8.18 minutes. Report tails as well as means; these are not service guarantees.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「修正追蹤」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for corrective-action tracking?","options":["改善事項需負責人、到期與重演證據。","寫下改善建議便等於風險已降低。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「修正追蹤」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Actions need owners, deadlines and re-exercise evidence.","Writing a recommendation means risk is reduced.","One matching output proves corrective-action tracking for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"改善事項需負責人、到期與重演證據。 將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。 因此「寫下改善建議便等於風險已降低。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Actions need owners, deadlines and re-exercise evidence. Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. The alternative \"Writing a recommendation means risk is reduced.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a369-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"prerequisiteIds":["a369-v11-31"],"title":"修正追蹤：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Corrective-action tracking: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「修正追蹤」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for corrective-action tracking.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。」；將結果與「改善事項需負責人、到期與重演證據。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. Compare results against: Actions need owners, deadlines and re-exercise evidence. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：寫下改善建議便等於風險已降低。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Writing a recommendation means risk is reduced. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「修正追蹤」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「寫下改善建議便等於風險已降低。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for corrective-action tracking; explain why this claim fails: Writing a recommendation means risk is reduced.","knowledge":[{"id":"a369-v11-32-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"改善事項需負責人、到期與重演證據。","textEn":"Actions need owners, deadlines and re-exercise evidence.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a369-v11-32-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a369-v11-32-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 12 起演練事件的偵測總時間 180 分鐘，平均 MTTD=15 分鐘；若一事件耗 90 分鐘，剩餘 11 起平均僅 8.18 分鐘。平均不能替代最慢事件與分位數，也不是服務保證。","textEn":"Twelve synthetic incidents detected over 180 minutes give mean MTTD=15 minutes. If one takes 90 minutes, the other eleven average 8.18 minutes. Report tails as well as means; these are not service guarantees.","sourceIds":["v4-related-f53ed62dd159","v11c-forensic"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「修正追蹤」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for corrective-action tracking?","options":["寫下改善建議便等於風險已降低。","將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。","先把「修正追蹤」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Writing a recommendation means risk is reduced.","Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise.","Tune the displayed corrective-action tracking result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"改善事項需負責人、到期與重演證據。 將一項流程缺口轉成可觀察的再次演練。 因此「寫下改善建議便等於風險已降低。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Actions need owners, deadlines and re-exercise evidence. Turn a process gap into an observable repeat exercise. The alternative \"Writing a recommendation means risk is reduced.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]}],"curriculumVersion":11,"scope":"公開原理的本地科教模擬與工程判讀。只使用自製、合成或明確授權的資料；不操作真實受害主機、他人帳號、工業控制或超算設施。數值不代表廠商規格或實測效能，完成課程不是專業資格、真實裝置操作經歷或生產部署認證。","scopeEn":"Local educational simulation and engineering interpretation of public principles. Use self-made, synthetic or explicitly licensed data only; do not operate real victim hosts, other accounts, industrial control or supercomputing facilities. Values are not product specifications or measured performance. Completion is not a qualification, real-equipment experience or production-deployment certification.","workedExample":{"title":"含假設的可重算工程例","titleEn":"Reproducible assumed engineering case","text":"假想 12 起演練事件的偵測總時間 180 分鐘，平均 MTTD=15 分鐘；若一事件耗 90 分鐘，剩餘 11 起平均僅 8.18 分鐘。平均不能替代最慢事件與分位數，也不是服務保證。","textEn":"Twelve synthetic incidents detected over 180 minutes give mean MTTD=15 minutes. If one takes 90 minutes, the other eleven average 8.18 minutes. Report tails as well as means; these are not service guarantees.","assumptions":"使用算例明列的單位、分佈、精度、拓撲與理想化條件；改變鄰接、位寬、取樣或系統邊界必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use the stated units, distributions, precision, topology and idealizations; recompute after changing adjacency, width, sampling or boundaries.","sourceScope":"作者獨立設定的假想數值例，非引用機構的實測資料；來源支援領域定義與架構。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen hypothetical values, not institutional measurements; sources support definitions and architecture."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["準備與演練","辨識與判斷","遏止與復原","學習與驗收"],"labelsEn":["Preparation and exercises","Identification and decisions","Containment and recovery","Learning and acceptance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a370","title":"數位鑑識證據保全","titleEn":"Digital-forensics evidence preservation","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以可追溯、完整且可重現的數位證據串連 16 個原創技術單元、32 步；涵蓋原理解析、架構圖、假想量化、合成資料實驗、競爭失效原因及可重算驗收。","summaryEn":"Sixteen original technical units and 32 tasks connect traceable, intact and reproducible digital evidence with principles, architectures, assumed calculations, synthetic experiments, competing failure causes and reproducible acceptance.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a370-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"授權與識別","titleEn":"Authority and identification","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「授權與識別」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop authority and identification through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a370-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"合法與任務範圍：原理與架構","titleEn":"Authority and scope: principles and architecture","objective":"以「合法與任務範圍」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for authority and scope.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「合法與任務範圍」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：證據接觸需限定資料、目的與處理授權。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for authority and scope. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Evidence access is bounded by data, purpose and authority. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：擁有技術能力就代表取得資料的授權。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Technical ability implies authority to obtain data. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「合法與任務範圍」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for authority and scope; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-01-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"證據接觸需限定資料、目的與處理授權。","textEn":"Evidence access is bounded by data, purpose and authority.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-01-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a370-v11-01-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"一份假想 64 GiB 映像以 250 MiB/s 讀取，理想單次時間為 64×1024/250=262.14 秒；若採集後再完整驗證讀取一次，最低讀取時間約 524.29 秒。未含 I/O 競爭、寫入與工具開銷。","textEn":"A synthetic 64 GiB image read at 250 MiB/s takes 262.14 seconds ideally. One further full verification read brings minimum reading time to 524.29 seconds, excluding contention, writes and tool overhead.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「合法與任務範圍」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for authority and scope?","options":["擁有技術能力就代表取得資料的授權。","證據接觸需限定資料、目的與處理授權。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「合法與任務範圍」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Technical ability implies authority to obtain data.","Evidence access is bounded by data, purpose and authority.","One matching output proves authority and scope for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"證據接觸需限定資料、目的與處理授權。 用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。 因此「擁有技術能力就代表取得資料的授權。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Evidence access is bounded by data, purpose and authority. Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. The alternative \"Technical ability implies authority to obtain data.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-01"],"title":"合法與任務範圍：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Authority and scope: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「合法與任務範圍」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for authority and scope.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。」；將結果與「證據接觸需限定資料、目的與處理授權。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. Compare results against: Evidence access is bounded by data, purpose and authority. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：擁有技術能力就代表取得資料的授權。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Technical ability implies authority to obtain data. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「合法與任務範圍」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「擁有技術能力就代表取得資料的授權。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for authority and scope; explain why this claim fails: Technical ability implies authority to obtain data.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-02-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"證據接觸需限定資料、目的與處理授權。","textEn":"Evidence access is bounded by data, purpose and authority.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-02-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a370-v11-02-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"一份假想 64 GiB 映像以 250 MiB/s 讀取，理想單次時間為 64×1024/250=262.14 秒；若採集後再完整驗證讀取一次，最低讀取時間約 524.29 秒。未含 I/O 競爭、寫入與工具開銷。","textEn":"A synthetic 64 GiB image read at 250 MiB/s takes 262.14 seconds ideally. One further full verification read brings minimum reading time to 524.29 seconds, excluding contention, writes and tool overhead.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「合法與任務範圍」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for authority and scope?","options":["擁有技術能力就代表取得資料的授權。","先把「合法與任務範圍」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。"],"optionsEn":["Technical ability implies authority to obtain data.","Tune the displayed authority and scope result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Define analyzable areas on self-created test files."],"answer":2,"explanation":"證據接觸需限定資料、目的與處理授權。 用自建測試檔描述可分析與不可分析區域。 因此「擁有技術能力就代表取得資料的授權。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Evidence access is bounded by data, purpose and authority. Define analyzable areas on self-created test files. The alternative \"Technical ability implies authority to obtain data.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-02"],"title":"證據識別：原理與架構","titleEn":"Evidence identification: principles and architecture","objective":"以「證據識別」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for evidence identification.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「證據識別」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：唯一識別連結媒體、映像、版本與交接紀錄。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for evidence identification. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Unique IDs connect media, images, versions and custody records. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：檔名相同即可合併證物。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal filenames justify merging evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「證據識別」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for evidence identification; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-03-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"唯一識別連結媒體、映像、版本與交接紀錄。","textEn":"Unique IDs connect media, images, versions and custody records.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-03-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「證據識別」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for evidence identification?","options":["唯一識別連結媒體、映像、版本與交接紀錄。","檔名相同即可合併證物。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「證據識別」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Unique IDs connect media, images, versions and custody records.","Equal filenames justify merging evidence.","One matching output proves evidence identification for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"唯一識別連結媒體、映像、版本與交接紀錄。 對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。 因此「檔名相同即可合併證物。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Unique IDs connect media, images, versions and custody records. Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. The alternative \"Equal filenames justify merging evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-03"],"title":"證據識別：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Evidence identification: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「證據識別」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for evidence identification.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。」；將結果與「唯一識別連結媒體、映像、版本與交接紀錄。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. Compare results against: Unique IDs connect media, images, versions and custody records. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：檔名相同即可合併證物。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal filenames justify merging evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「證據識別」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「檔名相同即可合併證物。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for evidence identification; explain why this claim fails: Equal filenames justify merging evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-04-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"唯一識別連結媒體、映像、版本與交接紀錄。","textEn":"Unique IDs connect media, images, versions and custody records.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-04-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「證據識別」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for evidence identification?","options":["檔名相同即可合併證物。","對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。","先把「證據識別」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Equal filenames justify merging evidence.","Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files.","Tune the displayed evidence identification result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"唯一識別連結媒體、映像、版本與交接紀錄。 對兩個相似測試檔建立不同證物識別。 因此「檔名相同即可合併證物。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Unique IDs connect media, images, versions and custody records. Assign separate evidence IDs to similar test files. The alternative \"Equal filenames justify merging evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-04"],"title":"揮發性排序：原理與架構","titleEn":"Volatility ordering: principles and architecture","objective":"以「揮發性排序」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for volatility ordering.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「揮發性排序」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：記憶體與暫存狀態可能先於磁碟消失。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for volatility ordering. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Memory and transient state can disappear before disk evidence. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有資料在關機後仍完整可讀。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: All data remains intact after shutdown. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「揮發性排序」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for volatility ordering; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-05-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"記憶體與暫存狀態可能先於磁碟消失。","textEn":"Memory and transient state can disappear before disk evidence.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-05-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「揮發性排序」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for volatility ordering?","options":["所有資料在關機後仍完整可讀。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「揮發性排序」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","記憶體與暫存狀態可能先於磁碟消失。"],"optionsEn":["All data remains intact after shutdown.","One matching output proves volatility ordering for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Memory and transient state can disappear before disk evidence."],"answer":2,"explanation":"記憶體與暫存狀態可能先於磁碟消失。 在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。 因此「所有資料在關機後仍完整可讀。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Memory and transient state can disappear before disk evidence. Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. The alternative \"All data remains intact after shutdown.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-05"],"title":"揮發性排序：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Volatility ordering: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「揮發性排序」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for volatility ordering.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。」；將結果與「記憶體與暫存狀態可能先於磁碟消失。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. Compare results against: Memory and transient state can disappear before disk evidence. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有資料在關機後仍完整可讀。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: All data remains intact after shutdown. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「揮發性排序」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「所有資料在關機後仍完整可讀。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for volatility ordering; explain why this claim fails: All data remains intact after shutdown.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-06-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"記憶體與暫存狀態可能先於磁碟消失。","textEn":"Memory and transient state can disappear before disk evidence.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-06-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「揮發性排序」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for volatility ordering?","options":["在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。","所有資料在關機後仍完整可讀。","先把「揮發性排序」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system.","All data remains intact after shutdown.","Tune the displayed volatility ordering result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"記憶體與暫存狀態可能先於磁碟消失。 在假想系統中排序易失與持久資料。 因此「所有資料在關機後仍完整可讀。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Memory and transient state can disappear before disk evidence. Rank volatile and durable data in a fictional system. The alternative \"All data remains intact after shutdown.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-06"],"title":"採集變更：原理與架構","titleEn":"Collection alteration: principles and architecture","objective":"以「採集變更」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for collection alteration.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「採集變更」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：採集工具自身可能造成可觀察系統變更。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for collection alteration. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Collection tools may themselves change observed state. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：讀取工具永不改變任何系統狀態。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Read tools never change system state. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「採集變更」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for collection alteration; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-07-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"採集工具自身可能造成可觀察系統變更。","textEn":"Collection tools may themselves change observed state.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-07-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「採集變更」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for collection alteration?","options":["讀取工具永不改變任何系統狀態。","採集工具自身可能造成可觀察系統變更。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「採集變更」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Read tools never change system state.","Collection tools may themselves change observed state.","One matching output proves collection alteration for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"採集工具自身可能造成可觀察系統變更。 列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。 因此「讀取工具永不改變任何系統狀態。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Collection tools may themselves change observed state. List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. The alternative \"Read tools never change system state.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-07"],"title":"採集變更：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Collection alteration: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「採集變更」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for collection alteration.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。」；將結果與「採集工具自身可能造成可觀察系統變更。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. Compare results against: Collection tools may themselves change observed state. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：讀取工具永不改變任何系統狀態。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Read tools never change system state. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「採集變更」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「讀取工具永不改變任何系統狀態。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for collection alteration; explain why this claim fails: Read tools never change system state.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-08-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"採集工具自身可能造成可觀察系統變更。","textEn":"Collection tools may themselves change observed state.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-08-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「採集變更」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for collection alteration?","options":["讀取工具永不改變任何系統狀態。","先把「採集變更」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。"],"optionsEn":["Read tools never change system state.","Tune the displayed collection alteration result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change."],"answer":2,"explanation":"採集工具自身可能造成可觀察系統變更。 列出玩具工具可能產生的日誌與時間戳。 因此「讀取工具永不改變任何系統狀態。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Collection tools may themselves change observed state. List logs and timestamps a toy collector may change. The alternative \"Read tools never change system state.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a370-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"採集與保全","titleEn":"Collection and preservation","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「採集與保全」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop collection and preservation through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a370-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-08"],"title":"唯讀路徑：原理與架構","titleEn":"Read-only paths: principles and architecture","objective":"以「唯讀路徑」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for read-only paths.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「唯讀路徑」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：寫入阻斷需涵蓋整個採集路徑而非單一設定。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for read-only paths. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Write blocking covers the entire collection path. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：唯讀標籤就是完整寫入阻斷證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A read-only label proves complete write blocking. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「唯讀路徑」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for read-only paths; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-09-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"寫入阻斷需涵蓋整個採集路徑而非單一設定。","textEn":"Write blocking covers the entire collection path.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-09-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「唯讀路徑」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for read-only paths?","options":["寫入阻斷需涵蓋整個採集路徑而非單一設定。","唯讀標籤就是完整寫入阻斷證據。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「唯讀路徑」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Write blocking covers the entire collection path.","A read-only label proves complete write blocking.","One matching output proves read-only paths for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"寫入阻斷需涵蓋整個採集路徑而非單一設定。 只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。 因此「唯讀標籤就是完整寫入阻斷證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Write blocking covers the entire collection path. Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. The alternative \"A read-only label proves complete write blocking.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-09"],"title":"唯讀路徑：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Read-only paths: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「唯讀路徑」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for read-only paths.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。」；將結果與「寫入阻斷需涵蓋整個採集路徑而非單一設定。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. Compare results against: Write blocking covers the entire collection path. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：唯讀標籤就是完整寫入阻斷證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A read-only label proves complete write blocking. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「唯讀路徑」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「唯讀標籤就是完整寫入阻斷證據。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for read-only paths; explain why this claim fails: A read-only label proves complete write blocking.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-10-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"寫入阻斷需涵蓋整個採集路徑而非單一設定。","textEn":"Write blocking covers the entire collection path.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-10-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「唯讀路徑」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for read-only paths?","options":["唯讀標籤就是完整寫入阻斷證據。","只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。","先把「唯讀路徑」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["A read-only label proves complete write blocking.","Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only.","Tune the displayed read-only paths result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"寫入阻斷需涵蓋整個採集路徑而非單一設定。 只在本地副本上比較唯讀設定與寫入行為。 因此「唯讀標籤就是完整寫入阻斷證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Write blocking covers the entire collection path. Compare read-only settings and writes on local copies only. The alternative \"A read-only label proves complete write blocking.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-10"],"title":"位元映像：原理與架構","titleEn":"Bitstream images: principles and architecture","objective":"以「位元映像」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for bitstream images.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「位元映像」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：映像範圍與讀取錯誤決定哪些位元被保留。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for bitstream images. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Image scope and read errors determine preserved bits. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：成功產生映像檔代表每個位元都成功採集。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Producing an image proves every bit was collected. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「位元映像」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for bitstream images; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-11-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"映像範圍與讀取錯誤決定哪些位元被保留。","textEn":"Image scope and read errors determine preserved bits.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-11-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「位元映像」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for bitstream images?","options":["成功產生映像檔代表每個位元都成功採集。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「位元映像」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","映像範圍與讀取錯誤決定哪些位元被保留。"],"optionsEn":["Producing an image proves every bit was collected.","One matching output proves bitstream images for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Image scope and read errors determine preserved bits."],"answer":2,"explanation":"映像範圍與讀取錯誤決定哪些位元被保留。 在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。 因此「成功產生映像檔代表每個位元都成功採集。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Image scope and read errors determine preserved bits. Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. The alternative \"Producing an image proves every bit was collected.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-11"],"title":"位元映像：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Bitstream images: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「位元映像」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for bitstream images.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。」；將結果與「映像範圍與讀取錯誤決定哪些位元被保留。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. Compare results against: Image scope and read errors determine preserved bits. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：成功產生映像檔代表每個位元都成功採集。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Producing an image proves every bit was collected. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「位元映像」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「成功產生映像檔代表每個位元都成功採集。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for bitstream images; explain why this claim fails: Producing an image proves every bit was collected.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-12-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"映像範圍與讀取錯誤決定哪些位元被保留。","textEn":"Image scope and read errors determine preserved bits.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-12-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「位元映像」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for bitstream images?","options":["在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。","成功產生映像檔代表每個位元都成功採集。","先把「位元映像」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image.","Producing an image proves every bit was collected.","Tune the displayed bitstream images result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"映像範圍與讀取錯誤決定哪些位元被保留。 在自製小映像記錄缺損區段與錯誤。 因此「成功產生映像檔代表每個位元都成功採集。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Image scope and read errors determine preserved bits. Record missing ranges and errors in a self-made image. The alternative \"Producing an image proves every bit was collected.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-12"],"title":"雜湊完整性：原理與架構","titleEn":"Hash integrity: principles and architecture","objective":"以「雜湊完整性」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for hash integrity.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「雜湊完整性」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：密碼雜湊可偵測位元變更但不證明內容真實。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for hash integrity. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Cryptographic hashes detect changes, not content truth. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：雜湊吻合便證明事件敘述真實。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Matching hashes prove the event narrative true. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「雜湊完整性」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for hash integrity; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-13-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"密碼雜湊可偵測位元變更但不證明內容真實。","textEn":"Cryptographic hashes detect changes, not content truth.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-13-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「雜湊完整性」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for hash integrity?","options":["雜湊吻合便證明事件敘述真實。","密碼雜湊可偵測位元變更但不證明內容真實。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「雜湊完整性」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Matching hashes prove the event narrative true.","Cryptographic hashes detect changes, not content truth.","One matching output proves hash integrity for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"密碼雜湊可偵測位元變更但不證明內容真實。 修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。 因此「雜湊吻合便證明事件敘述真實。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Cryptographic hashes detect changes, not content truth. Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. The alternative \"Matching hashes prove the event narrative true.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-13"],"title":"雜湊完整性：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Hash integrity: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「雜湊完整性」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for hash integrity.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。」；將結果與「密碼雜湊可偵測位元變更但不證明內容真實。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. Compare results against: Cryptographic hashes detect changes, not content truth. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：雜湊吻合便證明事件敘述真實。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Matching hashes prove the event narrative true. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「雜湊完整性」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「雜湊吻合便證明事件敘述真實。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for hash integrity; explain why this claim fails: Matching hashes prove the event narrative true.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-14-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"密碼雜湊可偵測位元變更但不證明內容真實。","textEn":"Cryptographic hashes detect changes, not content truth.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-14-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「雜湊完整性」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for hash integrity?","options":["雜湊吻合便證明事件敘述真實。","先把「雜湊完整性」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。"],"optionsEn":["Matching hashes prove the event narrative true.","Tune the displayed hash integrity result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests."],"answer":2,"explanation":"密碼雜湊可偵測位元變更但不證明內容真實。 修改自製副本一個位元並比較摘要。 因此「雜湊吻合便證明事件敘述真實。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Cryptographic hashes detect changes, not content truth. Change one bit in a self-made copy and compare digests. The alternative \"Matching hashes prove the event narrative true.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-14"],"title":"交接紀錄：原理與架構","titleEn":"Custody records: principles and architecture","objective":"以「交接紀錄」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for custody records.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「交接紀錄」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：每次接觸需紀錄人、時點、動作與版本。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for custody records. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Each access records actor, time, action and version. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有最初取得者需要被記錄。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Only the initial collector needs recording. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「交接紀錄」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for custody records; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-15-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"每次接觸需紀錄人、時點、動作與版本。","textEn":"Each access records actor, time, action and version.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-15-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「交接紀錄」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for custody records?","options":["每次接觸需紀錄人、時點、動作與版本。","只有最初取得者需要被記錄。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「交接紀錄」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Each access records actor, time, action and version.","Only the initial collector needs recording.","One matching output proves custody records for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"每次接觸需紀錄人、時點、動作與版本。 模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。 因此「只有最初取得者需要被記錄。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Each access records actor, time, action and version. Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. The alternative \"Only the initial collector needs recording.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-15"],"title":"交接紀錄：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Custody records: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「交接紀錄」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for custody records.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。」；將結果與「每次接觸需紀錄人、時點、動作與版本。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. Compare results against: Each access records actor, time, action and version. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有最初取得者需要被記錄。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Only the initial collector needs recording. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「交接紀錄」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「只有最初取得者需要被記錄。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for custody records; explain why this claim fails: Only the initial collector needs recording.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-16-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"每次接觸需紀錄人、時點、動作與版本。","textEn":"Each access records actor, time, action and version.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-16-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「交接紀錄」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for custody records?","options":["只有最初取得者需要被記錄。","模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。","先把「交接紀錄」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Only the initial collector needs recording.","Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps.","Tune the displayed custody records result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"每次接觸需紀錄人、時點、動作與版本。 模擬兩次交接並找出無法追溯的空白。 因此「只有最初取得者需要被記錄。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Each access records actor, time, action and version. Simulate two handoffs and identify untraceable gaps. The alternative \"Only the initial collector needs recording.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a370-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"分析與交查","titleEn":"Analysis and cross-checking","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「分析與交查」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop analysis and cross-checking through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a370-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-16"],"title":"時間戳語意：原理與架構","titleEn":"Timestamp semantics: principles and architecture","objective":"以「時間戳語意」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for timestamp semantics.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「時間戳語意」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：建立、修改、存取時間與時區具有不同語意。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for timestamp semantics. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Creation, modification, access and timezone have different meanings. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：不同顯示時間必然代表檔案被改寫。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Different displayed times prove alteration. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「時間戳語意」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for timestamp semantics; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-17-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"建立、修改、存取時間與時區具有不同語意。","textEn":"Creation, modification, access and timezone have different meanings.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-17-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「時間戳語意」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for timestamp semantics?","options":["不同顯示時間必然代表檔案被改寫。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「時間戳語意」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","建立、修改、存取時間與時區具有不同語意。"],"optionsEn":["Different displayed times prove alteration.","One matching output proves timestamp semantics for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Creation, modification, access and timezone have different meanings."],"answer":2,"explanation":"建立、修改、存取時間與時區具有不同語意。 比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。 因此「不同顯示時間必然代表檔案被改寫。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Creation, modification, access and timezone have different meanings. Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. The alternative \"Different displayed times prove alteration.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-17"],"title":"時間戳語意：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Timestamp semantics: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「時間戳語意」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for timestamp semantics.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。」；將結果與「建立、修改、存取時間與時區具有不同語意。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. Compare results against: Creation, modification, access and timezone have different meanings. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：不同顯示時間必然代表檔案被改寫。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Different displayed times prove alteration. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「時間戳語意」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「不同顯示時間必然代表檔案被改寫。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for timestamp semantics; explain why this claim fails: Different displayed times prove alteration.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-18-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"建立、修改、存取時間與時區具有不同語意。","textEn":"Creation, modification, access and timezone have different meanings.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-18-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「時間戳語意」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for timestamp semantics?","options":["比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。","不同顯示時間必然代表檔案被改寫。","先把「時間戳語意」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file.","Different displayed times prove alteration.","Tune the displayed timestamp semantics result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"建立、修改、存取時間與時區具有不同語意。 比較同一測試檔跨時區顯示和原始值。 因此「不同顯示時間必然代表檔案被改寫。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Creation, modification, access and timezone have different meanings. Compare timezone display with raw values for one test file. The alternative \"Different displayed times prove alteration.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-18"],"title":"檔案與磁區：原理與架構","titleEn":"Files and sectors: principles and architecture","objective":"以「檔案與磁區」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for files and sectors.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「檔案與磁區」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：檔案系統配置與未配置區不能混為一談。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for files and sectors. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Allocated files and unallocated regions differ. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：未配置區一定沒有與事件相關資料。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unallocated regions never contain relevant data. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「檔案與磁區」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for files and sectors; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-19-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"檔案系統配置與未配置區不能混為一談。","textEn":"Allocated files and unallocated regions differ.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-19-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「檔案與磁區」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for files and sectors?","options":["未配置區一定沒有與事件相關資料。","檔案系統配置與未配置區不能混為一談。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「檔案與磁區」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Unallocated regions never contain relevant data.","Allocated files and unallocated regions differ.","One matching output proves files and sectors for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"檔案系統配置與未配置區不能混為一談。 在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。 因此「未配置區一定沒有與事件相關資料。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Allocated files and unallocated regions differ. Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. The alternative \"Unallocated regions never contain relevant data.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-19"],"title":"檔案與磁區：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Files and sectors: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「檔案與磁區」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for files and sectors.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。」；將結果與「檔案系統配置與未配置區不能混為一談。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. Compare results against: Allocated files and unallocated regions differ. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：未配置區一定沒有與事件相關資料。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Unallocated regions never contain relevant data. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「檔案與磁區」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「未配置區一定沒有與事件相關資料。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for files and sectors; explain why this claim fails: Unallocated regions never contain relevant data.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-20-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"檔案系統配置與未配置區不能混為一談。","textEn":"Allocated files and unallocated regions differ.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-20-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「檔案與磁區」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for files and sectors?","options":["未配置區一定沒有與事件相關資料。","先把「檔案與磁區」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。"],"optionsEn":["Unallocated regions never contain relevant data.","Tune the displayed files and sectors result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image."],"answer":2,"explanation":"檔案系統配置與未配置區不能混為一談。 在自製映像對照目錄項與位元範圍。 因此「未配置區一定沒有與事件相關資料。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Allocated files and unallocated regions differ. Compare directory entries with byte ranges in a self-made image. The alternative \"Unallocated regions never contain relevant data.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-20"],"title":"解析器驗證：原理與架構","titleEn":"Parser validation: principles and architecture","objective":"以「解析器驗證」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for parser validation.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「解析器驗證」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：解析結果依格式、版本與錯誤處理而異。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for parser validation. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Parsing depends on format, version and error handling. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：兩工具輸出一致即可排除共同解析錯誤。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Matching tools exclude shared parsing errors. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「解析器驗證」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for parser validation; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-21-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"解析結果依格式、版本與錯誤處理而異。","textEn":"Parsing depends on format, version and error handling.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-21-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「解析器驗證」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for parser validation?","options":["解析結果依格式、版本與錯誤處理而異。","兩工具輸出一致即可排除共同解析錯誤。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「解析器驗證」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Parsing depends on format, version and error handling.","Matching tools exclude shared parsing errors.","One matching output proves parser validation for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"解析結果依格式、版本與錯誤處理而異。 對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。 因此「兩工具輸出一致即可排除共同解析錯誤。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Parsing depends on format, version and error handling. Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. The alternative \"Matching tools exclude shared parsing errors.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-21"],"title":"解析器驗證：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Parser validation: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「解析器驗證」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for parser validation.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。」；將結果與「解析結果依格式、版本與錯誤處理而異。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. Compare results against: Parsing depends on format, version and error handling. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：兩工具輸出一致即可排除共同解析錯誤。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Matching tools exclude shared parsing errors. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「解析器驗證」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「兩工具輸出一致即可排除共同解析錯誤。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for parser validation; explain why this claim fails: Matching tools exclude shared parsing errors.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-22-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"解析結果依格式、版本與錯誤處理而異。","textEn":"Parsing depends on format, version and error handling.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-22-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「解析器驗證」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for parser validation?","options":["兩工具輸出一致即可排除共同解析錯誤。","對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。","先把「解析器驗證」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Matching tools exclude shared parsing errors.","Compare two parsers on known synthetic content.","Tune the displayed parser validation result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"解析結果依格式、版本與錯誤處理而異。 對已知內容的合成檔比較兩個解析路徑。 因此「兩工具輸出一致即可排除共同解析錯誤。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Parsing depends on format, version and error handling. Compare two parsers on known synthetic content. The alternative \"Matching tools exclude shared parsing errors.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-22"],"title":"獨立交查：原理與架構","titleEn":"Independent corroboration: principles and architecture","objective":"以「獨立交查」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for independent corroboration.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「獨立交查」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：獨立來源能區分工具錯誤和真實事件。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for independent corroboration. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Independent sources separate tool error from events. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Cross-check synthetic login and application records. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Cross-check synthetic login and application records. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：複製同一份日誌便增加獨立證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Copying one log creates independent evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「獨立交查」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for independent corroboration; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-23-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"獨立來源能區分工具錯誤和真實事件。","textEn":"Independent sources separate tool error from events.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-23-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Cross-check synthetic login and application records. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「獨立交查」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for independent corroboration?","options":["複製同一份日誌便增加獨立證據。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「獨立交查」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","獨立來源能區分工具錯誤和真實事件。"],"optionsEn":["Copying one log creates independent evidence.","One matching output proves independent corroboration for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Independent sources separate tool error from events."],"answer":2,"explanation":"獨立來源能區分工具錯誤和真實事件。 對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。 因此「複製同一份日誌便增加獨立證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Independent sources separate tool error from events. Cross-check synthetic login and application records. The alternative \"Copying one log creates independent evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-23"],"title":"獨立交查：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Independent corroboration: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「獨立交查」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for independent corroboration.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。」；將結果與「獨立來源能區分工具錯誤和真實事件。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Cross-check synthetic login and application records. Compare results against: Independent sources separate tool error from events. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Cross-check synthetic login and application records. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：複製同一份日誌便增加獨立證據。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Copying one log creates independent evidence. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「獨立交查」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「複製同一份日誌便增加獨立證據。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for independent corroboration; explain why this claim fails: Copying one log creates independent evidence.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-24-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"獨立來源能區分工具錯誤和真實事件。","textEn":"Independent sources separate tool error from events.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-24-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Cross-check synthetic login and application records. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「獨立交查」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for independent corroboration?","options":["對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。","複製同一份日誌便增加獨立證據。","先把「獨立交查」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Cross-check synthetic login and application records.","Copying one log creates independent evidence.","Tune the displayed independent corroboration result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"獨立來源能區分工具錯誤和真實事件。 對合成登入紀錄與自製應用紀錄交查。 因此「複製同一份日誌便增加獨立證據。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Independent sources separate tool error from events. Cross-check synthetic login and application records. The alternative \"Copying one log creates independent evidence.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a370-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"報告與重現","titleEn":"Reporting and reproduction","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「報告與重現」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop reporting and reproduction through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a370-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-24"],"title":"採集吞吐：原理與架構","titleEn":"Collection throughput: principles and architecture","objective":"以「採集吞吐」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for collection throughput.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「採集吞吐」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：讀寫瓶頸與驗證次數共同決定耗時。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for collection throughput. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Read/write bottlenecks and verification passes set duration. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：標稱磁碟頻寬就是端到端採集速度。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Rated disk bandwidth equals end-to-end collection speed. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「採集吞吐」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for collection throughput; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-25-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"讀寫瓶頸與驗證次數共同決定耗時。","textEn":"Read/write bottlenecks and verification passes set duration.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-25-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「採集吞吐」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for collection throughput?","options":["標稱磁碟頻寬就是端到端採集速度。","讀寫瓶頸與驗證次數共同決定耗時。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「採集吞吐」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Rated disk bandwidth equals end-to-end collection speed.","Read/write bottlenecks and verification passes set duration.","One matching output proves collection throughput for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"讀寫瓶頸與驗證次數共同決定耗時。 重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。 因此「標稱磁碟頻寬就是端到端採集速度。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Read/write bottlenecks and verification passes set duration. Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. The alternative \"Rated disk bandwidth equals end-to-end collection speed.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-25"],"title":"採集吞吐：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Collection throughput: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「採集吞吐」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for collection throughput.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。」；將結果與「讀寫瓶頸與驗證次數共同決定耗時。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. Compare results against: Read/write bottlenecks and verification passes set duration. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：標稱磁碟頻寬就是端到端採集速度。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Rated disk bandwidth equals end-to-end collection speed. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「採集吞吐」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「標稱磁碟頻寬就是端到端採集速度。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for collection throughput; explain why this claim fails: Rated disk bandwidth equals end-to-end collection speed.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-26-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"讀寫瓶頸與驗證次數共同決定耗時。","textEn":"Read/write bottlenecks and verification passes set duration.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-26-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「採集吞吐」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for collection throughput?","options":["標稱磁碟頻寬就是端到端採集速度。","先把「採集吞吐」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。"],"optionsEn":["Rated disk bandwidth equals end-to-end collection speed.","Tune the displayed collection throughput result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Recalculate collection and verification time bounds."],"answer":2,"explanation":"讀寫瓶頸與驗證次數共同決定耗時。 重算本課映像採集與驗證下限。 因此「標稱磁碟頻寬就是端到端採集速度。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Read/write bottlenecks and verification passes set duration. Recalculate collection and verification time bounds. The alternative \"Rated disk bandwidth equals end-to-end collection speed.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-26"],"title":"假設邊界：原理與架構","titleEn":"Inference boundaries: principles and architecture","objective":"以「假設邊界」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for inference boundaries.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「假設邊界」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：看不到紀錄不等於行為未發生。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for inference boundaries. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Missing records do not prove an action never occurred. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：沒有日誌即可證明沒有事件。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: No log proves no event. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「假設邊界」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for inference boundaries; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-27-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"看不到紀錄不等於行為未發生。","textEn":"Missing records do not prove an action never occurred.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-27-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「假設邊界」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for inference boundaries?","options":["看不到紀錄不等於行為未發生。","沒有日誌即可證明沒有事件。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「假設邊界」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Missing records do not prove an action never occurred.","No log proves no event.","One matching output proves inference boundaries for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"看不到紀錄不等於行為未發生。 為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。 因此「沒有日誌即可證明沒有事件。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Missing records do not prove an action never occurred. List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. The alternative \"No log proves no event.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-27"],"title":"假設邊界：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Inference boundaries: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「假設邊界」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for inference boundaries.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。」；將結果與「看不到紀錄不等於行為未發生。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. Compare results against: Missing records do not prove an action never occurred. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：沒有日誌即可證明沒有事件。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: No log proves no event. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「假設邊界」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「沒有日誌即可證明沒有事件。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for inference boundaries; explain why this claim fails: No log proves no event.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-28-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"看不到紀錄不等於行為未發生。","textEn":"Missing records do not prove an action never occurred.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-28-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「假設邊界」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for inference boundaries?","options":["沒有日誌即可證明沒有事件。","為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。","先把「假設邊界」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["No log proves no event.","List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps.","Tune the displayed inference boundaries result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"看不到紀錄不等於行為未發生。 為合成日誌缺口列出保留、遺失與未產生解釋。 因此「沒有日誌即可證明沒有事件。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Missing records do not prove an action never occurred. List retention, loss and noncreation explanations for gaps. The alternative \"No log proves no event.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-28"],"title":"報告重現：原理與架構","titleEn":"Report reproduction: principles and architecture","objective":"以「報告重現」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for report reproduction.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「報告重現」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：報告需列工具版本、輸入摘要與分析假設。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for report reproduction. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Reports specify tool versions, input digests and assumptions. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有截圖即可完整重現分析。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Screenshots alone fully reproduce analysis. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「報告重現」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for report reproduction; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-29-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"報告需列工具版本、輸入摘要與分析假設。","textEn":"Reports specify tool versions, input digests and assumptions.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-29-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「報告重現」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for report reproduction?","options":["只有截圖即可完整重現分析。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「報告重現」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","報告需列工具版本、輸入摘要與分析假設。"],"optionsEn":["Screenshots alone fully reproduce analysis.","One matching output proves report reproduction for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Reports specify tool versions, input digests and assumptions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"報告需列工具版本、輸入摘要與分析假設。 讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。 因此「只有截圖即可完整重現分析。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reports specify tool versions, input digests and assumptions. Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. The alternative \"Screenshots alone fully reproduce analysis.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-29"],"title":"報告重現：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Report reproduction: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「報告重現」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for report reproduction.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。」；將結果與「報告需列工具版本、輸入摘要與分析假設。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. Compare results against: Reports specify tool versions, input digests and assumptions. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有截圖即可完整重現分析。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Screenshots alone fully reproduce analysis. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「報告重現」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「只有截圖即可完整重現分析。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for report reproduction; explain why this claim fails: Screenshots alone fully reproduce analysis.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-30-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"報告需列工具版本、輸入摘要與分析假設。","textEn":"Reports specify tool versions, input digests and assumptions.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-30-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「報告重現」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for report reproduction?","options":["讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。","只有截圖即可完整重現分析。","先把「報告重現」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report.","Screenshots alone fully reproduce analysis.","Tune the displayed report reproduction result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"報告需列工具版本、輸入摘要與分析假設。 讓另一位同學只依匿名報告重算結果。 因此「只有截圖即可完整重現分析。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reports specify tool versions, input digests and assumptions. Have a peer reproduce findings from an anonymous report. The alternative \"Screenshots alone fully reproduce analysis.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-30"],"title":"儲存與刪除：原理與架構","titleEn":"Retention and deletion: principles and architecture","objective":"以「儲存與刪除」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for retention and deletion.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「儲存與刪除」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：儲存期限、存取與合規要求需獨立管理。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for retention and deletion. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Retention, access and compliance requirements are managed separately. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：證據越多儲存越久永遠越好。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Keeping more evidence forever is always better. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「儲存與刪除」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for retention and deletion; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-31-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"儲存期限、存取與合規要求需獨立管理。","textEn":"Retention, access and compliance requirements are managed separately.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-31-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a370-v11-31-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"一份假想 64 GiB 映像以 250 MiB/s 讀取，理想單次時間為 64×1024/250=262.14 秒；若採集後再完整驗證讀取一次，最低讀取時間約 524.29 秒。未含 I/O 競爭、寫入與工具開銷。","textEn":"A synthetic 64 GiB image read at 250 MiB/s takes 262.14 seconds ideally. One further full verification read brings minimum reading time to 524.29 seconds, excluding contention, writes and tool overhead.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「儲存與刪除」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for retention and deletion?","options":["證據越多儲存越久永遠越好。","儲存期限、存取與合規要求需獨立管理。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「儲存與刪除」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Keeping more evidence forever is always better.","Retention, access and compliance requirements are managed separately.","One matching output proves retention and deletion for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"儲存期限、存取與合規要求需獨立管理。 在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。 因此「證據越多儲存越久永遠越好。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Retention, access and compliance requirements are managed separately. Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. The alternative \"Keeping more evidence forever is always better.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a370-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"prerequisiteIds":["a370-v11-31"],"title":"儲存與刪除：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Retention and deletion: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「儲存與刪除」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for retention and deletion.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。」；將結果與「儲存期限、存取與合規要求需獨立管理。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. Compare results against: Retention, access and compliance requirements are managed separately. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：證據越多儲存越久永遠越好。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Keeping more evidence forever is always better. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「儲存與刪除」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「證據越多儲存越久永遠越好。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for retention and deletion; explain why this claim fails: Keeping more evidence forever is always better.","knowledge":[{"id":"a370-v11-32-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"儲存期限、存取與合規要求需獨立管理。","textEn":"Retention, access and compliance requirements are managed separately.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a370-v11-32-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a370-v11-32-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"一份假想 64 GiB 映像以 250 MiB/s 讀取，理想單次時間為 64×1024/250=262.14 秒；若採集後再完整驗證讀取一次，最低讀取時間約 524.29 秒。未含 I/O 競爭、寫入與工具開銷。","textEn":"A synthetic 64 GiB image read at 250 MiB/s takes 262.14 seconds ideally. One further full verification read brings minimum reading time to 524.29 seconds, excluding contention, writes and tool overhead.","sourceIds":["v11c-forensic","v11c-evidence"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「儲存與刪除」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for retention and deletion?","options":["證據越多儲存越久永遠越好。","先把「儲存與刪除」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。"],"optionsEn":["Keeping more evidence forever is always better.","Tune the displayed retention and deletion result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow."],"answer":2,"explanation":"儲存期限、存取與合規要求需獨立管理。 在假想流程列出儲存、到期及例外批准。 因此「證據越多儲存越久永遠越好。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Retention, access and compliance requirements are managed separately. Specify retention, expiry and exceptions in a fictional workflow. The alternative \"Keeping more evidence forever is always better.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]}],"curriculumVersion":11,"scope":"公開原理的本地科教模擬與工程判讀。只使用自製、合成或明確授權的資料；不操作真實受害主機、他人帳號、工業控制或超算設施。數值不代表廠商規格或實測效能，完成課程不是專業資格、真實裝置操作經歷或生產部署認證。","scopeEn":"Local educational simulation and engineering interpretation of public principles. Use self-made, synthetic or explicitly licensed data only; do not operate real victim hosts, other accounts, industrial control or supercomputing facilities. Values are not product specifications or measured performance. Completion is not a qualification, real-equipment experience or production-deployment certification.","workedExample":{"title":"含假設的可重算工程例","titleEn":"Reproducible assumed engineering case","text":"一份假想 64 GiB 映像以 250 MiB/s 讀取，理想單次時間為 64×1024/250=262.14 秒；若採集後再完整驗證讀取一次，最低讀取時間約 524.29 秒。未含 I/O 競爭、寫入與工具開銷。","textEn":"A synthetic 64 GiB image read at 250 MiB/s takes 262.14 seconds ideally. One further full verification read brings minimum reading time to 524.29 seconds, excluding contention, writes and tool overhead.","assumptions":"使用算例明列的單位、分佈、精度、拓撲與理想化條件；改變鄰接、位寬、取樣或系統邊界必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use the stated units, distributions, precision, topology and idealizations; recompute after changing adjacency, width, sampling or boundaries.","sourceScope":"作者獨立設定的假想數值例，非引用機構的實測資料；來源支援領域定義與架構。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen hypothetical values, not institutional measurements; sources support definitions and architecture."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["授權與識別","採集與保全","分析與交查","報告與重現"],"labelsEn":["Authority and identification","Collection and preservation","Analysis and cross-checking","Reporting and reproduction"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-defense","subcategoryTitle":"防禦、監測與事件應變","subcategoryTitleEn":"Defense, monitoring and incident response","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-defense","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a371","title":"隱私保護資料分析","titleEn":"Privacy-preserving data analytics","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以資料最小化與隱私效用權衡串連 16 個原創技術單元、32 步；涵蓋原理解析、架構圖、假想量化、合成資料實驗、競爭失效原因及可重算驗收。","summaryEn":"Sixteen original technical units and 32 tasks connect data minimization and privacy–utility trade-offs with principles, architectures, assumed calculations, synthetic experiments, competing failure causes and reproducible acceptance.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a371-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"資料與目的","titleEn":"Data and purpose","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「資料與目的」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop data and purpose through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a371-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"用途邊界：原理與架構","titleEn":"Purpose boundaries: principles and architecture","objective":"以「用途邊界」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for purpose boundaries.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「用途邊界」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：同一資料可因使用目的不同而形成不同隱私風險。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for purpose boundaries. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: The same data creates different privacy risks under different purposes. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：取得一次同意便能用於任何新目的。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: One consent permits every future purpose. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「用途邊界」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for purpose boundaries; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-01-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"同一資料可因使用目的不同而形成不同隱私風險。","textEn":"The same data creates different privacy risks under different purposes.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-01-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a371-v11-01-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 100 人平均收入分析先將收入界定於 0–100,000 單位；固定樣本數替換鄰接下，平均敏感度 Δ=100000/100=1000 單位。Laplace ε=1 時尺度 b=1000、標準差 √2b=1414.21 單位。只此假設成立時適用。","textEn":"For 100 synthetic people with values bounded to 0–100,000 units and fixed-size replace-one adjacency, mean sensitivity is 1,000 units. Laplace ε=1 gives b=1,000 and standard deviation 1,414.21 units; the assumptions are essential.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「用途邊界」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for purpose boundaries?","options":["取得一次同意便能用於任何新目的。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「用途邊界」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","同一資料可因使用目的不同而形成不同隱私風險。"],"optionsEn":["One consent permits every future purpose.","One matching output proves purpose boundaries for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","The same data creates different privacy risks under different purposes."],"answer":2,"explanation":"同一資料可因使用目的不同而形成不同隱私風險。 寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。 因此「取得一次同意便能用於任何新目的。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"The same data creates different privacy risks under different purposes. Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. The alternative \"One consent permits every future purpose.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-01"],"title":"用途邊界：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Purpose boundaries: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「用途邊界」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for purpose boundaries.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。」；將結果與「同一資料可因使用目的不同而形成不同隱私風險。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. Compare results against: The same data creates different privacy risks under different purposes. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：取得一次同意便能用於任何新目的。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: One consent permits every future purpose. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「用途邊界」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「取得一次同意便能用於任何新目的。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for purpose boundaries; explain why this claim fails: One consent permits every future purpose.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-02-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"同一資料可因使用目的不同而形成不同隱私風險。","textEn":"The same data creates different privacy risks under different purposes.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-02-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a371-v11-02-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 100 人平均收入分析先將收入界定於 0–100,000 單位；固定樣本數替換鄰接下，平均敏感度 Δ=100000/100=1000 單位。Laplace ε=1 時尺度 b=1000、標準差 √2b=1414.21 單位。只此假設成立時適用。","textEn":"For 100 synthetic people with values bounded to 0–100,000 units and fixed-size replace-one adjacency, mean sensitivity is 1,000 units. Laplace ε=1 gives b=1,000 and standard deviation 1,414.21 units; the assumptions are essential.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「用途邊界」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for purpose boundaries?","options":["寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。","取得一次同意便能用於任何新目的。","先把「用途邊界」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data.","One consent permits every future purpose.","Tune the displayed purpose boundaries result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"同一資料可因使用目的不同而形成不同隱私風險。 寫出合成資料分析的必要與非必要用途。 因此「取得一次同意便能用於任何新目的。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"The same data creates different privacy risks under different purposes. Specify necessary and unnecessary uses of synthetic data. The alternative \"One consent permits every future purpose.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-02"],"title":"資料最小化：原理與架構","titleEn":"Data minimization: principles and architecture","objective":"以「資料最小化」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for data minimization.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「資料最小化」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：少收欄位能降低暴露但可能降低可辨識性。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for data minimization. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Fewer fields reduce exposure but can reduce identifiability of effects. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：刪除姓名即完成最小化。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Deleting names completes minimization. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「資料最小化」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for data minimization; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-03-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"少收欄位能降低暴露但可能降低可辨識性。","textEn":"Fewer fields reduce exposure but can reduce identifiability of effects.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-03-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「資料最小化」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for data minimization?","options":["刪除姓名即完成最小化。","少收欄位能降低暴露但可能降低可辨識性。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「資料最小化」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Deleting names completes minimization.","Fewer fields reduce exposure but can reduce identifiability of effects.","One matching output proves data minimization for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"少收欄位能降低暴露但可能降低可辨識性。 比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。 因此「刪除姓名即完成最小化。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Fewer fields reduce exposure but can reduce identifiability of effects. Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. The alternative \"Deleting names completes minimization.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-03"],"title":"資料最小化：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Data minimization: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「資料最小化」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for data minimization.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。」；將結果與「少收欄位能降低暴露但可能降低可辨識性。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. Compare results against: Fewer fields reduce exposure but can reduce identifiability of effects. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：刪除姓名即完成最小化。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Deleting names completes minimization. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「資料最小化」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「刪除姓名即完成最小化。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for data minimization; explain why this claim fails: Deleting names completes minimization.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-04-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"少收欄位能降低暴露但可能降低可辨識性。","textEn":"Fewer fields reduce exposure but can reduce identifiability of effects.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-04-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「資料最小化」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for data minimization?","options":["刪除姓名即完成最小化。","先把「資料最小化」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。"],"optionsEn":["Deleting names completes minimization.","Tune the displayed data minimization result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields."],"answer":2,"explanation":"少收欄位能降低暴露但可能降低可辨識性。 比較完整與最小化欄位的合成模型誤差。 因此「刪除姓名即完成最小化。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Fewer fields reduce exposure but can reduce identifiability of effects. Compare synthetic-model errors with full and minimal fields. The alternative \"Deleting names completes minimization.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-04"],"title":"準識別欄位：原理與架構","titleEn":"Quasi-identifiers: principles and architecture","objective":"以「準識別欄位」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for quasi-identifiers.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「準識別欄位」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：時間、位置與屬性組合仍可能識別個人。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for quasi-identifiers. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Time, location and attribute combinations may identify people. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：沒有姓名的資料絕不可能識別個人。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Nameless data cannot identify people. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「準識別欄位」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for quasi-identifiers; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-05-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"時間、位置與屬性組合仍可能識別個人。","textEn":"Time, location and attribute combinations may identify people.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-05-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「準識別欄位」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for quasi-identifiers?","options":["時間、位置與屬性組合仍可能識別個人。","沒有姓名的資料絕不可能識別個人。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「準識別欄位」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Time, location and attribute combinations may identify people.","Nameless data cannot identify people.","One matching output proves quasi-identifiers for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"時間、位置與屬性組合仍可能識別個人。 對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。 因此「沒有姓名的資料絕不可能識別個人。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Time, location and attribute combinations may identify people. Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. The alternative \"Nameless data cannot identify people.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-05"],"title":"準識別欄位：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Quasi-identifiers: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「準識別欄位」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for quasi-identifiers.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。」；將結果與「時間、位置與屬性組合仍可能識別個人。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. Compare results against: Time, location and attribute combinations may identify people. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：沒有姓名的資料絕不可能識別個人。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Nameless data cannot identify people. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「準識別欄位」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「沒有姓名的資料絕不可能識別個人。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for quasi-identifiers; explain why this claim fails: Nameless data cannot identify people.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-06-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"時間、位置與屬性組合仍可能識別個人。","textEn":"Time, location and attribute combinations may identify people.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-06-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「準識別欄位」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for quasi-identifiers?","options":["沒有姓名的資料絕不可能識別個人。","對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。","先把「準識別欄位」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Nameless data cannot identify people.","Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups.","Tune the displayed quasi-identifiers result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"時間、位置與屬性組合仍可能識別個人。 對自行生成的群組計算唯一組合比例。 因此「沒有姓名的資料絕不可能識別個人。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Time, location and attribute combinations may identify people. Measure unique combinations in self-generated groups. The alternative \"Nameless data cannot identify people.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-06"],"title":"信任邊界：原理與架構","titleEn":"Trust boundaries: principles and architecture","objective":"以「信任邊界」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for trust boundaries.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「信任邊界」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：蒐集者、分析者與發布者可有不同許可權。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for trust boundaries. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Collectors, analysts and publishers can have different privileges. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有參與者都必須看原始資料。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Every participant must see raw data. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「信任邊界」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for trust boundaries; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-07-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"蒐集者、分析者與發布者可有不同許可權。","textEn":"Collectors, analysts and publishers can have different privileges.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-07-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「信任邊界」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for trust boundaries?","options":["所有參與者都必須看原始資料。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「信任邊界」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","蒐集者、分析者與發布者可有不同許可權。"],"optionsEn":["Every participant must see raw data.","One matching output proves trust boundaries for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Collectors, analysts and publishers can have different privileges."],"answer":2,"explanation":"蒐集者、分析者與發布者可有不同許可權。 標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。 因此「所有參與者都必須看原始資料。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Collectors, analysts and publishers can have different privileges. Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. The alternative \"Every participant must see raw data.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-07"],"title":"信任邊界：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Trust boundaries: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「信任邊界」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for trust boundaries.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。」；將結果與「蒐集者、分析者與發布者可有不同許可權。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. Compare results against: Collectors, analysts and publishers can have different privileges. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：所有參與者都必須看原始資料。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Every participant must see raw data. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「信任邊界」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「所有參與者都必須看原始資料。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for trust boundaries; explain why this claim fails: Every participant must see raw data.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-08-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"蒐集者、分析者與發布者可有不同許可權。","textEn":"Collectors, analysts and publishers can have different privileges.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-08-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「信任邊界」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for trust boundaries?","options":["標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。","所有參與者都必須看原始資料。","先把「信任邊界」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture.","Every participant must see raw data.","Tune the displayed trust boundaries result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"蒐集者、分析者與發布者可有不同許可權。 標示匿名架構每一層可見的欄位。 因此「所有參與者都必須看原始資料。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Collectors, analysts and publishers can have different privileges. Mark fields visible at each layer of an anonymous architecture. The alternative \"Every participant must see raw data.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a371-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"風險與模型","titleEn":"Risk and models","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「風險與模型」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop risk and models through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a371-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-08"],"title":"威脅模型：原理與架構","titleEn":"Threat models: principles and architecture","objective":"以「威脅模型」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for threat models.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「威脅模型」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：保護方法依攻擊者先驗知識與可見輸出而異。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for threat models. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Protection depends on adversary knowledge and visible outputs. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：保護強度完全與外部知識無關。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Protection is independent of outside knowledge. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「威脅模型」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for threat models; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-09-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"保護方法依攻擊者先驗知識與可見輸出而異。","textEn":"Protection depends on adversary knowledge and visible outputs.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-09-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「威脅模型」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for threat models?","options":["保護強度完全與外部知識無關。","保護方法依攻擊者先驗知識與可見輸出而異。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「威脅模型」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Protection is independent of outside knowledge.","Protection depends on adversary knowledge and visible outputs.","One matching output proves threat models for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"保護方法依攻擊者先驗知識與可見輸出而異。 在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。 因此「保護強度完全與外部知識無關。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Protection depends on adversary knowledge and visible outputs. Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. The alternative \"Protection is independent of outside knowledge.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-09"],"title":"威脅模型：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Threat models: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「威脅模型」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for threat models.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。」；將結果與「保護方法依攻擊者先驗知識與可見輸出而異。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. Compare results against: Protection depends on adversary knowledge and visible outputs. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：保護強度完全與外部知識無關。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Protection is independent of outside knowledge. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「威脅模型」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「保護強度完全與外部知識無關。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for threat models; explain why this claim fails: Protection is independent of outside knowledge.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-10-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"保護方法依攻擊者先驗知識與可見輸出而異。","textEn":"Protection depends on adversary knowledge and visible outputs.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-10-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「威脅模型」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for threat models?","options":["保護強度完全與外部知識無關。","先把「威脅模型」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。"],"optionsEn":["Protection is independent of outside knowledge.","Tune the displayed threat models result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Specify two priors on paper without real personal data."],"answer":2,"explanation":"保護方法依攻擊者先驗知識與可見輸出而異。 在紙上設定兩種先驗而不使用真實個資。 因此「保護強度完全與外部知識無關。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Protection depends on adversary knowledge and visible outputs. Specify two priors on paper without real personal data. The alternative \"Protection is independent of outside knowledge.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-10"],"title":"連結風險：原理與架構","titleEn":"Linkage risk: principles and architecture","objective":"以「連結風險」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for linkage risk.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「連結風險」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：外部資料連結會改變原資料的識別風險。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for linkage risk. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: External linkage changes identifiability risk. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每一表單獨匿名便保證聯結後匿名。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Separately anonymous tables stay anonymous after joining. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「連結風險」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for linkage risk; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-11-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"外部資料連結會改變原資料的識別風險。","textEn":"External linkage changes identifiability risk.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-11-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「連結風險」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for linkage risk?","options":["外部資料連結會改變原資料的識別風險。","每一表單獨匿名便保證聯結後匿名。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「連結風險」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["External linkage changes identifiability risk.","Separately anonymous tables stay anonymous after joining.","One matching output proves linkage risk for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"外部資料連結會改變原資料的識別風險。 在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。 因此「每一表單獨匿名便保證聯結後匿名。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"External linkage changes identifiability risk. Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. The alternative \"Separately anonymous tables stay anonymous after joining.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-12","order":4,"sequence":12,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-11"],"title":"連結風險：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Linkage risk: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「連結風險」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for linkage risk.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。」；將結果與「外部資料連結會改變原資料的識別風險。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. Compare results against: External linkage changes identifiability risk. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每一表單獨匿名便保證聯結後匿名。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Separately anonymous tables stay anonymous after joining. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「連結風險」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「每一表單獨匿名便保證聯結後匿名。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for linkage risk; explain why this claim fails: Separately anonymous tables stay anonymous after joining.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-12-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"外部資料連結會改變原資料的識別風險。","textEn":"External linkage changes identifiability risk.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-12-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「連結風險」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for linkage risk?","options":["每一表單獨匿名便保證聯結後匿名。","在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。","先把「連結風險」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Separately anonymous tables stay anonymous after joining.","Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables.","Tune the displayed linkage risk result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"外部資料連結會改變原資料的識別風險。 在兩組自製資料比較連結前後群組大小。 因此「每一表單獨匿名便保證聯結後匿名。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"External linkage changes identifiability risk. Compare group sizes before and after joining synthetic tables. The alternative \"Separately anonymous tables stay anonymous after joining.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-13","order":5,"sequence":13,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-12"],"title":"聚合選擇：原理與架構","titleEn":"Aggregation choices: principles and architecture","objective":"以「聚合選擇」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for aggregation choices.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「聚合選擇」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：粗分群降低解析度但不自動給出正式隱私保證。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for aggregation choices. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Coarse grouping reduces detail without automatically giving formal privacy. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：群組有多人便等於差分隱私。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A multi-person group implies differential privacy. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「聚合選擇」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for aggregation choices; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-13-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"粗分群降低解析度但不自動給出正式隱私保證。","textEn":"Coarse grouping reduces detail without automatically giving formal privacy.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-13-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「聚合選擇」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for aggregation choices?","options":["群組有多人便等於差分隱私。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「聚合選擇」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","粗分群降低解析度但不自動給出正式隱私保證。"],"optionsEn":["A multi-person group implies differential privacy.","One matching output proves aggregation choices for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Coarse grouping reduces detail without automatically giving formal privacy."],"answer":2,"explanation":"粗分群降低解析度但不自動給出正式隱私保證。 比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。 因此「群組有多人便等於差分隱私。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Coarse grouping reduces detail without automatically giving formal privacy. Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. The alternative \"A multi-person group implies differential privacy.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-14","order":6,"sequence":14,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-13"],"title":"聚合選擇：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Aggregation choices: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「聚合選擇」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for aggregation choices.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。」；將結果與「粗分群降低解析度但不自動給出正式隱私保證。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. Compare results against: Coarse grouping reduces detail without automatically giving formal privacy. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：群組有多人便等於差分隱私。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: A multi-person group implies differential privacy. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「聚合選擇」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「群組有多人便等於差分隱私。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for aggregation choices; explain why this claim fails: A multi-person group implies differential privacy.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-14-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"粗分群降低解析度但不自動給出正式隱私保證。","textEn":"Coarse grouping reduces detail without automatically giving formal privacy.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-14-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「聚合選擇」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for aggregation choices?","options":["比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。","群組有多人便等於差分隱私。","先把「聚合選擇」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning.","A multi-person group implies differential privacy.","Tune the displayed aggregation choices result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"粗分群降低解析度但不自動給出正式隱私保證。 比較不同分箱的偏差與最小群組數。 因此「群組有多人便等於差分隱私。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Coarse grouping reduces detail without automatically giving formal privacy. Compare bias and smallest groups under different binning. The alternative \"A multi-person group implies differential privacy.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-15","order":7,"sequence":15,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-14"],"title":"存取控管：原理與架構","titleEn":"Access control: principles and architecture","objective":"以「存取控管」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for access control.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「存取控管」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：控管限制誰能讀，不限制合法輸出透露多少。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「分開畫存取風險與發布風險。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for access control. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Access control limits readers, not information in permitted outputs. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Draw separate access and release risks. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"分開畫存取風險與發布風險。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Draw separate access and release risks. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有登入使用者就不需輸出隱私評估。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Logged-in users remove release-privacy needs. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「存取控管」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「分開畫存取風險與發布風險。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for access control; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-15-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"控管限制誰能讀，不限制合法輸出透露多少。","textEn":"Access control limits readers, not information in permitted outputs.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-15-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"分開畫存取風險與發布風險。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Draw separate access and release risks. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「存取控管」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for access control?","options":["只有登入使用者就不需輸出隱私評估。","控管限制誰能讀，不限制合法輸出透露多少。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「存取控管」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Logged-in users remove release-privacy needs.","Access control limits readers, not information in permitted outputs.","One matching output proves access control for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"控管限制誰能讀，不限制合法輸出透露多少。 分開畫存取風險與發布風險。 因此「只有登入使用者就不需輸出隱私評估。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Access control limits readers, not information in permitted outputs. Draw separate access and release risks. The alternative \"Logged-in users remove release-privacy needs.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-16","order":8,"sequence":16,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-15"],"title":"存取控管：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Access control: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「存取控管」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for access control.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「分開畫存取風險與發布風險。」；將結果與「控管限制誰能讀，不限制合法輸出透露多少。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Draw separate access and release risks. Compare results against: Access control limits readers, not information in permitted outputs. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"分開畫存取風險與發布風險。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Draw separate access and release risks. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只有登入使用者就不需輸出隱私評估。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Logged-in users remove release-privacy needs. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「存取控管」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「只有登入使用者就不需輸出隱私評估。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for access control; explain why this claim fails: Logged-in users remove release-privacy needs.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-16-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"控管限制誰能讀，不限制合法輸出透露多少。","textEn":"Access control limits readers, not information in permitted outputs.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-16-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"分開畫存取風險與發布風險。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Draw separate access and release risks. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「存取控管」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for access control?","options":["只有登入使用者就不需輸出隱私評估。","先把「存取控管」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","分開畫存取風險與發布風險。"],"optionsEn":["Logged-in users remove release-privacy needs.","Tune the displayed access control result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Draw separate access and release risks."],"answer":2,"explanation":"控管限制誰能讀，不限制合法輸出透露多少。 分開畫存取風險與發布風險。 因此「只有登入使用者就不需輸出隱私評估。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Access control limits readers, not information in permitted outputs. Draw separate access and release risks. The alternative \"Logged-in users remove release-privacy needs.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a371-v11-stage03","order":3,"title":"分析與保護","titleEn":"Analytics and protection","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「分析與保護」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop analytics and protection through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a371-v11-17","order":1,"sequence":17,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-16"],"title":"統計敏感度：原理與架構","titleEn":"Statistical sensitivity: principles and architecture","objective":"以「統計敏感度」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for statistical sensitivity.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「統計敏感度」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：一人資料可使統計改變多少取決於界限與鄰接。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「重算有界平均的替換敏感度。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for statistical sensitivity. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Single-person influence depends on bounds and adjacency. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"重算有界平均的替換敏感度。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：敏感度只取決於資料量，不依數值界限。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Sensitivity depends only on sample count. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「統計敏感度」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「重算有界平均的替換敏感度。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for statistical sensitivity; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-17-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"一人資料可使統計改變多少取決於界限與鄰接。","textEn":"Single-person influence depends on bounds and adjacency.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-17-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"重算有界平均的替換敏感度。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「統計敏感度」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for statistical sensitivity?","options":["一人資料可使統計改變多少取決於界限與鄰接。","敏感度只取決於資料量，不依數值界限。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「統計敏感度」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Single-person influence depends on bounds and adjacency.","Sensitivity depends only on sample count.","One matching output proves statistical sensitivity for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"一人資料可使統計改變多少取決於界限與鄰接。 重算有界平均的替換敏感度。 因此「敏感度只取決於資料量，不依數值界限。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Single-person influence depends on bounds and adjacency. Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. The alternative \"Sensitivity depends only on sample count.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-18","order":2,"sequence":18,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-17"],"title":"統計敏感度：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Statistical sensitivity: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「統計敏感度」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for statistical sensitivity.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「重算有界平均的替換敏感度。」；將結果與「一人資料可使統計改變多少取決於界限與鄰接。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. Compare results against: Single-person influence depends on bounds and adjacency. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"重算有界平均的替換敏感度。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：敏感度只取決於資料量，不依數值界限。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Sensitivity depends only on sample count. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「統計敏感度」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「敏感度只取決於資料量，不依數值界限。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for statistical sensitivity; explain why this claim fails: Sensitivity depends only on sample count.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-18-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"一人資料可使統計改變多少取決於界限與鄰接。","textEn":"Single-person influence depends on bounds and adjacency.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-18-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"重算有界平均的替換敏感度。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「統計敏感度」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for statistical sensitivity?","options":["敏感度只取決於資料量，不依數值界限。","重算有界平均的替換敏感度。","先把「統計敏感度」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Sensitivity depends only on sample count.","Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity.","Tune the displayed statistical sensitivity result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"一人資料可使統計改變多少取決於界限與鄰接。 重算有界平均的替換敏感度。 因此「敏感度只取決於資料量，不依數值界限。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Single-person influence depends on bounds and adjacency. Recalculate bounded-mean replace-one sensitivity. The alternative \"Sensitivity depends only on sample count.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-19","order":3,"sequence":19,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-18"],"title":"噪聲與誤差：原理與架構","titleEn":"Noise and error: principles and architecture","objective":"以「噪聲與誤差」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for noise and error.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「噪聲與誤差」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：隨機保護會增加估計方差而非保證無偏於所有操作。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for noise and error. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Randomized protection adds variance and does not guarantee every operation unbiased. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：增加噪聲永遠不影響下游決策。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Adding noise never affects downstream decisions. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「噪聲與誤差」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for noise and error; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-19-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"隨機保護會增加估計方差而非保證無偏於所有操作。","textEn":"Randomized protection adds variance and does not guarantee every operation unbiased.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-19-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「噪聲與誤差」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for noise and error?","options":["增加噪聲永遠不影響下游決策。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「噪聲與誤差」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","隨機保護會增加估計方差而非保證無偏於所有操作。"],"optionsEn":["Adding noise never affects downstream decisions.","One matching output proves noise and error for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Randomized protection adds variance and does not guarantee every operation unbiased."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隨機保護會增加估計方差而非保證無偏於所有操作。 用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。 因此「增加噪聲永遠不影響下游決策。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Randomized protection adds variance and does not guarantee every operation unbiased. Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. The alternative \"Adding noise never affects downstream decisions.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-20","order":4,"sequence":20,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-19"],"title":"噪聲與誤差：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Noise and error: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「噪聲與誤差」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for noise and error.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。」；將結果與「隨機保護會增加估計方差而非保證無偏於所有操作。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. Compare results against: Randomized protection adds variance and does not guarantee every operation unbiased. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：增加噪聲永遠不影響下游決策。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Adding noise never affects downstream decisions. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「噪聲與誤差」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「增加噪聲永遠不影響下游決策。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for noise and error; explain why this claim fails: Adding noise never affects downstream decisions.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-20-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"隨機保護會增加估計方差而非保證無偏於所有操作。","textEn":"Randomized protection adds variance and does not guarantee every operation unbiased.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-20-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「噪聲與誤差」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for noise and error?","options":["用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。","增加噪聲永遠不影響下游決策。","先把「噪聲與誤差」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling.","Adding noise never affects downstream decisions.","Tune the displayed noise and error result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隨機保護會增加估計方差而非保證無偏於所有操作。 用合成抽樣比較發布前後誤差分佈。 因此「增加噪聲永遠不影響下游決策。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Randomized protection adds variance and does not guarantee every operation unbiased. Compare error distributions with synthetic sampling. The alternative \"Adding noise never affects downstream decisions.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-21","order":5,"sequence":21,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-20"],"title":"查詢組合：原理與架構","titleEn":"Query composition: principles and architecture","objective":"以「查詢組合」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for query composition.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「查詢組合」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：多次發布會累積資訊洩漏預算。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for query composition. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Repeated releases accumulate information-disclosure budgets. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每次單獨安全便表示無限次安全。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Individually safe queries are safe without limit. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「查詢組合」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for query composition; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-21-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"多次發布會累積資訊洩漏預算。","textEn":"Repeated releases accumulate information-disclosure budgets.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-21-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「查詢組合」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for query composition?","options":["每次單獨安全便表示無限次安全。","多次發布會累積資訊洩漏預算。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「查詢組合」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Individually safe queries are safe without limit.","Repeated releases accumulate information-disclosure budgets.","One matching output proves query composition for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"多次發布會累積資訊洩漏預算。 對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。 因此「每次單獨安全便表示無限次安全。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Repeated releases accumulate information-disclosure budgets. Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. The alternative \"Individually safe queries are safe without limit.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-22","order":6,"sequence":22,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-21"],"title":"查詢組合：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Query composition: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「查詢組合」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for query composition.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。」；將結果與「多次發布會累積資訊洩漏預算。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. Compare results against: Repeated releases accumulate information-disclosure budgets. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：每次單獨安全便表示無限次安全。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Individually safe queries are safe without limit. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「查詢組合」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「每次單獨安全便表示無限次安全。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for query composition; explain why this claim fails: Individually safe queries are safe without limit.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-22-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"多次發布會累積資訊洩漏預算。","textEn":"Repeated releases accumulate information-disclosure budgets.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-22-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「查詢組合」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for query composition?","options":["每次單獨安全便表示無限次安全。","先把「查詢組合」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。"],"optionsEn":["Individually safe queries are safe without limit.","Tune the displayed query composition result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table."],"answer":2,"explanation":"多次發布會累積資訊洩漏預算。 對假想查詢表追蹤累積 ε。 因此「每次單獨安全便表示無限次安全。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Repeated releases accumulate information-disclosure budgets. Track cumulative ε for a fictional query table. The alternative \"Individually safe queries are safe without limit.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-23","order":7,"sequence":23,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-22"],"title":"小群組效用：原理與架構","titleEn":"Small-group utility: principles and architecture","objective":"以「小群組效用」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for small-group utility.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「小群組效用」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：固定噪聲在小群組中有更大相對影響。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for small-group utility. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Fixed noise has larger relative effects on small groups. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：相同噪聲代表所有群組同等準確。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal noise implies equal group accuracy. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「小群組效用」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for small-group utility; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-23-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"固定噪聲在小群組中有更大相對影響。","textEn":"Fixed noise has larger relative effects on small groups.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-23-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「小群組效用」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for small-group utility?","options":["固定噪聲在小群組中有更大相對影響。","相同噪聲代表所有群組同等準確。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「小群組效用」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Fixed noise has larger relative effects on small groups.","Equal noise implies equal group accuracy.","One matching output proves small-group utility for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"固定噪聲在小群組中有更大相對影響。 比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。 因此「相同噪聲代表所有群組同等準確。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Fixed noise has larger relative effects on small groups. Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. The alternative \"Equal noise implies equal group accuracy.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-24","order":8,"sequence":24,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-23"],"title":"小群組效用：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Small-group utility: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「小群組效用」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for small-group utility.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。」；將結果與「固定噪聲在小群組中有更大相對影響。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. Compare results against: Fixed noise has larger relative effects on small groups. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：相同噪聲代表所有群組同等準確。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal noise implies equal group accuracy. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「小群組效用」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「相同噪聲代表所有群組同等準確。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for small-group utility; explain why this claim fails: Equal noise implies equal group accuracy.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-24-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"固定噪聲在小群組中有更大相對影響。","textEn":"Fixed noise has larger relative effects on small groups.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-24-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「小群組效用」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for small-group utility?","options":["相同噪聲代表所有群組同等準確。","比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。","先把「小群組效用」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Equal noise implies equal group accuracy.","Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise.","Tune the displayed small-group utility result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"固定噪聲在小群組中有更大相對影響。 比較同噪聲下 10 與 1000 人群組誤差。 因此「相同噪聲代表所有群組同等準確。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Fixed noise has larger relative effects on small groups. Compare 10- and 1,000-person relative errors with equal noise. The alternative \"Equal noise implies equal group accuracy.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a371-v11-stage04","order":4,"title":"驗證與治理","titleEn":"Verification and governance","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「驗證與治理」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop verification and governance through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a371-v11-25","order":1,"sequence":25,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-24"],"title":"偏差檢查：原理與架構","titleEn":"Bias checks: principles and architecture","objective":"以「偏差檢查」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for bias checks.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「偏差檢查」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：總體效用可能掩蓋少數群組的不良誤差。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for bias checks. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Overall utility can hide poor minority-group errors. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：總體準確度高就代表群組公平。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: High overall accuracy proves group fairness. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「偏差檢查」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for bias checks; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-25-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"總體效用可能掩蓋少數群組的不良誤差。","textEn":"Overall utility can hide poor minority-group errors.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-25-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「偏差檢查」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for bias checks?","options":["總體準確度高就代表群組公平。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「偏差檢查」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","總體效用可能掩蓋少數群組的不良誤差。"],"optionsEn":["High overall accuracy proves group fairness.","One matching output proves bias checks for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Overall utility can hide poor minority-group errors."],"answer":2,"explanation":"總體效用可能掩蓋少數群組的不良誤差。 以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。 因此「總體準確度高就代表群組公平。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Overall utility can hide poor minority-group errors. Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. The alternative \"High overall accuracy proves group fairness.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-26","order":2,"sequence":26,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-25"],"title":"偏差檢查：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Bias checks: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「偏差檢查」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for bias checks.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。」；將結果與「總體效用可能掩蓋少數群組的不良誤差。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. Compare results against: Overall utility can hide poor minority-group errors. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：總體準確度高就代表群組公平。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: High overall accuracy proves group fairness. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「偏差檢查」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「總體準確度高就代表群組公平。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for bias checks; explain why this claim fails: High overall accuracy proves group fairness.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-26-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"總體效用可能掩蓋少數群組的不良誤差。","textEn":"Overall utility can hide poor minority-group errors.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-26-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「偏差檢查」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for bias checks?","options":["以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。","總體準確度高就代表群組公平。","先把「偏差檢查」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately.","High overall accuracy proves group fairness.","Tune the displayed bias checks result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"總體效用可能掩蓋少數群組的不良誤差。 以合成群組另列誤差與缺測率。 因此「總體準確度高就代表群組公平。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Overall utility can hide poor minority-group errors. Report synthetic-group errors and missingness separately. The alternative \"High overall accuracy proves group fairness.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-27","order":3,"sequence":27,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-26"],"title":"發布審查：原理與架構","titleEn":"Release review: principles and architecture","objective":"以「發布審查」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for release review.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「發布審查」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：模型、報告與中間檔都可能帶有隱私資訊。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for release review. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Models, reports and intermediate files may expose private information. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只審查最終表格就足夠。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Reviewing only the final table is sufficient. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「發布審查」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for release review; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-27-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"模型、報告與中間檔都可能帶有隱私資訊。","textEn":"Models, reports and intermediate files may expose private information.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-27-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「發布審查」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for release review?","options":["只審查最終表格就足夠。","模型、報告與中間檔都可能帶有隱私資訊。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「發布審查」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Reviewing only the final table is sufficient.","Models, reports and intermediate files may expose private information.","One matching output proves release review for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"模型、報告與中間檔都可能帶有隱私資訊。 盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。 因此「只審查最終表格就足夠。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Models, reports and intermediate files may expose private information. Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. The alternative \"Reviewing only the final table is sufficient.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-28","order":4,"sequence":28,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-27"],"title":"發布審查：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Release review: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「發布審查」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for release review.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。」；將結果與「模型、報告與中間檔都可能帶有隱私資訊。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. Compare results against: Models, reports and intermediate files may expose private information. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：只審查最終表格就足夠。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Reviewing only the final table is sufficient. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「發布審查」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「只審查最終表格就足夠。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for release review; explain why this claim fails: Reviewing only the final table is sufficient.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-28-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"模型、報告與中間檔都可能帶有隱私資訊。","textEn":"Models, reports and intermediate files may expose private information.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-28-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「發布審查」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for release review?","options":["只審查最終表格就足夠。","先把「發布審查」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。"],"optionsEn":["Reviewing only the final table is sufficient.","Tune the displayed release review result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis."],"answer":2,"explanation":"模型、報告與中間檔都可能帶有隱私資訊。 盤點玩具分析留下的所有產物。 因此「只審查最終表格就足夠。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Models, reports and intermediate files may expose private information. Inventory all artifacts from a toy analysis. The alternative \"Reviewing only the final table is sufficient.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-29","order":5,"sequence":29,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-28"],"title":"再現與稽核：原理與架構","titleEn":"Reproduction and audit: principles and architecture","objective":"以「再現與稽核」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for reproduction and audit.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「再現與稽核」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：可重現分析需保留設定而不必散佈原始個資。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「用合成替代資料重現指標計算。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for reproduction and audit. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Reproducibility needs settings without distributing personal data. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"用合成替代資料重現指標計算。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：重現必須向所有人公開原始個資。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Reproduction requires sharing personal data with everyone. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「再現與稽核」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「用合成替代資料重現指標計算。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for reproduction and audit; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-29-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可重現分析需保留設定而不必散佈原始個資。","textEn":"Reproducibility needs settings without distributing personal data.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-29-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用合成替代資料重現指標計算。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「再現與稽核」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for reproduction and audit?","options":["可重現分析需保留設定而不必散佈原始個資。","重現必須向所有人公開原始個資。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「再現與稽核」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Reproducibility needs settings without distributing personal data.","Reproduction requires sharing personal data with everyone.","One matching output proves reproduction and audit for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可重現分析需保留設定而不必散佈原始個資。 用合成替代資料重現指標計算。 因此「重現必須向所有人公開原始個資。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reproducibility needs settings without distributing personal data. Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. The alternative \"Reproduction requires sharing personal data with everyone.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-30","order":6,"sequence":30,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-29"],"title":"再現與稽核：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Reproduction and audit: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「再現與稽核」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for reproduction and audit.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「用合成替代資料重現指標計算。」；將結果與「可重現分析需保留設定而不必散佈原始個資。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. Compare results against: Reproducibility needs settings without distributing personal data. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"用合成替代資料重現指標計算。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：重現必須向所有人公開原始個資。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Reproduction requires sharing personal data with everyone. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「再現與稽核」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「重現必須向所有人公開原始個資。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for reproduction and audit; explain why this claim fails: Reproduction requires sharing personal data with everyone.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-30-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可重現分析需保留設定而不必散佈原始個資。","textEn":"Reproducibility needs settings without distributing personal data.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-30-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用合成替代資料重現指標計算。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「再現與稽核」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for reproduction and audit?","options":["重現必須向所有人公開原始個資。","用合成替代資料重現指標計算。","先把「再現與稽核」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Reproduction requires sharing personal data with everyone.","Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes.","Tune the displayed reproduction and audit result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"可重現分析需保留設定而不必散佈原始個資。 用合成替代資料重現指標計算。 因此「重現必須向所有人公開原始個資。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Reproducibility needs settings without distributing personal data. Reproduce metric calculations using synthetic substitutes. The alternative \"Reproduction requires sharing personal data with everyone.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-31","order":7,"sequence":31,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-30"],"title":"效用決策：原理與架構","titleEn":"Utility decisions: principles and architecture","objective":"以「效用決策」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for utility decisions.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「效用決策」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：隱私、誤差與服務目的需共同定義可接受範圍。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for utility decisions. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Privacy, error and purpose jointly define acceptable performance. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: State limits and unresolved risk for the example. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"State limits and unresolved risk for the example. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：選最小 ε 就必然得到最佳產品。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: The smallest ε necessarily yields the best product. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「效用決策」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for utility decisions; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-31-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"隱私、誤差與服務目的需共同定義可接受範圍。","textEn":"Privacy, error and purpose jointly define acceptable performance.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-31-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"State limits and unresolved risk for the example. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a371-v11-31-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 100 人平均收入分析先將收入界定於 0–100,000 單位；固定樣本數替換鄰接下，平均敏感度 Δ=100000/100=1000 單位。Laplace ε=1 時尺度 b=1000、標準差 √2b=1414.21 單位。只此假設成立時適用。","textEn":"For 100 synthetic people with values bounded to 0–100,000 units and fixed-size replace-one adjacency, mean sensitivity is 1,000 units. Laplace ε=1 gives b=1,000 and standard deviation 1,414.21 units; the assumptions are essential.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「效用決策」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for utility decisions?","options":["選最小 ε 就必然得到最佳產品。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「效用決策」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","隱私、誤差與服務目的需共同定義可接受範圍。"],"optionsEn":["The smallest ε necessarily yields the best product.","One matching output proves utility decisions for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Privacy, error and purpose jointly define acceptable performance."],"answer":2,"explanation":"隱私、誤差與服務目的需共同定義可接受範圍。 用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。 因此「選最小 ε 就必然得到最佳產品。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Privacy, error and purpose jointly define acceptable performance. State limits and unresolved risk for the example. The alternative \"The smallest ε necessarily yields the best product.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a371-v11-32","order":8,"sequence":32,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"prerequisiteIds":["a371-v11-31"],"title":"效用決策：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Utility decisions: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「效用決策」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for utility decisions.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。」；將結果與「隱私、誤差與服務目的需共同定義可接受範圍。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: State limits and unresolved risk for the example. Compare results against: Privacy, error and purpose jointly define acceptable performance. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"State limits and unresolved risk for the example. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：選最小 ε 就必然得到最佳產品。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: The smallest ε necessarily yields the best product. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「效用決策」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「選最小 ε 就必然得到最佳產品。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for utility decisions; explain why this claim fails: The smallest ε necessarily yields the best product.","knowledge":[{"id":"a371-v11-32-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"隱私、誤差與服務目的需共同定義可接受範圍。","textEn":"Privacy, error and purpose jointly define acceptable performance.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a371-v11-32-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"State limits and unresolved risk for the example. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a371-v11-32-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想 100 人平均收入分析先將收入界定於 0–100,000 單位；固定樣本數替換鄰接下，平均敏感度 Δ=100000/100=1000 單位。Laplace ε=1 時尺度 b=1000、標準差 √2b=1414.21 單位。只此假設成立時適用。","textEn":"For 100 synthetic people with values bounded to 0–100,000 units and fixed-size replace-one adjacency, mean sensitivity is 1,000 units. Laplace ε=1 gives b=1,000 and standard deviation 1,414.21 units; the assumptions are essential.","sourceIds":["v11c-privacy","v11c-dp"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「效用決策」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for utility decisions?","options":["用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。","選最小 ε 就必然得到最佳產品。","先把「效用決策」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["State limits and unresolved risk for the example.","The smallest ε necessarily yields the best product.","Tune the displayed utility decisions result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"隱私、誤差與服務目的需共同定義可接受範圍。 用本課算例寫出限用條件與未決風險。 因此「選最小 ε 就必然得到最佳產品。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Privacy, error and purpose jointly define acceptable performance. State limits and unresolved risk for the example. The alternative \"The smallest ε necessarily yields the best product.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]}],"curriculumVersion":11,"scope":"公開原理的本地科教模擬與工程判讀。只使用自製、合成或明確授權的資料；不操作真實受害主機、他人帳號、工業控制或超算設施。數值不代表廠商規格或實測效能，完成課程不是專業資格、真實裝置操作經歷或生產部署認證。","scopeEn":"Local educational simulation and engineering interpretation of public principles. Use self-made, synthetic or explicitly licensed data only; do not operate real victim hosts, other accounts, industrial control or supercomputing facilities. Values are not product specifications or measured performance. Completion is not a qualification, real-equipment experience or production-deployment certification.","workedExample":{"title":"含假設的可重算工程例","titleEn":"Reproducible assumed engineering case","text":"假想 100 人平均收入分析先將收入界定於 0–100,000 單位；固定樣本數替換鄰接下，平均敏感度 Δ=100000/100=1000 單位。Laplace ε=1 時尺度 b=1000、標準差 √2b=1414.21 單位。只此假設成立時適用。","textEn":"For 100 synthetic people with values bounded to 0–100,000 units and fixed-size replace-one adjacency, mean sensitivity is 1,000 units. Laplace ε=1 gives b=1,000 and standard deviation 1,414.21 units; the assumptions are essential.","assumptions":"使用算例明列的單位、分佈、精度、拓撲與理想化條件；改變鄰接、位寬、取樣或系統邊界必須重算。","assumptionsEn":"Use the stated units, distributions, precision, topology and idealizations; recompute after changing adjacency, width, sampling or boundaries.","sourceScope":"作者獨立設定的假想數值例，非引用機構的實測資料；來源支援領域定義與架構。","sourceScopeEn":"Independently chosen hypothetical values, not institutional measurements; sources support definitions and architecture."},"diagram":{"type":"network","labels":["資料與目的","風險與模型","分析與保護","驗證與治理"],"labelsEn":["Data and purpose","Risk and models","Analytics and protection","Verification and governance"],"original":true,"notToScale":true},"educationEdition":11,"subcategory":"it-privacy","subcategoryTitle":"隱私保護與安全計算","subcategoryTitleEn":"Privacy-preserving and secure computation","learningTrack":"computing","learningSubdiscipline":"it-privacy","enrichmentVersion":11},{"id":"a372","title":"聯邦學習系統","titleEn":"Federated-learning systems","category":"computing","kind":"course","summary":"以分散神經網路訓練、聚合與非同分佈資料串連 16 個原創技術單元、32 步；涵蓋原理解析、架構圖、假想量化、合成資料實驗、競爭失效原因及可重算驗收。","summaryEn":"Sixteen original technical units and 32 tasks connect distributed neural training, aggregation and non-iid data with principles, architectures, assumed calculations, synthetic experiments, competing failure causes and reproducible acceptance.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"status":"guided","contentStatus":"reviewable-educational-curriculum","depth":4,"stepCount":32,"estimatedMinutes":1120,"simulationOnly":true,"languageCoverage":["zh-TW","en"],"stages":[{"id":"a372-v11-stage01","order":1,"title":"參與者與資料","titleEn":"Participants and data","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「參與者與資料」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop participants and data through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a372-v11-01","order":1,"sequence":1,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":[],"title":"聯邦邊界：原理與架構","titleEn":"Federation boundaries: principles and architecture","objective":"以「聯邦邊界」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for federation boundaries.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「聯邦邊界」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：資料留本地不表示梯度或模型不洩漏資訊。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for federation boundaries. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Local data retention does not prevent update or model leakage. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：不傳原始資料就自動有差分隱私。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Not sending raw data automatically gives differential privacy. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「聯邦邊界」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for federation boundaries; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-01-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"資料留本地不表示梯度或模型不洩漏資訊。","textEn":"Local data retention does not prevent update or model leakage.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-01-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a372-v11-01-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想三個客戶分別有 20、30、50 筆資料與標量更新 1、3、5；FedAvg 權重為 0.2、0.3、0.5，聚合更新為 3.6。等權平均為 3；權重差異反映樣本數而非品質保證，也未提供隱私保證。","textEn":"Three synthetic clients have 20, 30 and 50 samples and scalar updates 1, 3 and 5. Sample-weighted FedAvg yields 3.6; equal weighting yields 3. Weights reflect sample counts, not guaranteed quality or privacy.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「聯邦邊界」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for federation boundaries?","options":["資料留本地不表示梯度或模型不洩漏資訊。","不傳原始資料就自動有差分隱私。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「聯邦邊界」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Local data retention does not prevent update or model leakage.","Not sending raw data automatically gives differential privacy.","One matching output proves federation boundaries for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"資料留本地不表示梯度或模型不洩漏資訊。 畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。 因此「不傳原始資料就自動有差分隱私。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Local data retention does not prevent update or model leakage. Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. The alternative \"Not sending raw data automatically gives differential privacy.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-02","order":2,"sequence":2,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-01"],"title":"聯邦邊界：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Federation boundaries: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「聯邦邊界」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for federation boundaries.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。」；將結果與「資料留本地不表示梯度或模型不洩漏資訊。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. Compare results against: Local data retention does not prevent update or model leakage. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：不傳原始資料就自動有差分隱私。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Not sending raw data automatically gives differential privacy. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「聯邦邊界」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「不傳原始資料就自動有差分隱私。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for federation boundaries; explain why this claim fails: Not sending raw data automatically gives differential privacy.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-02-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"資料留本地不表示梯度或模型不洩漏資訊。","textEn":"Local data retention does not prevent update or model leakage.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-02-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"},{"id":"a372-v11-02-k3","title":"本課量化算例","titleEn":"Course quantitative example","text":"假想三個客戶分別有 20、30、50 筆資料與標量更新 1、3、5；FedAvg 權重為 0.2、0.3、0.5，聚合更新為 3.6。等權平均為 3；權重差異反映樣本數而非品質保證，也未提供隱私保證。","textEn":"Three synthetic clients have 20, 30 and 50 samples and scalar updates 1, 3 and 5. Sample-weighted FedAvg yields 3.6; equal weighting yields 3. Weights reflect sample counts, not guaranteed quality or privacy.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-hypothetical-exercise"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「聯邦邊界」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for federation boundaries?","options":["不傳原始資料就自動有差分隱私。","畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。","先把「聯邦邊界」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Not sending raw data automatically gives differential privacy.","Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows.","Tune the displayed federation boundaries result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"資料留本地不表示梯度或模型不洩漏資訊。 畫原始資料、更新與全域模型的流向。 因此「不傳原始資料就自動有差分隱私。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Local data retention does not prevent update or model leakage. Trace raw data, updates and global-model flows. The alternative \"Not sending raw data automatically gives differential privacy.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-03","order":3,"sequence":3,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-02"],"title":"模型同構：原理與架構","titleEn":"Model compatibility: principles and architecture","objective":"以「模型同構」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for model compatibility.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「模型同構」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：可聚合權重需有相同參數語意與次序。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for model compatibility. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Aggregated weights need aligned parameter meanings and ordering. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：參數數量相同便代表模型相容。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal parameter counts imply compatibility. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「模型同構」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for model compatibility; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-03-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可聚合權重需有相同參數語意與次序。","textEn":"Aggregated weights need aligned parameter meanings and ordering.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-03-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「模型同構」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for model compatibility?","options":["參數數量相同便代表模型相容。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「模型同構」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","可聚合權重需有相同參數語意與次序。"],"optionsEn":["Equal parameter counts imply compatibility.","One matching output proves model compatibility for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Aggregated weights need aligned parameter meanings and ordering."],"answer":2,"explanation":"可聚合權重需有相同參數語意與次序。 比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。 因此「參數數量相同便代表模型相容。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Aggregated weights need aligned parameter meanings and ordering. Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. The alternative \"Equal parameter counts imply compatibility.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-04","order":4,"sequence":4,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-03"],"title":"模型同構：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Model compatibility: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「模型同構」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for model compatibility.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。」；將結果與「可聚合權重需有相同參數語意與次序。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. Compare results against: Aggregated weights need aligned parameter meanings and ordering. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：參數數量相同便代表模型相容。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal parameter counts imply compatibility. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「模型同構」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「參數數量相同便代表模型相容。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for model compatibility; explain why this claim fails: Equal parameter counts imply compatibility.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-04-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"可聚合權重需有相同參數語意與次序。","textEn":"Aggregated weights need aligned parameter meanings and ordering.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-04-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「模型同構」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for model compatibility?","options":["比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。","參數數量相同便代表模型相容。","先把「模型同構」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs.","Equal parameter counts imply compatibility.","Tune the displayed model compatibility result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"可聚合權重需有相同參數語意與次序。 比對兩個玩具 MLP 的層形狀與名稱。 因此「參數數量相同便代表模型相容。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Aggregated weights need aligned parameter meanings and ordering. Compare layer shapes and names in two toy MLPs. The alternative \"Equal parameter counts imply compatibility.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-05","order":5,"sequence":5,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-04"],"title":"MLP 前向：原理與架構","titleEn":"MLP forward pass: principles and architecture","objective":"以「MLP 前向」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for mlp forward pass.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「MLP 前向」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：h=φ(Wx+b) 的非線性決定多層表達能力。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for mlp forward pass. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Nonlinearity in h=φ(Wx+b) enables multilayer expressiveness. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：堆疊線性層必然增加非線性表達。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Stacking linear layers necessarily adds nonlinearity. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「MLP 前向」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for mlp forward pass; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-05-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"h=φ(Wx+b) 的非線性決定多層表達能力。","textEn":"Nonlinearity in h=φ(Wx+b) enables multilayer expressiveness.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-05-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「MLP 前向」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for mlp forward pass?","options":["堆疊線性層必然增加非線性表達。","h=φ(Wx+b) 的非線性決定多層表達能力。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「MLP 前向」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["Stacking linear layers necessarily adds nonlinearity.","Nonlinearity in h=φ(Wx+b) enables multilayer expressiveness.","One matching output proves mlp forward pass for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":1,"explanation":"h=φ(Wx+b) 的非線性決定多層表達能力。 手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。 因此「堆疊線性層必然增加非線性表達。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Nonlinearity in h=φ(Wx+b) enables multilayer expressiveness. Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. The alternative \"Stacking linear layers necessarily adds nonlinearity.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-06","order":6,"sequence":6,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-05"],"title":"MLP 前向：實驗與證據","titleEn":"MLP forward pass: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「MLP 前向」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for mlp forward pass.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。」；將結果與「h=φ(Wx+b) 的非線性決定多層表達能力。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. Compare results against: Nonlinearity in h=φ(Wx+b) enables multilayer expressiveness. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：堆疊線性層必然增加非線性表達。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Stacking linear layers necessarily adds nonlinearity. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「MLP 前向」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「堆疊線性層必然增加非線性表達。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for mlp forward pass; explain why this claim fails: Stacking linear layers necessarily adds nonlinearity.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-06-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"h=φ(Wx+b) 的非線性決定多層表達能力。","textEn":"Nonlinearity in h=φ(Wx+b) enables multilayer expressiveness.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-06-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「MLP 前向」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for mlp forward pass?","options":["堆疊線性層必然增加非線性表達。","先把「MLP 前向」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。","手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。"],"optionsEn":["Stacking linear layers necessarily adds nonlinearity.","Tune the displayed mlp forward pass result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation.","Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions."],"answer":2,"explanation":"h=φ(Wx+b) 的非線性決定多層表達能力。 手算兩層小網路的前向值與飽和區。 因此「堆疊線性層必然增加非線性表達。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Nonlinearity in h=φ(Wx+b) enables multilayer expressiveness. Calculate a tiny two-layer network and saturation regions. The alternative \"Stacking linear layers necessarily adds nonlinearity.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-07","order":7,"sequence":7,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-06"],"title":"本地反傳：原理與架構","titleEn":"Local backpropagation: principles and architecture","objective":"以「本地反傳」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for local backpropagation.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「本地反傳」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：鏈式法則將本地損失梯度傳回每層參數。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for local backpropagation. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: The chain rule propagates local loss gradients to parameters. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：梯度只由最後一層決定。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Only the last layer determines gradients. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「本地反傳」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for local backpropagation; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-07-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"鏈式法則將本地損失梯度傳回每層參數。","textEn":"The chain rule propagates local loss gradients to parameters.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-07-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「本地反傳」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for local backpropagation?","options":["鏈式法則將本地損失梯度傳回每層參數。","梯度只由最後一層決定。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「本地反傳」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。"],"optionsEn":["The chain rule propagates local loss gradients to parameters.","Only the last layer determines gradients.","One matching output proves local backpropagation for all sizes, versions and failure conditions."],"answer":0,"explanation":"鏈式法則將本地損失梯度傳回每層參數。 以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。 因此「梯度只由最後一層決定。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"The chain rule propagates local loss gradients to parameters. Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. The alternative \"Only the last layer determines gradients.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-08","order":8,"sequence":8,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-07"],"title":"本地反傳：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Local backpropagation: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「本地反傳」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for local backpropagation.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。」；將結果與「鏈式法則將本地損失梯度傳回每層參數。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. Compare results against: The chain rule propagates local loss gradients to parameters. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：梯度只由最後一層決定。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Only the last layer determines gradients. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「本地反傳」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「梯度只由最後一層決定。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for local backpropagation; explain why this claim fails: Only the last layer determines gradients.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-08-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"鏈式法則將本地損失梯度傳回每層參數。","textEn":"The chain rule propagates local loss gradients to parameters.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-08-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「本地反傳」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for local backpropagation?","options":["梯度只由最後一層決定。","以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。","先把「本地反傳」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Only the last layer determines gradients.","Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences.","Tune the displayed local backpropagation result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":1,"explanation":"鏈式法則將本地損失梯度傳回每層參數。 以有限差分核對小網路的一個權重梯度。 因此「梯度只由最後一層決定。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"The chain rule propagates local loss gradients to parameters. Check one tiny-network gradient with finite differences. The alternative \"Only the last layer determines gradients.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}}]},{"id":"a372-v11-stage02","order":2,"title":"梯度與聚合","titleEn":"Gradients and aggregation","description":"四個技術單元依序完成「梯度與聚合」的架構與證據，共八步可分別儲存的本地科教實作。","descriptionEn":"Four technical units develop gradients and aggregation through eight separately saved local educational tasks.","steps":[{"id":"a372-v11-09","order":1,"sequence":9,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-08"],"title":"樣本權重：原理與架構","titleEn":"Sample weights: principles and architecture","objective":"以「樣本權重」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for sample weights.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「樣本權重」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：FedAvg 樣本權重與客戶等權有不同目標。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for sample weights. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: Sample weighting and equal-client weighting target different objectives. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：等權與樣本加權永遠相等。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal and sample-weighted aggregation always agree. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「樣本權重」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for sample weights; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-09-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"FedAvg 樣本權重與客戶等權有不同目標。","textEn":"Sample weighting and equal-client weighting target different objectives.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-09-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「樣本權重」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for sample weights?","options":["等權與樣本加權永遠相等。","只要一次輸出符合預期，就能推定「樣本權重」對所有資料量、版本與故障條件都成立。","FedAvg 樣本權重與客戶等權有不同目標。"],"optionsEn":["Equal and sample-weighted aggregation always agree.","One matching output proves sample weights for all sizes, versions and failure conditions.","Sample weighting and equal-client weighting target different objectives."],"answer":2,"explanation":"FedAvg 樣本權重與客戶等權有不同目標。 重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。 因此「等權與樣本加權永遠相等。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Sample weighting and equal-client weighting target different objectives. Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. The alternative \"Equal and sample-weighted aggregation always agree.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-10","order":2,"sequence":10,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-09"],"title":"樣本權重：實驗與證據","titleEn":"Sample weights: experiments and evidence","objective":"以「樣本權重」建立可重算實驗、錯誤辨識與驗收證據。","objectiveEn":"Build reproducible experiments, diagnosis and acceptance evidence for sample weights.","instruction":"重播本單元示意後，僅在自製資料、副本或本地合成環境驗證，不連線真實目標、不取得旁人資料。實作：「重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。」；將結果與「FedAvg 樣本權重與客戶等權有不同目標。」逐項對照。保留基準和變更後輸出，先列至少兩個可能造成差異的原因，再用版本、單位、誤差或信任邊界排除其中一項。未有實測的數值須明寫為假想值。最後寫出透過／保留的理由和仍待驗證條件。","instructionEn":"Replay the unit, then validate only self-made data, copies or a local synthetic environment; do not connect to real targets or collect other people's data. Exercise: Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. Compare results against: Sample weighting and equal-client weighting target different objectives. Preserve baseline and changed outputs. List at least two competing causes and discriminate one using versions, units, errors or trust boundaries. Label unmeasured values hypothetical. Document pass/hold reasons and remaining conditions.","observation":"重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：等權與樣本加權永遠相等。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: Equal and sample-weighted aggregation always agree. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「樣本權重」實驗輸出、基準差異、誤判排除與限用條件；解釋「等權與樣本加權永遠相等。」為何不成立。","checkEn":"Submit outputs, baseline differences, rejected misconceptions and limits for sample weights; explain why this claim fails: Equal and sample-weighted aggregation always agree.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-10-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"FedAvg 樣本權重與客戶等權有不同目標。","textEn":"Sample weighting and equal-client weighting target different objectives.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-10-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「樣本權重」的驗證方法時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which validation approach is justified for sample weights?","options":["重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。","等權與樣本加權永遠相等。","先把「樣本權重」的顯示結果調到符合預期，再把這次吻合當作獨立驗證。"],"optionsEn":["Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients.","Equal and sample-weighted aggregation always agree.","Tune the displayed sample weights result to the expected value and count that agreement as independent validation."],"answer":0,"explanation":"FedAvg 樣本權重與客戶等權有不同目標。 重算本課三客戶兩種聚合。 因此「等權與樣本加權永遠相等。」混淆了本單元必須分開檢查的條件。","explanationEn":"Sample weighting and equal-client weighting target different objectives. Recalculate both aggregation choices for three clients. The alternative \"Equal and sample-weighted aggregation always agree.\" conflates conditions that must be checked separately."}},{"id":"a372-v11-11","order":3,"sequence":11,"estimatedMinutes":35,"simulationOnly":true,"sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"prerequisiteIds":["a372-v11-10"],"title":"本地輪數：原理與架構","titleEn":"Local epochs: principles and architecture","objective":"以「本地輪數」建立原理、介面與可反駁模型。","objectiveEn":"Build principles, interfaces and a falsifiable model for local epochs.","instruction":"先觀察師傅的「本地輪數」示意，依序辨認輸入、狀態、輸出與信任或數值邊界，再在學徒工作臺排出資料／元件路徑。原理：更多本地更新減少通訊但可能放大客戶漂移。 使用自行生成的小資料、紙上圖或本地玩具程式建立基準與一項受控變更；先寫下可觀察預測，再設計「在合成異分佈資料比較 1 與 5 輪。」的驗證。記錄單位、版本、假設與未知量，不把示意模型當真實裝置或服務。","instructionEn":"Watch the mentor demonstration for local epochs. Identify inputs, state, outputs and trust/numerical boundaries, then arrange the data/component flow in the apprentice workspace. Principle: More local updates reduce communication but can amplify client drift. Use self-generated small data, paper diagrams or a local toy program to create a baseline and one controlled change. State an observable prediction before planning this check: Compare one and five epochs on synthetic non-IID data. Record units, versions, assumptions and unknowns; the model is not real equipment or service.","observation":"在合成異分佈資料比較 1 與 5 輪。 核對上述原理的適用範圍並記錄不符合預期之處。","observationEn":"Compare one and five epochs on synthetic non-IID data. Check the scope of the stated principle and record departures from expectations.","failure":"常見誤判：本地輪數越多全域模型必然越好。 應檢查資料版本、單位、信任邊界與可區分原因的證據。","failureEn":"Common misconception: More local epochs always improve the global model. Check versions, units, trust boundaries and discriminating evidence.","check":"提交「本地輪數」兩情境架構圖、假設與可反駁預測，並說明「在合成異分佈資料比較 1 與 5 輪。」如何辨別它們。","checkEn":"Submit a two-case architecture, assumptions and falsifiable prediction for local epochs; explain how the proposed evidence discriminates the cases.","knowledge":[{"id":"a372-v11-11-k1","title":"原理與架構依據","titleEn":"Principle and architecture","text":"更多本地更新減少通訊但可能放大客戶漂移。","textEn":"More local updates reduce communication but can amplify client drift.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-educational-analysis"},{"id":"a372-v11-11-k2","title":"辨別模型的證據","titleEn":"Discriminating model evidence","text":"在合成異分佈資料比較 1 與 5 輪。 保留基準、輸入版本、單位與誤差範圍；這項證據只支援已列出的模型邊界，不能自動推廣為整套真實系統保證。","textEn":"Compare one and five epochs on synthetic non-IID data. Preserve baselines, input versions, units and errors; this evidence supports stated model boundaries, not an automatic guarantee for an entire real system.","sourceIds":["v11c-flower","v11c-secagg"],"authorship":"original-validation-plan"}],"quiz":{"question":"審查「本地輪數」的原理與架構時，哪個說法成立？","questionEn":"Which principle/architecture claim is justified for local epochs?","options":["本地輪數越多全域模型必�